Dr. Kin Phea: Cambodia-China Relations: A Model of Steel Friendship
(Phnom Penh): 2023 is designated as the year of Cambodia-China friendship to celebrate the 65th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and China. Over the past 65 years, the two countries have nurtured and nurtured an inseparable "steel" friendship that has gone through many storms and overcame many difficulties.
In a daily press conference ahead of Prime Minister Hun Sen's first visit to China since 2020, a Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman stressed that "Cambodia and China are traditional neighbors and friends. "Steel, while the friendship between the two countries was established by the previous generation leaders of the two countries, has gone through the trials of time and has grown stronger day by day."
Chinese Foreign Ministry Spokeswoman Jiang Yu's Remarks on Samdech Techo Hun Sen's Visit The future together and continue the Sino-Cambodian friendly relations from generation to generation.
Cambodia has always adhered to the one-China policy and opposed any action or comment that undermines China's sovereignty and territorial integrity in all forms of separatist activities aimed at declaring "Taiwan independence" and any form of outside interference. Internal affairs of a sovereign state. Cambodia supports China's efforts to safeguard its core interests and achieve China's national reunification.
The special and inseparable relationship between Cambodia and China is a "special model" of interstate relations that can be applied both regionally and globally. In this year of Cambodia-China friendship, the strong commitment and great efforts of the leaders and people of the two countries clearly show that both Cambodia and China have truly recognized that community building Cambodia-China with a common future is real.
