The commitment was made on the occasion that the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen led a high-level delegation, including his two sons, to pay a courtesy call on Chinese President Xi Jinping on the occasion. Official visit on February 10, 2023.
During the meeting, the two leaders, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and President Xi Jinping, praised the two countries' bilateral relations, which have gone from comprehensive cooperation to iron friendship and community cooperation. Together, the same destiny.
The two leaders will continue to strengthen the spirit of building a single community, a single destiny, focusing on six areas, including: 1. Politics and diplomacy 2. Capacity manufacturing and textiles 3. Agriculture 4. Energy 5. Security 6. Relations between People and people, including the promotion of the health sector in Cambodia.
It should be noted that Cambodia and China have established diplomatic relations between the two countries for 65 years as of 2023. The two countries have continuously upgraded their relations and become strategic partners in all fields, and are building a common destiny.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen highlighted this during a bilateral working meeting with Chinese President Xi Jinping on Friday morning, February 10, 2023 in Beijing, China.
In addition to discussing bilateral and international relations, as well as strengthening economic and trade cooperation, Xi Jinping expressed support for Cambodia's foreign policy stance of independence and territorial integrity.
Regarding the remarks made by the Chinese President, Samdech Techo replied that Chinese aid not only contributed to Cambodia's progress, but also contributed to strengthening Cambodia's independence and raising Cambodia's profile on the international stage.
He further emphasized that the Cambodian economy was able to recover after the Kovid 19 crisis due to Chinese gestures and support in providing vaccines. Without the vaccines provided by the Chinese side, the fate of the Cambodian people would not be known. In particular, Cambodia reopened its economy and country on November 1, 2021.
According to the report, China has provided a lot of assistance to support the development of Cambodia. Since 2001, China has provided more than $ 2 billion in aid. In addition to aid, China has provided about $ 5 billion in loans.
Through these grants and loans, Cambodia has been used to develop many sectors. In particular, the construction of road and bridge infrastructure plays an important role in transportation.
