Spokesperson: Cambodia is moving towards implementing 4R policy to reduce the use of plastic products (Video inside) (Siem Reap): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, said that Cambodia is currently moving towards implementing the principle. 4R to help reduce the use of plastic products, while many countries are still implementing the 3R principle, which is a common principle.
Neth Pheaktra made the remarks while giving an interview to the media during the 11th Asia-Pacific Summit on "3R and Chakra Economy". At Sokha Hotel, Siem Reap on February 9, 2023 yesterday.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that in Cambodia, more than 10,000 tons of waste is generated every day, of which 60 to 65 percent is organic waste, 20 percent is plastic waste and about 10 percent is solid waste. Only 60 percent of the waste generated is dumped in landfills, while only 10 to 15 percent is recycled.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia has also banned the import of plastic waste into Cambodia, while a few years ago, many containers of plastic waste were imported, but the waste was sent back to the country of origin. Back, too.
Meanwhile, Mr. Pheaktra pointed out that today, some water and beverage companies have started to buy waste, such as bottles and plastic cans, which they have produced about 2,000 tons for recycling.
