Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Presides Over a Meeting on Establishment of Kampong Cham Transport Services Association Committee
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, on the morning of February 10, 2023, chaired a meeting to establish a committee of the Transport Services Association in Kampong Cham province with the participation of leaders and relevant departments and units in the province. Well.
According to Kampong Cham provincial administration officials, the establishment of the Kampong Cham Transport Services Association committee is aimed at organizing transport services associations in the member provinces, including motodup drivers, pass app drivers and drivers. Taxis for them to participate in social work in good cooperation with local authorities and police forces to maintain security, safety and public order better.
The official confirmed that the Executive Committee of the Kampong Cham Transport Services Association, which was established, has the following duties and responsibilities:
* Advise, guide and operate the Secretariat and the Association to take preventive measures against members of the transport service provider in the event of a legal violation.
* Supervise the daily activities of the association members in the livelihood business.
* Collect money from local and foreign philanthropists, members of the association committee, working groups or dignitaries to support the association.
Examine and provide urgent legal intervention assistance at the request and request of the President or Vice President (in the case of Chairman Sak), the Secretariat and the President of the Association of Transport Providers when they need legal assistance from the Association Committee.
* Provide guidance and work procedures to the Secretariat to monitor and summarize monthly, quarterly, semi-annual work from members of the Association of Transport Providers in the province.
The same official added that those who have become members of the Kampong Cham Transport Services Association will receive many benefits from this association as well. Groundbreaking ceremony for a 4-kilometer-long red gravel road and a 20-meter-long spillway in Bos Ta Som village, Rong Roeung commune, Stong district
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Say Kim Lam, Governor of Stong District, inaugurated the construction site of a 4,448-meter-long red gravel road and a 20-meter-long, 05-meter-wide spillway in Bos Ta Som village, Rong Roeung commune, Stong district, Kampong Thom province this morning. February 10, 2023
On that occasion, Mr. Say Kim Lam said that the new achievements and infrastructure that are happening today also depend on our nation being fully peaceful under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Mr. Stoung District Governor urged the administration of Rong Roeung commune to make a comprehensive notification to the people to open the road, and Veng Bunthoeun Company must pay more attention to cooperate to build this road and spillway construction as soon as possible according to technical standards. And ensure quality on time, long-term use.
It should be noted that the red gravel road and spillway, which is currently under construction, has a total length of 4448 meters, a width of 5 meters and a thickness of 0.15 meters. 590,500 riels.
The Closing Ceremony of the 11th Asia-Pacific Forum was presided over by Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, on behalf of Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment.
The closing ceremony was also attended by representatives of ministries, institutions, provincial and district administrations across the country, local organizations and private companies, and international participants representing member countries, international organizations and educational institutions.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth praised all the above discussions with fruit, experience and understanding. He also thanked the active participation and contribution of the delegation, policy makers, private sector representatives, researchers and experts from various fields.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth also expressed his excitement at this year's forum as more and more mayors and municipalities in the region signed the Asian Mayor's Declaration on Indore 3R on Achieving Clean Water. And fresh air in the city. He expressed his sincere congratulations and gratitude to the signatory countries for their strong commitment to the environment.
However, Eang Sophalleth also drew participants' attention to the environmental challenges posed by the devastating epidemic of Kovid 19 and the global situation remains uncertain.
The Secretary of State stressed that 2023 will be an important year in achieving the Sustainable Development Goals adopted nearly eight years ago. To achieve this goal, we must do our best to restore the time lost due to the Kovid-19 crisis and to return to our path of sustainable development.
"The broader and more effective implementation of the 3R principles and the chakra economy is extremely useful, especially in terms of waste reduction, improving material traffic, resource efficiency and regional economy, as well as natural restoration." This is the confirmation of Mr. Eang Sophalleth.
"We strongly believe that by promoting the 3R principles and the active chakra economy in our economic and social spheres, we have made significant contributions to addressing regional and global environmental issues as well as achieving SDGs ”.
Mr. Sophalleth also encouraged the dissemination of the forum results to the general public, including political leaders, youth policy makers, civil society and the private sector.
For Sophalleth to do so, the 3R principles and the economy will be more effective and can become practical to maximize results and serve as a basis for the devil to address a wide range of environmental issues.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth expressed his belief that through the unification of all parties, we will move towards achieving the goal of a waste-free society and sustainable development in our Asia-Pacific region and beyond.
It should be noted that the 11th Asia-Pacific Forum on 3R Chakra Economy was held under the theme "Economic integration into development in all areas towards achieving a waste-free society and sustainable development goals." The first forum held in Cambodia took place from 8 to 10 February 2023 in Angkor, Siem Reap.
The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment, and was attended by ministries, institutions, provincial and district administrations across the country, local organizations and private companies, and about 500 international participants from 39 countries. Also from Japan, Maldives and Tuvalu.
The 11th Asia-Pacific Forum aims to discuss the implementation of 3R and the chakra economy in key areas and link the achievement of sustainable development goals and address climate change and biodiversity issues.
