In January 2022, the US Customs and Border Protection (CBP) banned the import of YTY rubber gloves, citing reasonable evidence of the use of "forced labor" in the company's production operations. This includes violations of living and working conditions.
Reuters reported on Thursday that the CBP reported that YTY had taken steps to address the issue of forced labor and that the company had reimbursed the recruitment fees paid by migrant workers. Conducted an independent social audit.
Malaysian companies, including some of the world's largest suppliers of palm oil and medical gloves, have come under increasing scrutiny over suspected abuses of foreign workers, a key part of Malaysia's manufacturing workforce. .
YTY said it was in the process of notifying its US customers and looked forward to re-establishing supply relations following the lifting of the import ban. According to Reuters.
At a meeting at the Diao Yutai State Guesthouse in Beijing, Xi Jinping welcomed the Prime Minister, the first world leader to pay a visit to China after the New Year. China.
During the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen recalled his visit to China on February 5, 2020, at a time when China was experiencing a severe epidemic of Kovid 19 virus.
Samdech Techo emphasized that when Samdech went to China, he wanted to encourage some students in Wuhan, and on the other hand, he wanted to stand with the Chinese people in difficult times.
During the meeting, the two leaders exchanged views on bilateral, multilateral and international issues of common concern. Mr. Xi Jinping praised the work of Samdech and the Royal Government of Cambodia in leading the ASEAN Summit with great success.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked his Chinese friends for their participation in ensuring success. During the meeting, the two leaders praised the bilateral relations between the two countries, which have gone from comprehensive cooperation to steel friendship and community cooperation to a common destiny.
Xi Jinping supported Cambodia's policy stance on Cambodia's independence and territorial integrity. Regarding the remarks of the Chinese President, Samdech Techo replied that the Chinese support is not only contributing to the progress of Cambodia, but also contributing to the strengthening of Cambodia's independence on the international stage.
Both sides praised the entry into force of the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement, which entered into force on January 1, 2022, which promoted the opening up of Chinese markets for Cambodian agricultural and fishery products.
The President expressed interest in the development of agriculture and hydrological culture in the area around the Tonle Sap Lake. Regarding the President's remarks, Samdech welcomed the President's important initiative to establish the Fish and Angkor Corridor in northwestern Cambodia.
Samdech Techo added that Cambodia already has three economic poles: Phnom Penh, Sihanoukville and Northeast, and Cambodia will establish a fourth economic pole in the Northwest Zone. At the meeting, Xi Jinping and Samdech Techo agreed to boost cooperation on promoting the production of electricity sources, focusing on protecting the green energy environment.
Samdech Techo asked the President to encourage more Chinese tourists to visit Cambodia after the easing of Chinese restrictions, especially the President's encouragement for Chinese tourists to travel to Cambodia without fear.
Samdech Techo stressed that the recovery of the Cambodian economy is due to the gestures and support of China in providing vaccines, that is, without the vaccines provided by the Chinese side, the Cambodian people do not know the fate. Which. In particular, Cambodia reopened its economy and country on November 1, 2023.
During the meeting, which lasted about 100 minutes, the leaders of the two countries agreed to boost diamond cooperation to push the two countries' relations to a new high.
South Korea to resume short-stay visas for Chinese travelers this weekend (Video inside) (Seoul): Seoul has announced that it plans to resume short-stay visas A short time for travelers from China on Saturday this week after the situation of Kovid 19 in China improved. This was released by the AFP news agency on Friday, February 10, 2023.
South Korea suspended the issuance of short-stay visas to Chinese travelers in January after China scrapped its strict zero-Kivid policy, leading to an increase in domestic cases. Up sharply. Beijing, meanwhile, has retaliated against Seoul by suspending short-stay visas for South Korean travelers.
However, on Friday, South Korean Deputy Interior Minister Kim Sung Ho said the government had decided to resume visa issuance after seeing 19 cases of Kovid crossing. The number of Chinese passengers arriving in South Korea has dropped significantly and no new strains of the virus have been detected.
The presence of Samdech Techo Hun Sen was warmly welcomed by the President of China. During the meeting, Samdech Techo's sons, Mr. Hun Manet and Mr. Hun Many, were also welcomed by the Chinese President.
According to Minister of Information Khieu Kanharith, who accompanied Samdech Techo, during the meeting, the Chinese President welcomed Prime Minister Hun Sen, an "old friend" and the first foreign guest after the Chinese New Year. To and highly valued the "diamond" cooperation between Cambodia and China.
The Minister said that during the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also raised the intention to establish a fourth economic pole on the three existing economic poles: the economic pole of fish and rice, which covers the southwestern provinces. Cambodia.
After the courtesy call and discussion, the Chinese President also hosted a high-level friendly meal for Samdech Techo and the delegation.
Please note that Samdech Techo Prime Minister of Cambodia is leading a delegation to visit China. In addition to meeting with the President of the People's Republic of China, Samdech Techo also met with the Speaker of the National Assembly and the Prime Minister of the People's Republic of China, Li Keqiang.
After the meeting, Samdech Techo and Mr. Ly Ker Chheang co-chaired the signing ceremony of some important documents. About 12 documents are expected to be signed during the visit.
