Thirty military and police trainees complete explosive ordnance disposal training for UN peacekeeping operations
(Phnom Penh): After a month of hard training, 30 trainees of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Ministry of Interior, including two women, completed a training course on explosive ordnance disposal for the United Nations peacekeeping operation. Nations under the cooperation and financing of the French Republic.
This training is to provide more new knowledge and fill in the gaps for capacity building for the Blue Hat Force to understand the basic explosive ordnance disposal procedures in achieving both national and UN missions.
The Closing Ceremony of the Training Course was held on the morning of February 10, 2023 under the chairmanship of General Pol Saroeun, Senior Minister in Charge of Deployment, Mr. Jacques Pellet, Ambassador of France to Cambodia, General Sem Sovanny, Vice Chairman of the National Committee and Director General of the National Peacekeeping Center, as well as the leaders of the National Center, as well as French military teachers and leaders of the National Center.
He pointed out that the French side has also provided equipment and military personnel to train explosive ordnance disposal skills for the Cambodian army to be more capable in carrying out UN missions, in particular, and has been making significant contributions to Build the intellectual capital of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, which is the key to building, developing and ensuring the competitiveness of the Cambodian Army in the regional and global community.
