(Phnom Penh): According to the joint statement of the Editor-in-Chief of the Cambodian Press, the recommendation of the Minister of Information, Mr. Khieu Kanharith, on 10 February 2023, the Committee
The Director of the Club of Cambodian Journalists (CCJ) held a meeting to review and discuss the establishment of the Press Council of Cambodia.
The CEC Board of Directors believes that the establishment of the Media Ethics Council is very important in orienting the fines as well as improving the journalism profession, especially for the current situation of journalism in Cambodia.
Beginning with today's meeting, the CEC Board of Directors has decided to set up a committee to review and conduct ethics from other ASEAN countries and other countries to supplement your club's code of conduct. Cambodian newspapers to be better than today and in line with the evolution of the digital age.
In order to carry out this work smoothly and effectively, the Board of Directors will also set up another committee, which will be composed of a mix of relevant institutions and experts, including legal experts, to study in detail and in depth before proceeding to establish In the form of a Press Ethics Council.
The CJCC will establish a series of first and large-scale forums to discuss and disseminate media ethics for the first time in early April, starting with more than 500 CEC members from 172 institutions to Members of the CJC receive the common essence of journalistic ethics and promote the promotion of ethical respect with high responsibility.
