General knowledge: The beautiful light at the North Pole and the South Pole is called what light and how it occurs?
It is at these two poles of our planet that solar particles react with gases in the Earth's atmosphere and form beautiful light phenomena in the sky. Because our environment is rich in oxygen and nitrogen, Aurora lights are usually green, but sometimes red, blue, or purple.
India, Russia vow to boost energy cooperation
MOSCOW (Reuters) - Senior executives of major Russian energy companies are attending a week-long summit on India's energy sector as Moscow and New Delhi pledge to strengthen their ties and expand economic cooperation. . This is according to the publication by the Russian newspaper RT on Thursday, February 9, 2023.
India, the world's third-largest oil importer, has begun boosting energy purchases from Russia after Western sanctions forced Moscow to offer a discount on its exports. Throughout 2022, New Delhi has evolved from a small Russian oil buyer to a major consumer of Moscow. In December alone, Moscow supplied India with 1.17 million barrels of crude oil a day.
India imports many types of crude oil from Russia, including lesser-known ones. Indian officials have repeatedly said that New Delhi will continue to pursue an independent policy and is seeking a stable energy relationship with Russia.
