(Phnom Penh): General Department of Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud "KPR" On the morning of February 9, 2023, a seminar was held on disseminating laws and regulations related to the food sector.
The workshop was chaired by Mr. Phan Aun, Royal Government of Cambodia delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud "KPR". At the invitation of Dr. Suong Noy, Deputy Secretary General of the National Committee for the Promotion of Village 1 Product 1, and Mr. Lim Phara, Vice President of the Cambodian Food Producers Association, as well as Ms. Food Business Operators (Small and Medium Enterprises) Many.
The purpose of this workshop is to provide food business operators with a clear understanding of the Food Safety Law and the sub-decree on the conditions, procedures and procedures for food surveillance and seizure that all food business operators are required to follow.
The Food Safety Law sets out a framework and mechanism for managing and ensuring the safety, quality, hygiene and legitimacy of food at all stages of the food production chain to provide health protection and food safety for consumers and ensure Honest food trading.
This law applies to the management of food quality and safety, covering all stages of the food production chain and the food business in Cambodia.
This law is important to set the basic principles to promote food products that are safe, quality and in line with the standards set to ensure the level of protection of life and health of the people, ensure the effectiveness of protection of consumer interests, contribute significantly to the cut. Reduce the poverty of the people.
