Fitch raises China's growth forecast for 523 to 5%
NEW YORK (Reuters) - Debt rating agency Fitch revised its forecast for China's economic growth in 2023 to 5 percent from 4.1 percent as consumption and activity widened. Recover faster than initially expected after the completion of the Kovid Zero measure. According to Reuters.
According to Reuters, US Fitch said the economic recovery will be driven primarily by consumption. The agency notes that many indicators have recently recovered, although still below pre-epidemic levels.
Despite raising the forecast, the debt rating agency expects this year's economic recovery to be slower than in 2021, when China's economy announced GDP growth of 8.4 percent. Percentage.
"This is partly due to the ongoing weakness in the real estate market, which shows little evidence of the beginning of a recovery in sales or growth," Reuters reported in a Fitch statement. "Housing construction by the end of 2022, despite increased policy support."
