The hospital provides cataract examination and surgery services with specialized doctors, as well as state-of-the-art Japanese standard medical equipment and facilities.
Members of the State Buddhist Association of Cambodia pay a study visit to the National Assembly
(Phnom Penh): About 70 members of the State Buddhist Association of Cambodia, led by Ms. Men Neary Vuthy, Head of the Delegation of the State Buddhist Association of Cambodia, paid a study visit to the National Assembly on the morning of February 9, 2023 to learn about the structure of roles. And the duties of the supreme institution of this nation.
Mr. Leng Peng Lang, Secretary General of the National Assembly and his colleagues warmly welcomed the visit and presented a presentation on the role and responsibilities of the National Assembly and its overview, as well as a presentation on women's statistics in the legal field related to the promotion of gender equality. Empower women and demonstrate parliamentary work as well as other mechanisms in promoting gender equality.
Mr. Leng Peng Lang emphasized that the National Assembly is the place of work of the deputies as well as the place of all the people. And the General Secretariat of the National Assembly is the staff of the National Assembly, which has the main responsibility to provide all kinds of services and techniques to the day-to-day running of the National Assembly in fulfilling its duties to the people and the nation.
He said that the National Assembly is the supreme body representing the nation's democracy because the National Assembly is formed by the will of the people through elections every five years. At the same time, he gave a detailed presentation on the three main tasks of the National Assembly, which are the legislative work, monitoring the implementation of the law of the Royal Government and the representation of the people.
Ms. Men Neary Vuthy expressed her deep gratitude to Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia for allowing the members of the State Buddhist Association of Cambodia to visit the National Assembly building in person and also to Mr. Leng Peng Long. Welcoming and giving a detailed presentation on the work of the National Assembly to the delegates of the State Buddhist Association of Cambodia.
At the same time, Ms. Men Neary Vuthy expressed her pleasure that this visit is a valuable opportunity for members of the State Buddhist Association of Cambodia to gain more knowledge about the role of the National Assembly of Cambodia is to expand more knowledge about the law. Methods and procedures of the national legislature. In addition, members of the State Buddhist Association of Cambodia also visited some important places in the National Assembly.
