CEO: Digital asset market will be another new option for investors in the securities sector of Cambodia
(Korea): Mr. Su Socheat, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Securities Regulator of Cambodia, said that the Securities Regulator of Cambodia has been developing another new product in the securities market, the digital asset market, which is a new option for investors. Trading in the market.
He expressed optimism that "the first phase of the development of the digital asset market will be an option for another investment in the securities sector of Cambodia."
"Digital assets are very important to use as a source to organize, store, share and secure, and are very useful for key business operations such as marketing, branding and business development," he said. And so on. "Developing a thriving market requires the efforts and involvement of the private sector."
However, he also expressed concern about the rapid development of information technology systems, which could pose a risk to the market, causing investors to lose money due to the lack of specific management regulations that will affect this. To the confidence of the market and the sector as a whole.
He stressed that in order to hedge this risk, the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia has been drafting regulations to establish and regulate the digital asset market in Cambodia. However, in order to promote market efficiency, better risk management and create new opportunities, the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia has adopted the Guidelines on Environmental Testing of Financial Technology in the Securities Sector.
For companies participating in the financial technology testing environment, can test their products and services with real customers, but within a certain size and time before launching and promoting the use of a wide range.
He said that after the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia approved the implementation of this guideline, nine companies have submitted a letter of intent, of which three companies are in the application stage.
