(Phnom Penh): On June 5, 2022, a group of 4 suspects broke into electronic devices, including: 9 laptops and 17 computer headphones of LG. Located at 135, Street 93, Village 1, Sangkat Monorom, Khan 7 Makara, Phnom Penh, and escaped safely.
Representatives of LG then filed a complaint with the Phnom Penh Military Police in Khan 7 Makara to help search for the suspect. After receiving the complaint, the 7 Makara District Armed Forces launched an investigation to arrest the suspects and bring them to justice.
Until February 1-2, 2023, the Khan 7 Makara Military Force, in cooperation with the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie and Meanchey District Military Police, arrested two suspects in a row.
The first suspect is Chhun Sopheak, male, 34 years old, unspecified occupation, current address is Street 149, Village 3, Sangkat Veal Vong, Khan 7 Makara, and the second suspect is Ung Bunthoeun, male, 42 years old, occupation: Worker, currently living in a rented house in Sangkat Boeung Tumpun, Khan Meanchey. As for the suspects who escaped, the Phnom Penh Military Police is continuing to search and arrest them.
The two suspects also confessed that on June 5, 2022, they actually climbed the wall, walked through the roof of the building and stole the LG Electronics. They sold it, shared the money, and then separated.
Until February 1 and 2, 2023, they were detained by the military police. As for the suspect, Ung Bunthoeun said that during 2000, he was imprisoned for 5 years in connection with the theft of electricity from a trader around Wat Koh.
The two suspects are currently being investigated by the Phnom Penh Anti-Criminal Bureau of the Phnom Penh Military Police and will be sent to court for legal action.
(Phnom Penh): The Governor of Kampong Speu Province, Mr. Vy Samnang, on the morning of February 9, 2023, confirmed that there was no clearing to build a road to climb to the top of Khnong Phsar, and the construction site was shared on social media. That saw the clearing of the road, just to prepare for the installation of light poles across parts of the road up to the top of the mountain.
Mr. Vy Samnang's statement was made at a press conference of the Royal Government Spokesperson's Unit and to end the doubts of the people, especially those who like to travel uphill after sharing pictures of the clearing site of the road up. Phnom Khnong Phsar Resort is located in Rolak Kang Cheung, Oral District.
The Governor of Kampong Speu Province said, "I would like to emphasize that you may be confused that this is a state project or something, but not because we are growing economically, especially in the industrial sector, which requires electricity. So much. "So we have to prepare to pull the light pole, so he has to transport the equipment to set up the light pole, so he has to clear this road."
Vy Samnang continues to claim that the state has no plans to build a road to the top of Khnong Phsar, an attractive eco-tourism site. He cited the slogan that you used to go to Phnom Khnong Phsar, "To see the beautiful scenery, you have to cross a difficult road" and that going up to this area is irreversible, that is, for those who like adventure to rest. At the top of the mountain.
Please be informed that Phnom Khnong Phsar is an area of "natural paradise" buried in a large mountain forest located in Taing Pum village, Rolak Kang Cheung area, Ta Sal commune, Oral district, Kampong Speu province. Khnong Phsar is a junction of three corners that connects three provinces: Koh Kong, Kampong Speu and Pursat. Khnong Phsar is an area rich in dense forests, high valleys, beautiful meadows and rich in rare species of wildlife.
However, before reaching the top of the mountain, tourists face many difficulties by traveling on foot for more than 5 to 7 hours.
