Ministry of Environment prepares 16 master plans for Kesor Kol Sok An Research and Conservation Center in Phnom Kulen to turn into a conservation and study tourism area
(Siem Reap): The Ministry of Environment has prepared a master plan for 16 areas at the "Kesor Kol (Orchid) Sok An Phnom Kulen" Research and Conservation Center to transform into development zones such as infrastructure, research, education, outreach, animal husbandry and Other development mechanisms.
Kes Kol Sok An Phnom Kulen Research and Conservation Center is located in Banteay Srei District, Siem Reap Province, at the foot of Kulen Mountain near the entrance to the Kulen Ridge Resort.
She said the center was established in 2019 with a total area of 2,020 hectares. The main purpose of establishing this center has four main objectives: first: to focus on research, second: to preserve the conservation of Cambodia's wild species and plants, and third: to educate and disseminate in order to People understand the rich national cultural heritage of Cambodia and fourth: how to link the economy and conservation.
The senior official confirmed that the Kes Kol Sok An Research and Conservation Center in Phnom Kulen is also a place for recreation and also a place that can help create jobs for people and additional income, not only for protection but also for Section for economic development. The center is under the management of the Ministry of Environment, after receiving permission from the Royal Government, she is in charge and has prepared a master plan for 16 areas.
At the same time, the official said that the research center and conservation of Kesor Sok An Phnom Kulen is becoming a division of the center's development areas, such as infrastructure, research, education, animal husbandry. And collaboration with development partners and mechanisms.
Ms. Somaly expressed her belief that the establishment of this center is also a place for entertainment and also a place that can help her people find more income. This means that the goal of establishing this center is not only for defense but also for the economic development of the nation.
