General knowledge: What causes wind?
The reason it is called trade wind is because in the European colonial era, European merchants often traveled by sea, knowing the wind and using the wind to blow their ships to nearby places to explore new lands. Trade with the outside world, such as Asia, Africa, the United States, islands, etc., so this wind is called "trade wind".
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia is ready to send about 40 prison officials of the Ministry of Interior to carry out peacekeeping missions under the umbrella of the United Nations.
This preparation was confirmed by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, on February 08, 2023, at a meeting on sending prison officials to join the United Nations (UN) peacekeeping mission at the UN headquarters. Ministry of Interior.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng emphasized that "Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, has agreed to the United Nations' request to send 40 Cambodian prison officials to carry out peacekeeping missions under an umbrella. "The United Nations."
Prince Sar Kheng recalled that at a meeting held in Singapore about 10 years ago, senior UN officials had initiated the deployment of police forces to carry out missions under the UN umbrella in addition to sending troops.
Samdech instructed the Secretary of State in charge of Prisons and the Director General of Prisons to establish an internal mechanism for the Ministry of Interior to do this work and to have a mechanism for cooperation with the National Center for the Management of Peacekeeping Forces, Demining and Remnants of War.
The United Nations currently has more than 9,000 peacekeepers from more than 90 countries around the world. Most UN police forces are on a mission to provide support to the respective police forces in their respective countries.
