Kampot Provincial Court issues order to protect a plot of land in Boeung Tarong village, Prey Khmum commune, Teuk Chhou district after the land owner owed money but could not pay
Kampot Provincial Court issued the following decision:
1: Recognize the application for protection order dated December 26, 2022 of Mr. Heng Chanveasna as the lawyer representing the mandate to the creditors in accordance with the form and legal opinion.
2. Prohibit co-debtors named May Borey and his wife named Kouch Srey Muy from the process of registering ownership, selling, renting, mortgaging property, making gifts, making donations, making inheritance, especially on land with title deed to the real estate No. 006011. Dated August 18, 2014, located in Boeung Tarong village, Prey Khmum commune, Teuk Chhou district, Kampot province, temporarily waiting for the court to decide on the case.
3. The Co-Debtor shall deposit 139,828.54 (one hundred and thirty-nine thousand eight hundred and twenty-eight US dollars) at the Secretariat of the Kampot Provincial Court in order to cancel the confiscation practice. Temporarily.
4: Tax application fees are the responsibility of the creditors.
