Cambodia expects Japan to open cashew processing plant for export to international market
(Phnom Penh): The President of the Cambodian Cashew Association has high expectations that Japanese companies will decide to invest in a large cashew processing plant for export to international markets this year.
Mr. Uon Silot expects this after the senior management of three companies from Japan came to study the potential of the cashew sector for the last time and met with the Minister of Agriculture to decide to invest in opening a processing plant. Cashews While the companies are looking at 10 provinces with the potential to grow cashews.
"This study is the final decision on whether or not to open two cashew processing plants," he said. "If the two factories open, there will be two more factories: the crude oil mill, the cashew nut factory and the industrial charcoal factory from the crushed cashew nuts."
He expects that after the last visit, the Japanese company will decide to invest in a cashew processing plant to help provide value to farmers, create jobs in the community, give confidence to other foreign investors and provide standardized value. High on Cambodian goods. If the plant opens, it will be able to produce about 20,000 tons of cashew nuts per year.
In a meeting with the Director General of Top Planning Japan on February 7, 2023, Mr. Dith Tina, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, expressed his full welcome and support for the project to establish a large cashew processing plant in Cambodia to bring Cambodian cashews to the world market.
The Minister recommended a plan to produce processed cashews to get higher prices than quantity, in which processing must comply with environmental principles.
He added that promotion is a necessary factor to gain support and confidence in both the Japanese and global markets, get a high price, and consumers know about Cambodia without the goal of quantitative competition with other countries.
"In this regard, the Ministry will support the promotion and promotion in the production chain, including packaging," he said.
At the same time, the Minister praised the innovative ideas in processing cashew nuts into fuel and suggested to consider processing into food products or agricultural fertilizers while Cambodia is in need of fertilizer.
Processed cashew nuts are a potential agricultural export in the Japanese market. From 2019 to 2022, processed cashew nuts were exported to Japan about 184.90 tons, of which in 2022 there were 126.44 tons.
According to Uon Siloth, in addition to the Japanese company, a Chinese company is also looking at the opportunity to open a cashew processing factory, which is choosing an investment location between Kampong Thom and Kratie provinces. The company's management will visit and finalize this February.
