As of early February 2023, the US Federal Reserve has decided to raise interest rates by another 0.25%, raising the dollar rate to 4.75%, putting pressure on banks and microfinance institutions.
The leaders of the Association of Banks in Cambodia and the Association of Microfinance in Cambodia made this statement at a press conference on "Situation of the banking and financial sector and measures to respond to the provision of informal financial services" on the 7th. February 2023 at the Banking Association of Cambodia.
Rath Sophoan, vice president of the Banking Association of Cambodia, said that over the past year, interest rates in the United States have risen steadily, from the beginning of 2022 to only 0.25% of the dollar. From March 2022 to January 2023, the interest rate of the dollar in the international market increased continuously, rising from 0.25 to 4.75%.
He said the rise in interest rates has put a lot of pressure on economies in developing countries.
"The US Federal Reserve raising interest rates has led regulators and operators in the banking sector to keep a close eye on everyone as it affects the overall trade situation in the world, especially on the global economy," he said. "Developing countries."
He said that despite the high interest rates in the international market and the high interest rates of Cambodian banks, the Cambodian banks continued to provide normal loans with a slight increase in interest rates. Compared with the rise in interest rates in the international market and the savings rate of banking institutions in Cambodia.
Mr. Sok Voeun, Chairman of the Board of the Microfinance Association of Cambodia, stated that maintaining the same interest rate has caused the MFI to lose part of its annual profit. However, MFIs will not raise interest rates in the international market so as not to burden customers with higher interest rates.
However, he confirmed that maintaining the same interest rate has not caused the microfinance institutions to suffer losses.
According to the leaders of both associations, the Cambodian banking system has achieved good results and has made a significant contribution to maintaining macroeconomic stability and supporting economic growth, which is estimated at a recovery rate of 5.1%. The riel exchange rate against the US dollar has been kept stable at around 4,102 riel per US dollar, and the 2022 inflation rate is 5.5%.
On February 1, 2023, the US Federal Reserve decided to raise the benchmark interest rate by a further 0.25% to keep inflation low. According to the US Federal Reserve, the rate hike is not over yet, and there may be two or three more hikes in the future, despite the latest rate hike. This is at a lower rate than previous installations.
