(Kampong Cham): Mr. Un Chanda, President of Kampong Cham Provincial Red Cross Branch and his colleagues on the morning of February 7, 2023, visited and brought humanitarian donations from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross. To a family affected by a fire that killed three children in Angkor Ban III village, Angkor Ban commune, Kang Meas district, Kampong Cham province.
Mr. Touch Chhay, Executive Director of Kampong Cham Provincial Red Cross Branch, said that the owner of the house, 56-year-old Yael, had a wife and five children who were affected by the fire in the village.
Mr. Touch Chhay said that this incident happened at 3:30 am on February 7, 2023 due to an electric shock, causing a house made of stone under wood on a 6-meter tile roof. 8m was completely damaged by fire.
Suddenly, the parents, after blessing the two small children, came out and woke up the other three sleeping children who were sleeping in the same room, but the locked room could not be saved. On the other hand, due to the fire, the father was forced to kick the window and jump to the ground, causing serious injuries. The three daughters (17 years, 15 years and 10 years) were burned to death. Currently, her husband Elya is receiving emergency treatment in Phnom Penh.
