A-level students at Buor High School, Phnom Preuk District, Battambang Province, received a scholarship from Samdech Techo to study at a medical school (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Assistant to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Buor, Phnom Proek district, Battambang province, studied at the University of Health Sciences according to his wishes.
On the morning of Monday, February 6, 2023, Mr. Keo Phong, Assistant to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and his team arrived at the home of Ms. Von Surany in Buor Commune, Phnom Proek District, Battambang Province.
Visit to Surany's house to check the family situation of this outstanding student on the rural land and announce the Samdech Techo Scholarship for her to study at the University of Health Sciences. In addition, Mr. Keo Phong and his team also donated Samdech Techo, including budget and some food items to Ms. Surani.
Mr. Keo Phong told Fresh News that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, through his assistant, had decided to provide a scholarship to Surany to study at the University of Health Sciences if she passed the exam. But if he does not pass, even if this young woman goes to study other subjects, Samdech Techo will also give her a scholarship. In addition to providing scholarships, Samdech Techo also advised to consider accommodation and other expenses while studying in Phnom Penh.
Von Surany is the only student to receive an A grade for 2022 out of more than 100 students from Buor High School in Buor Commune, Phnom Proek District, Battambang Province. Buor High School is a remote high school on the Khmer-Thai border.
Studying medicine at the University of Health Sciences is the biggest desire of this rural student. But the family situation where his parents live as a farmer puts this young man in challenge to achieve his goal.
Therefore, on February 2, through Fresh News, Surani and her mother, who were invited to a meeting with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, insisted on a scholarship from Samdech Techo to be able to study at the University of Health Sciences. .
After meeting in person with Samdech Techo's assistant and announcing the scholarship, Surany and her family were overjoyed.
Ms. Surany expressed her deepest gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen for helping to achieve their wishes. The young woman wished Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen good health and long life to continue to lead Cambodia to progress.
