(Phnom Penh): General Santibandit Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner, accompanied by the leadership of the National Police General Commission, on February 6, 2023, paid tribute to the late Lok Chumteav Bun Sotha, who passed away on February 3. 2023 at 18:13 at the age of 67 due to illness.
In a condolence message to Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen on February 3, 2023, General Santibandit Neth Savoeun and his wife, as well as the National Police, are deeply saddened by the death of Lok Chumteav Bun Sotha. . In this time of sorrow, General Dr. Neth Savoeun would like to share this sad death.
The death of Lok Chumteav Bun Sotha is a tragic loss, the most incomparable loss of a brother, sister-in-law, wife, mother and grandmother, a deeply cherished and precious Brahmin, and a loss of Buddhism. A kind and sincere person in Buddhism.
Please note that Lok Chumteav Bun Sotha is the sister of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen. The body was laid to rest in a traditional Buddhist ceremony at house 66, street 528, corner of street 285 in Sangkat Boeung Kak I, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh. Cambodia seeks rice exports to Philippine market
The two sides agreed to study the possibility of re-signing a memorandum of understanding on rice trade under state and state mechanisms, which is expected to be signed soon. At the same time, the Philippine side also allows free trade in rice under the private and direct image, according to the quantity, quality and price agreed between the two sides.
During the visit, the Cambodian delegation also discussed the mechanism and technical terms and prices for supply with Philippine rice importers. As a result, those importers are interested in the quality of rice and intend to import Cambodian rice into Philippine market as well.
It should be noted that the Philippines is a rice producer and also a major importer of rice in Asia, in fact, in 2022, the Philippines imported 3.82 million tons of rice from other countries. Most are plain white rice.
