(Siem Reap): Wat Svay Romeat in Siem Reap province has organized the Meak Bochea ceremony to commemorate three major events in Buddhism: the quadrangular event, the day on which the Buddha passed away, and the day on which the Buddha performed the Patimok advice.
The Meak Bochea ceremony at Wat Svay Romeat was attended by many Buddhist relatives, students and monks on Sunday, February 15, 2023.
Meak Bochea Day is an important event in Buddhism to commemorate the great Buddha when he was alive and to commemorate three major events: First, to commemorate the Quadrangle Day of the 1250 monks on 15 Born in May. Second, to commemorate the day of the Buddha's enlightenment, and third, the day on which the Buddha performed the Patimok advice.
Please note that the main contents of Meak Bochea Day are as follows:
* It is the day of the birth of Sangkha, that in the next three months, Tathagata will attain Nirvana.
* The day that Sariputta became a sage on the world as the first great apostle, better than any other monk among the wise apostles.
