Ms. O Vandin's appeal was made this morning, February 6, 2023, on the occasion of inspecting the 19-dose Kovid vaccination process to promote the sixth dose in schools in Phnom Penh, together with Ms. Kim Sethany, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports. The two high schools she inspected were Chea Sim Santhor Mok High School and Indratevi High School.
In an interview with the press, Ms. O Vandin claimed that according to the observation, some students were vaccinated on time according to the instructions, but some students were interrupted due to some parents not allowing or not advising. Her children are vaccinated on a regular basis for a variety of reasons.
At this point, the chairman of the Committee on Immunization of Kovid 19 called on parents or parents of students not to worry about the quality, effectiveness or side effects of this vaccine, on the contrary, if given properly on time will help the immune system. Of children, they are better able to prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
"I call on parents and guardians of students across the country not to worry about the vaccine, as the 19 Kovid vaccine we use today is a well-recognized vaccine," the health official said. From the World Health Organization. "All the vaccines we use are recognized."
Ms. O Vandin asserted that under the effective management and care of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, irrigation vaccination against Kovid 19 was effective and timely irrigation created conditions for the country. Cambodia can reopen in all areas.
She stressed that until now, Cambodia has benefited greatly from the Kovid 19 vaccine, which has saved lives. "The reason we continue to inject the booster dose until the sixth dose is because the effectiveness of the vaccine does not last long, that is, a period of time (6 to 8 months) will decrease, so it is necessary to inject the booster dose," she said.
Ms. O'Vandin added that Kovid 19 has not gone far from us yet and it has been constantly evolving, so if the individual's defenses are reduced, it will be easier for Kovid 19 to Offensive and serious. For these reasons, parents of students must allow their children to receive the recommended dose.
At the same time, Ms. O Vandin said that the injection of Kovid-19 vaccine (3rd dose, 4th dose, 5th dose and 6th dose) by Samdech Techo (Thida) Youth Volunteer Doctors to students, teachers And academic staff in primary, secondary and high schools in Phnom Penh from February 6 to March 4, 2023.
