Senior official of the Ministry of Environment: Local community development contributes to improving the livelihoods of local communities and protected area communities
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Khvay Atiya, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, stated that the development of local communities contributes to improving the lives of local communities and protected area communities.
The remarks of the senior official of the Ministry of Environment were made at the closing ceremony of the training course on tourism guide, hospitality and chef skills for the protected area community in Kampong Thom province, which took place on February 6, 2023 at the Department of Environment. Kampong Thom Province.
On that occasion, Mr. Khvay Atiya added that currently there are 73 protected areas in Cambodia, covering an area of about 7.3 million hectares, which is the basis for establishing natural protection communities to better protect natural resources for Descendants.
Mr. Khvay Atiya added that Cambodia has strengthened the management of natural resources and the conservation of biodiversity, improving the livelihood of local communities, educating and promoting the spirit of "Cambodia, my motherland", which has turned the environment into a "green belt" and aims to ensure excellence. Long-term national interests in terms of environment, economy, society, culture and politics.
The Ministry of Environment has established the Community Exhibition Project, the first community exhibition project under the guidance of His Excellency the Minister, in order to promote the protection of the protected area community by creating jobs for the community families. This project is to be implemented first in Kampong Thom province.
People from protected area communities can gain skills and be able to work in the community to earn an income to improve their family life.
