BEIJING, Feb. 5 (Xinhua) - Sixteen people were killed and dozens more injured in a series of car crashes on a highway in central China on Sunday, authorities said. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Sunday, February 5, 2023.
Nearly 50 vehicles collided on a highway in Hunan province on Saturday night, with some vehicles catching fire, local traffic police said in a statement.
Sixteen people were killed and 66 others were injured in the crash, police said.
