(Pursat): At least 101 students fainted in a row at Hun Sen Pramoy Secondary School and High School in Veal Veng District for 3 days, on 2-3 and 5 February. Go to Pursat Provincial Referral Hospital for treatment while the doctor did not find any disease but may be from air poisoning.
It should be reminded that on February 2-3, 61 students developed anxiety, difficulty breathing, soft hands and feet, fainted, some of which have recovered and some have returned home.
Veal Veng District Governor Vong Eng said that after the incident, the school's director and authorities were preparing to hold a ceremony for the owner of the land to take care of the land on February 5. Surprisingly, during the ceremony, 40 students cried and fainted, including a male student who had difficulty breathing and had soft hands and feet like the previous 61 students.
Mr. Vong Eng said that they were sent to the Pramoy Health Center and continued to be sent to Pursat Referral Hospital, while the examination and diagnosis that there is no disease, but may be from "air poisoning."
He said that many students have now recovered, and only two or three are still recovering, and doctors are continuing to monitor.
