Business Awareness: Businessmen say the establishment of a Cambodian private business center in China will be a place to display and sell Cambodian products, providing good opportunities for businesses to capture the market
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia plans to establish five Cambodian private business centers in China to further promote and promote the sale of Cambodian products in the Chinese market, while the Cambodian private business center now has one location in Japan. .
Speaking at the 2022 Business Review Meeting and 2023 Business Implementation Goals, Minister of Commerce Pan Sosak said that the Ministry of Commerce plans to study the establishment of five more Cambodian private business centers in China. In Changchun, Harbin, Nanjing, Taiyuan and Zhengzhou to further promote and promote the sale of Cambodian products in the Chinese market.
Pen Sovicheat, secretary of state and spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce, told Fresh News that a project to establish five Cambodian private business centers in China was in the process of being processed by the two countries' relevant authorities.
He added that the Cambodian Private Business Center Abroad was established with the aim of promoting trade and promoting Cambodia's cultural, tourism and trade policies with partner countries. The products that can benefit the most from this private business center are the potential products of Cambodia that are promoted in the international market, such as fresh agricultural products, processed agricultural products, nests and souvenirs.
