(Kampong Speu): A solar irrigation system donated by Coca-Cola Cambodia has been handed over to the Cardamom Mountain National Park Office in Kampong Speu Province as a means of irrigating nurseries.
The handover of this irrigation system is part of Coca-Cola's global efforts to contribute to environmental sustainability, climate change adaptation, and building a better common future for local communities and contributing to community-based greening and care. Maintain water sources.
The handover ceremony was presided over by Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, on the morning of February 4, 2023, with the participation of officials of Kampong Speu Provincial Department of Environment and representatives of Coca-Cola Cambodia and members of local authorities. .
He said Cambodia was at a turning point in conserving income through the sale of carbon credits and eco-tourism. Ecotourism, which is providing income to communities in protected areas.
Ms. Sambath Monivorleak, Director of Public Relations and Sustainability for Coca-Cola Cambodia, said, “At Coca-Cola, we are committed to contributing to climate change mitigation. "The delivery of this irrigation system is a clear example of our commitment to reducing our CO2 emissions, protecting biodiversity and building resilience."
In a similar project, which took place in early 2021, Coca-Cola Cambodia, in collaboration with the APSARA Authority, handed over a solar water well for irrigation of seedlings and green gardens in the Angkor area in the village. Leang Dai, Angkor Thom District, Siem Reap Province.
Coca-Cola is committed to achieving its goal of reducing greenhouse gas emissions by 25% by 2030 and aiming to achieve zero carbon emissions by 2050. The company achieved its 2020 target by reducing its CO2 emissions by 25% by the end of 2020 compared to the 2010 baseline data.
