(Kampong Speu): Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu Province, on February 3, 2023, donated to 171 families affected by the floods from 7 communes of Phnom Sruoch district.
Phnom Sruoch district governor Horn Piseth reports that Phnom Sruoch district was one of five districts in Kampong Speu province that were affected by the floods in January, which were caused by climate change. Make it rain for 4 days in a row.
The floods affected seven communes: Yeay Mao Pich Nil, Taing Samrong, Kraing Divay, O, Treng Trayeung, Moha Saing and Taing Sya communes, affecting 171 families. In addition, the floods also affected 3 schools in Taing Samrong commune, 2 in Yeay Pich Nil commune, 2 hectares of dry rice fields, 32 hectares of various crops and 3,752 meters of road infrastructure.
On that occasion, Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu Province, said that the climate change caused rain for 4 consecutive days, from 10 to 14 January, which is the month in the dry season. This month's rain, it really has never been before, and there has never been a flood this month. In response to the impact that the people face, the provincial administration, under the auspices of the Dignified Life Organization, has provided first aid to address daily living.
Mr. Vy Samnang emphasized that the gifts given at this time, of course, facilitated the eating for a while, so that you can resume work. At the same time, you must consider the health of living, be hygienic, eat clean, drink clean to avoid various diseases, and also bring family members of all ages to be vaccinated in all doses to prevent Kovid 19. Fire burns about 10 hectares of heavy plantations in Svay Leu district, Siem Reap province
(Siem Reap): The joint police force of Svay Leu district, Siem Reap province, cooperated to help put out the fire in the plantation of Thnong tree, which was burnt down by about 10 hectares due to the fire from the rice fields of the villagers.
