Tomorrow morning! Pursat and Trat governors will meet to promote economic and tourism cooperation between the two provinces
(Pursat): On the morning of February 4, 2023, tomorrow, the Governor of Pursat Province and the Governor of Trat Province, Thailand will hold a meeting to promote economic and tourism cooperation between the border provinces of the two countries.
The meeting will be held at Pursat Provincial Hall under the chairmanship of Mr. Khoy Rida, Governor of Pursat and Mr. Chham Nanvitterat, Governor of Trat, as well as a delegation and other officials.
The meeting came after the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Royal Government of Thailand pledged to work together to speed up the installation and opening of the remaining three international border crossings to better trade between the two countries.
It should be informed that according to the joint press release on the 7th meeting of the governors of the border provinces between Cambodia and Thailand on September 16, 2022 by video system chaired by General Anupong Pao Chenda, Minister of Interior of the Kingdom of Thailand and Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior of the Kingdom of Cambodia, said that the remaining three border gates have not yet been opened as international gates, including:
* First, An Ses border checkpoint, Preah Vihear province, against An Ma border checkpoint, Ubon Ratchathani province. * Second, the border checkpoint of Thmor Da, Pursat province, against the border checkpoint, Tha Sen, Trat province.
On the morning of February 3, 2023, Mr. Thong Rathsak, Director General of Tourism Development and International Cooperation and Senior Minister of Tourism, led the Ministry of Tourism, Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Cooperation. International Operations and the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation held a bilateral meeting with Shi Zeyi, Director-General of the Ministry of Culture and Tourism of China, and a delegation in Yukarta, Indonesia.
Mr. Thong Rathsak reminded that Cambodia and China have historically had close ties and cooperation with each other, which has so far been a steel friend. China has always supported the development of Cambodia, especially the tourism sector, by supporting the construction of tourism facilities, such as the construction of the new Siem Reap Airport, the Moradok Techo Stadium and the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway, and the development of human resources in the field. Tourism.
Mr. Shi Zeyi praised Cambodia for its continued strong ties and cooperation between the two countries, especially the warm attention and warm welcome to Chinese tourists visiting Cambodia.
Seeing the potential and appropriate time to strengthen tourism cooperation between the two countries during the reopening of China, the two sides agreed on a plan of action to boost tourism flow between the two countries. The following two:
Consider organizing joint art performances to further promote tourism destinations to the people of both countries, as well as to celebrate the 65th anniversary of Cambodia-China diplomatic relations.
* Increase direct flights from Chinese market destinations to Cambodia's three international airports and from Cambodia to China.
* Promote human resource development in tourism.
* Promote the organization of tourism business forums in both countries.
