(Stung Treng): Ms. Hun Dany, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, stated that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has introduced a social protection policy and legal protection for women working in the tourism industry. She said this while chairing a seminar on the implementation of policies to promote the rights and role of women in tourism in Stung Treng.
This workshop was held on the morning of February 3, 2023, co-organized by the Ministry of Tourism and Stung Treng Provincial Department of Tourism under the chairmanship of Mrs. Hun Dany, Secretary of State, Representative of Dr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism.
Secretary of State Hun Dany also said that "women play an important role in strengthening resilience, rehabilitation and development of tourism."
She emphasized that women working in the tourism sector were protected by the tourism law. Women are encouraged to participate and benefit equitably from tourism development.
She said law enforcement and policies have benefited women greatly, such as capacity building, increasing economic empowerment and decision-making, reducing violence, reducing poverty through employment and employment opportunities.
