In the announcement of the Ministry of Interior, obtained by Fresh News on February 3, 2023, it is stated that from 2012, the Ministry of Interior has started to produce and provide Khmer digital identity cards to the people of Cambodia. In December 2022, the Ministry issued 12,309,131 Khmer identity cards to 11,097 people aged 18 and over. .867 people.
According to the data extracted from the Khmer Nationality Identity Management System provided from 2012 and during July 2013 (as of July 2023, 1,727 Khmer Nationality Identity Cards have expired). 094 people.
To solve this problem, the Ministry of Interior has organized a campaign to promote the production of Khmer identity cards to those who have expired duplicate ID cards from November 2022, by extracting data on those who have expired Khmer nationality identity cards and sending them to communes. Across the country to organize a calendar program to invite people in villages, communes, sangkats to fill out the application form for the provision of dual Khmer identity cards.
The Ministry of Interior has set up an inter-departmental working group to monitor and promote the issuance of dual Khmer identity cards on a daily basis, including Saturdays, Sundays and other holidays. At the same time, mobile teams have been organized to visit the backs of houses, ministries, institutions and units to fill out the form to provide dual Khmer identity cards to citizens and government officials, as well as their families.
As of January 22, 2023, 616,721 people have been issued Khmer duplicate identity cards, so the remaining 1,110,373 people have yet to be issued. The main challenge in the process of issuing dual Khmer identity cards is that some people migrate without coming to complete the formalities.
