Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia presents the results of the ASEAN National Tourism Institution Meeting and related meetings in Indonesia
(Indonesia): The 57th Meeting of the ASEAN National Tourism Institutions and Related Meetings was held on 2-3 February 2023 in Yukarta, Indonesia, reviewing various documents to request the ASEAN Tourism Ministers' Meeting. The 26th and related meetings reviewed and approved. This is according to Mr. Thong Rathsak, Director General of Tourism Development and International Cooperation, Ministry of Tourism.
Mr. Thong Rathsak confirmed that the ASEAN National Tourism Institution Meeting and related meetings in Indonesia achieved the following results:
57th ASEAN National Tourism Institution Meeting
The meeting was attended by the presidents of the ASEAN National Tourism Institutions, the ASEAN Secretariat, the ASEAN Center, China, Japan and Korea, the Asia-Pacific Travel Association, the ASEAN Tourism Association, the ASEAN Tourism Research Association and the ASEAN-US Business Council (US-ABC). To prepare for the 26th ASEAN Tourism Ministers' Meeting to be held on February 4, 2023 in Yukarta.
To promote and support the recovery of ASEAN tourism after the Kovid-19 crisis, the ASEAN National Tourism Organization and its partners discussed and agreed as follows:
1. Urge all member countries to implement the ASEAN Guidelines on Safety and Hygiene for Employees and Communities in the Tourism Industry, adopted at the 25th ASEAN Tourism Ministers' Meeting on 19 January 2022 in Sihanoukville.
2. Discuss the implementation of the results of the environmental study on the implementation of mutual recognition of tourism professionals.
3. Develop a plan for the implementation of the ASEAN Framework on Sustainable Tourism Development, which is scheduled to begin and end in 2023.
4. End the ratification of the protocol for the amendment of the Mutual Recognition Agreement on Tourism Professionals.
5. Discuss with the World Tourism Organization on the preparation of a memorandum of understanding, identifying the potential to strengthen the role of tourism in social, economic and environmental development, especially the rehabilitation of tourism after the Kovid-19 crisis.
The meeting was attended by the chairmen of ASEAN, China, Japan, Korea, ASEAN Secretariat and ASEAN-China, ASEAN-Japan and ASEAN-Korea Centers, consisting of about 100 people. The meeting decided:
1. Encourage the implementation of the remaining 13 activities under the ASEAN Plus Three Tourism Cooperation Work Plan 2021-2025 in 2023 by identifying the coordinating countries for each activity.
2. Support and promote the implementation of priority activities in accordance with the ASEAN Tourism Restoration Plan after the Kovid-19 Crisis, adopted at the 25th ASEAN Tourism Ministers' Meeting on 19 January 2022 in Sihanoukville.
3. To mark the 50th anniversary of ASEAN-Japan relations, Japan will host the ASEAN-Japan Tourism Ministers' Special Dialogue Meeting in October 2023 in Tokyo, Japan.
4. Accelerate the implementation of initiatives and priority activities in the ASEAN Plus Three Tourism Plan 2021-2025, focusing on supporting the rehabilitation of tourism in each country and sustainable tourism.
5. Strengthen cooperation in human resource development and tourism promotion.
29th ASEAN-India National Tourism Organization Meeting
The meeting was attended by the chairperson of the National Institutes of Tourism, India, India, ASEAN Secretariat, consisting of about 100 people. The meeting agreed as follows:
1. Accelerate the implementation of the activities set out in the ASEAN-India Tourism Work Plan 2023-2027, focusing on supporting the rehabilitation of tourism in each country, especially marketing activities and capacity building.
2. Support the implementation of the ASEAN Framework on Sustainable Tourism Development as well as the Phnom Penh Declaration on the ASEAN Tourism Revolution for Socio-Economic Birth.
3. Include India as a target market defined in the ASEAN Tourism Marketing Strategy.
* Meeting of ASEAN-Russia National Tourism Institute
The meeting was attended by the chairperson of the ASEAN-Russia National Tourism Organization, the ASEAN Secretariat, consisting of about 100 people. The meeting agreed as follows:
1. Accelerate the implementation of the activities set out in the ASEAN-Russia Tourism Work Plan 2022-2024, focusing on supporting the rehabilitation of tourism in each country, especially marketing activities through the participation of the private sector in tourism activities. And human resource development.
2. Support the implementation of the ASEAN Framework on Sustainable Tourism Development, as well as the Phnom Penh Declaration on the ASEAN Tourism Revolution for Socio-Economic Birth.
