Nop Nget, 40, a resident of Thmey Village, Rovieng Commune, Samrong District, Takeo Province, the brother of the seriously injured victim, Det Thong, said he and his brother had traveled from Takeo to Koh Kong to attend the hearing. According to the procedure, but halfway through, his younger brother suddenly became very ill and returned home.
According to Mr. Nop Nget, he also called the court official at that time to explain the reason, but after talking for a while, the service stopped and he stopped calling for fear of disturbing the officer.
Nop Nget, the victim's plaintiff, intends to ask the court to adjourn the hearing, and if his brother's condition improves, he will definitely attend. He said that the $ 2,000 compensation provided by the perpetrators had almost been spent on medical treatment, so he wanted to ask for additional compensation to treat his brother.
