More than half of Cambodia's garment, footwear and travel accessories account for more than $ 10 billion in exports
(Phnom Penh): Garment, footwear and travel products account for more than half of Cambodia's total exports in 2022, valued at more than $ 10 billion.
According to a 2022 report by the Ministry of Commerce, Cambodia exported more than $ 9 billion worth of garments, an increase of more than $ 1 billion, or 13 percent, or about 40 percent of total exports. Footwear exports were valued at $ 1,737 million, up 25 percent, and exports of $ 1.777 billion were up 19 percent from the same period in 2021.
Tycoon Ly Khun Thai, Honorary President of the Footwear and Travel Products Association, told Fresh News that the garment sector has played an important role in the Cambodian economy and created jobs for Cambodians. There are now about 1 million workers working in factories all over the country, making life easier for his family.
However, for 2023, garment exports may face some challenges as orders do not increase earlier this year.
He added: "The problem is that by 2022, exports to Europe and the United States, sales will decline, with too much inventory left, not yet sold. "The key factor is the war between Ukraine and Russia, which has pushed up the price of raw materials around the world."
Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, recently stated that in 2022, exports of garments, footwear and travel accessories will account for about 57% of total exports. Of Cambodia, while this sector contributes about 10% of Cambodia's GDP. Cambodia's main markets are the United States and the European Union.
He added that the Royal Government plans to improve the quality of Cambodia's garment products to get more value and encourage more Cambodian investors to invest in this sector, while currently investing in the garment sector about 95. % Are foreigners.
In particular, the newly registered investment projects in Cambodia observed that the investment projects to build factories, clothing, footwear and travel equipment are also more than other sectors. Chinese, Japanese diplomats discuss concerns over disputed islands in East China Sea
