(Tbong Khmum): The construction of 1 million curtains planted by Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment and Chairman of the National Task Force for Ou Raing Ov District, Tbong Khmum Province has already been organized around the dry river in the area of Preah Temple. Theat Basrey is located in Preah Theat Commune, Ou Raing Ov District, Tbong Khmum Province.
The 1 million curtains that are planned to be planted here are dedicated to the New Year deity, who is scheduled to come to bless the people on the occasion of the traditional New Year in mid-April 2023 and to rule the territory of the Kingdom of Cambodia. Ahead.
Similarly, Mr. Svay Saroeun, Chief of Thnal Keng Village, Preah Theat Commune, Oreang Ov District, Tbong Khmum Province, said, More and more, especially during the upcoming Khmer New Year, which will boost people's livelihoods, as well as may have enough water to grow crops in all seasons.
One million curtain trees will flourish on the river of history and will make tourists from near and far come to relax with new achievements in the land of Ou Raing Ov, which is born of all leaders Special Class, Basic Strengthening Committee to preserve the legacy of the next generation of what is born of peace now.
It should be noted that according to the ancient legends related to the history of the dry river, it is said that in the beginning, the Khmer king used to come and do as he wished, and then he went to offer offerings, including A pair of golden palms in the river. Later, this place became a place where there was no water and the old people called it the dry river.
Khmer kings who reigned in history, especially the old ones, narrated that there was a black prince with great power to help preserve the land was here. In ancient times, it is said that King Kan, a Khmer king who reigned between 1512-1525, also came to pray for victory in ancient warfare. From then on, Wat Preah Theat Basrey has always been a land full of faith and respect.
