Director General of Accounting and Auditing: Adhering to a proper accounting culture will help brighten the tax culture
The workshop was held on February 2, 2023, with the participation of the management and officials of the Accounting and Auditing Regulators, as well as the presence of a total of 550 representatives of enterprises and non-profit organizations.
The forum is designed to disseminate and raise awareness of accounting and auditing obligations and related regulations and the submission of online financial statements to directors, enterprises, nonprofits, and beneficiaries. Responsible for the accounting work of enterprises and non-profit organizations.
Mr. Bou Tharin added that in accordance with the Law on Accounting and Auditing and the three essential obligations established for enterprises and non-profit organizations, namely:
* 1: Obligations to maintain accounting records * 2: Obligations to prepare financial statements in accordance with applicable standards and * 3: Submission of financial statements for independent audit in accordance with the prescribed conditions.
In accordance with the Law on Accounting and Auditing, three basic obligations have been established for enterprises and non-profit organizations, namely: the obligation to maintain accounting records, the obligation to prepare financial statements in accordance with applicable standards, and the obligation to submit financial statements. Perform an independent audit in accordance with the conditions.
The Director General delivered three important messages to the forum, including:
2. Adhering to a "proper accounting culture will help brighten the tax culture."
3: "Proper accounting, preparation of financial statements in accordance with applicable standards and submission of financial statements to the independent audit in accordance with the conditions will provide benefits for enterprises and non-profit organizations and contribute. "It also promotes non-fiscal revenue growth."
Butharin also stressed that sanctions or fines for enterprises and nonprofits are not the primary intentions of accounting and auditing regulators. The purpose of the regulator is to ensure that enterprises and non-profit organizations adhere to a "accounting culture".
