Ung Foundation Design Provides Nearly $ 200,000 Washing Machine and Medical Equipment to Kampong Chhnang Provincial Referral Hospital
(Kampong Chhnang): The "Ing Foundation" Foundation provides medical equipment, including washing machines, for nearly $ 200,000 to improve the provision of health services at Kampong Chhnang Provincial Referral Hospital.
The medical equipment equipped at Kampong Chhnang Provincial Referral Hospital includes: 2 washing machines with the latest technology made in Germany, 1 ultrasound machine made in the United States with high capacity for pregnancy ultrasound. And heart, 1 water purifier and repairing the washing machine, equipped with oxygen system, air conditioner, electric network and UV disinfection machine, totaling nearly 200,000 USD.
Oknha Ing Bunhou, President of the Eng Foundation Design, stated that the provision of medical equipment as described above, seeing that these facilities are necessary to use to save the lives of people in Kampong Chhnang and adjoining provinces. Diabetes and need dialysis.
Oknha Ing Bunhou said that in the past, people in Kampong Chhnang province who needed to wash their blood had to go to Phnom Penh, which took a long time and a lot of money. On the other hand, at this referral hospital, there is also a doctor who specializes in dialysis in the hospital, who he studied from abroad.
The President of the "Foundation" praised the team of doctors who care about the well-being of the people, strive to treat patients with quality and ethics. In particular, he encouraged doctors to continue to provide dialysis services to people in neighboring provinces, including Kampong Thom, Pursat and Kampong Speu. Those provinces do not have washing machines yet.
Duke Ing Bunhou emphasized that he would continue to support these facilities in case of increased demand.
The Director of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Health Department, Dr. Prak Von, expressed his congratulations on the new achievement, the new building, the new equipment of the dialysis service recently received from the Ing Foundation Design to treat and rescue the most needy patients.
Kampong Chhnang Provincial Referral Hospital receives more than 3,300 patients per month. Of those, 700 to 800 are diabetics.
Duke Ing Bun Hou and his family are generous people who always help Kampong Chhnang Provincial Referral Hospital. Duke Ing Bunhou and his family first helped build the hospital in 1998, when the hospital was in dire straits and continued to build another maternity ward in 2001.
The director of the department emphasized that this donation is important for the health sector in Kampong Chhnang province, which is not yet available, and it is very proud that Kampong Chhnang province is able to provide dialysis services.
During the ceremony, Mr. Yin Saven, Deputy Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, conveyed the heartfelt congratulations from the Provincial Governor to Duke Ing Bunhou, President of the "Ing Foundation Design" Foundation and his caring family. Sectors in Kampong Chhnang and other provinces. Especially in the fields of health, education, culture, environment, religion and helping people in need.
