Philippines allows US to use more military bases (Video inside) (Manila): The Philippines has decided to allow the United States to use more military bases on the occasion of the US Secretary of Defense. Complete the visit. This was released by the AFP news agency on Thursday, February 2, 2023.
The Philippine-US defense minister said in a statement that Washington would receive permits to use four more bases under the Military Cooperation Agreement (EDCA), which was established in 2014. The United States has previously invested more than $ 82 billion in five existing infrastructure under the EDCA, according to the statement.
The EDCA defense agreement allows the United States to use Philippine military bases for joint training, stockpiling, as well as the construction of infrastructure, including airports, fuel depots and military bases, but does not. Can maintain a permanent military presence.
On Thursday, US Secretary of Defense Lloyd Austin met with Philippine President Ferdinand Marcos Juna and Secretary of Defense Galito Galvez. Austin's three-day visit comes after US Vice President Kamala Harris visited the Asean archipelago in November 2022.
