The following is the circular: People from other provinces go to work to cut cassava tubers in Pailin province to reduce migration to Thailand
(Pailin): People from various provinces went to work to cut cassava tubers in Pich Kiri village, Sangkat Pailin, Pailin province to get money to support their daily lives while the boss bought cassava tubers from the plantations to plant. Let them cut the stalks, put them to dry, and then collect them for sale at a higher price than fresh cassava tubers.
According to the description of a woman living in Pich Kiri village, Pailin commune, Pailin city, on February 1, 2023, after taking a break from working in the fields in their respective hometowns, they traveled to Pailin province to camp for a living. Cutting cassava tubers for the boss in Pailin province to support the daily life.
Others work during the day and stay up late at night to turn on the lights until late at night, earning more money because they do not want to migrate to work for others. In Thailand, it is difficult to travel in and out of the country, you have to pay for a passport.
Some have been working to cut the cassava tubers for two to three months, while others have set up tents on land leased by their landlords to cut cassava tubers until the rainy season next month. Then they rested and returned to their homeland to work in the fields.
Please note that the market price of cassava tubers is now very high, with traders buying 1 kg for 3.3 baht (Thai currency) or more than 300 riel. After cutting and drying dried chewing gum, the price ranges from 7.5 to 7.8 baht or more than 700 riel, which is considered to be higher than in previous years. Dr. Yok Sambath chaired a health technical working group meeting with partner organizations and relevant institutions
