Surani received an average of 99,891, which is one of the highest average grades among A-20 students in 2022. On February 2, 2023, Surani and her mother also had a rare opportunity to participate in a face-to-face meeting with Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the Chroy Changvar Convention and Exhibition Center.
Surani and her mother had never met Samdech Techo Hun Sen in person before. The opportunity to meet the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia now is the happiest and happiest for the young women on the border, Surany and her mother.
Surany stated, "I feel really happy and excited to have the rare opportunity to participate in a get-together." In particular, met directly with Samdech Techo Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Going bankrupt with A score is a happy story, but Surany's study life as well as other failed students has not come to an end. They will have to go a long way to achieve their goals and objectives.
After passing the exam, despite getting an A, Surani did not apply for a scholarship at any school and even dropped out of the Food Chemistry Scholarship from the University of Battambang. Now Surany is trying to study more to prepare for the entrance exam to the University of Health.
Medicine is a subject that requires a long study period and the tuition fee is high. Surani wants to study for a doctorate, which takes about eight years and costs about $ 1,650 a year.
Surani also stated that according to the conditions of the University of Health, he could not get the scholarship, even though he could pass the exam. Not receiving a scholarship because Surani has already been offered a scholarship by another university.
As a child farmer from a rural area, tuition fees and expenses for medical education are becoming an obstacle and a concern for Surani, fearing that her parents will not be able to sustain her education to the end.
Surany's parents are farmers in Buor commune and now have three children in their care. Hen Pho, the mother of Surani, told Fresh News that as a farmer, the income is erratic, some years it is profitable, some years it is a loss. Therefore, she is also concerned about supporting her daughter's education to the fullest extent possible.
Despite her lack of ability to support her daughter's education, Hen Po did not dare to complain to her daughter for fear of discouraging her daughter.
In order to fulfill her daughter's desire to become a doctor, Ms. Hen Po respectfully asked Samdech Techo Hun Sen to provide scholarships for her daughter.
Ms. Sorani also respectfully asked Samdech Techo Prime Minister to provide a scholarship for her to achieve her goal of becoming a doctor.
