The Reserve Bank of Australia has decided to replace the portrait of former British Queen Elizabeth II on a $ 5 bill with a new design that will honor Australian culture. The decision not to choose a statue of King Charles III, the son of Queen Elizabeth and the current King of Britain, will replace all Australian banknotes with the King of Britain.
According to the Reserve Bank of Australia, the new $ 5 note could take years to design and print, and the $ 5 note featuring Queen Elizabeth will continue to circulate even when the design New ones are starting to be used.
It should be noted that Princess Elizabeth II passed away on September 8, 2022 at the age of 96. The decision by the Reserve Bank of Australia is backed by the government of Australian Prime Minister Anthony Albania, who supports Australia becoming a future republic. Today, Australia is among more than a dozen countries, including Canada and New Zealand, which still recognize the British monarch as its head of state.
Chongkal District Authority in Oddar Meanchey Province Starts Planting Luxury Trees and Mixed Flowers on National Road 68 After Death by Animals and Fire
(Oddar Meanchey): The authorities of Chong Kal district, Oddar Meanchey province, have started planting luxury trees and mixed flowers on both sides of National Road 68 from the border of Srey Snom district, Siem Reap province to the border of Samrong city, Oddar Meanchey province in the area of Chong Kal district. The flowers at some point were eaten by animals and subsequently burned.
Rithy Pak, Governor of Chong Kal District, Oddar Meanchey Province, told Fresh News on the morning of January 2, 2023 that in order to enhance the beauty of National Road 68 in Chong Kal District, the authorities have planted luxury trees. Thnong and mixed flowers include: sakura, diatom, peacock, bong mongkol, cactus, a total of about 4,500 plants from the border of Srey Snom district, Siem Reap province to the border of Samrong city, Oddar Meanchey province.
The district governor further stated that the luxury trees and mixed flowers planted on both sides of National Road 68 in Chongkal district cost about 100 million riels, including maintenance costs, which came from GIZ and some donors. Both the leadership of the Provincial Department of Agriculture, the Department of Water Resources, the Department of Rural Development, and the participation of village, commune, people's protection and people.
He said some of the trees and flowers planted on both sides of the road were eaten by animals and some were set on fire. Animals, grilling ... etc.
