Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police Continues to Tighten Road Traffic Law on National Road 4 to Reduce Traffic Accidents
(Preah Sihanouk): The Land Traffic Police Office, in cooperation with the Anti-Drug Bureau of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police, on February 2, 2023, enforced the law on road traffic by controlling alcohol. , Check the technical characteristics of the vehicle, speed and check for drugs on the driver.
The enforcement of the law on road traffic was carried out under the direction of Major General Chuon Narin, Sihanoukville Provincial Police Commissioner. This practice was carried out at km 220 in Village 1, Sangkat 1, Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province to reduce traffic accidents that may occur due to the above factors.
Lt. Gen. Chuon Narin has stated that this campaign is to increase respect for road traffic laws on all types of motorists so that they obey the law, especially for their own lives and the lives of commuters. Roads.
He added that this is a strict observance of the road traffic law, and from today, the police force of Sihanoukville Provincial Police will act like rain to make all drivers obey the traffic law. Land to be highly efficient.
