10 Vulnerable Families in Phnom Proek Commune Receive Donations from CRC Sub-Branch Phnom Proek District, Battambang Province
(Battambang): On February 1, 2023, Mr. Song Sopheak, Chairman of the CRC Sub-Branch Committee of Phnom Proek District and his colleagues visited and brought humanitarian donations to 10 vulnerable families in O Thom village, Phnom Proek commune. Phnom Proek district, Battambang province.
On that occasion, Mr. Song Sopheak addressed a message from Mr. Sok Lou, Chairman of the Provincial Branch Committee, especially from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, who always thinks about the well-being of the people in need. In line with the slogans "Where there is suffering, there is the Cambodian Red Cross" and "The Cambodian Red Cross is everywhere for everyone - leaving no one behind."
In addition, the district sub-branch president also reminded people to drink boiled water, live hygienically, rest in mosquito nets and improve daily food safety by growing vegetables in the family to be healthy and reduce Household expenses as well.
Please note that the gift given to each family received: 25 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 1 portable fish sauce.
Svay Rieng Doctors Successfully Donate Blood to Pregnant Woman After Severe Bleeding
(Svay Rieng): A pregnant woman with severe bleeding was sent to Svay Rieng Provincial Hospital for anemia and the doctor decided to donate blood for successful emergency surgery.
Doctors of Svay Rieng Provincial Hospital said on the afternoon of February 1, 2023 that the team of obstetricians and gynecologists of Svay Rieng Provincial Hospital operated to save a pregnant woman who was sent. From Romeas Hek District Referral Hospital with severe bleeding condition on January 31, 2023.
The source said that the woman who came for the operation was named Seng Sothea, 41 years old, living in Lobeuk village, Sambath Meanchey commune, Romeas Hek district, Svay Rieng province, because she needed a lot of blood (10 bags) to save and did not have a family to donate blood. The doctor of Svay Rieng Provincial Hospital also donated extra blood to save the pregnant woman until she survived the accident.
Doctors confirmed that after the operation, the woman's health was normal and did not change significantly.
The Svay Rieng Provincial Medical Team would like to call on the people as well as government officials around the province to continue to donate more blood to the Svay Rieng Provincial Hospital so that the medical team can be able to help the vulnerable people who need blood. Also. Cambodia to host 11th Asia-Pacific Forum on 3R and Chakra Economy for 3 days in Siem Reap
