Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government continues to support and promote the reform of the Baccalaureate exam, which makes it a good national movement to inspire this learning effort. Samdech stressed that this movement will not be allowed to go backwards.
2014 is the year of the bankruptcy exam, which does not allow any candidate to take copies of documents, electronic devices or be able to peek at each other. 2014 is also an unforgettable year for both students and the public, as it is the year when students fail the most and have up to two exams.
However, starting from 2014, the general knowledge students began to change their attitudes and start to wake up and study hard, without relying on plagiarism or plagiarism during exams.
