Key remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of meeting with A-level students
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Thursday, February 2, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, met with more than 1,000 A-level students in the 2021-2022 academic year. The meeting took place at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center.
On the occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen had a talk with A-level students for more than 2 hours, the following are the main messages of Samdech Techo:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen joins in the congratulations with all A-level students.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen would like to ask for your understanding on the postponement of the exam because of the ASEAN Summit and related meetings.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen, please understand from teachers and students for the delay of the meeting because waiting for the production of iPad from the factory.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his satisfaction with the reform of the Baccalaureate exam because it changed the attitude on learning and the exam.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the reform of the bankruptcy exam for nearly 10 years has ended the culture of intervention.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that bankruptcy reform has become a competitive movement of education and learning in each province.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the reform of the bankruptcy exam will continue forever.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the A-level students have created opportunities and built honor for their families with pride.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the parents, authorities, teachers for supporting the students' education.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that peace cannot be overlooked, there is peace only when there is an opportunity for education as it is now.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the flames of war have made the youth of the past lose the opportunity to study.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech spent about $ 400 million to build a school when he traveled to the provinces in 2016.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that traffic accidents are a new obstacle for students.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed concern over the bankruptcy rate of male students, which is lower than female students.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructs A-level students to continue their efforts to learn more.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen assigned the Capital Governor to arrange accommodation for poor students from the provinces.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the past there was an imbalance between demand and lack of schools, lack of teachers. But now the imbalance is reduced, more and more schools are closer to people's homes.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the next few days, Samdech Techo will announce the policy of public financial reform.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen advises to pay attention to vocational training. Samdech Techo confirmed that vocational training may begin after the formation of the new government.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen invites Cambodians abroad to visit the district to avoid fraudulent propaganda.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces that the Pope will not drag the opposition supporters who once insulted Samdech.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on Cambodians abroad to stop cheating the opposition's propaganda.
