Food reserves and rice seeds of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit continue to be distributed to 219 families affected by the dry season floods in Bakan district
(Pursat): Mr. Khoy Rida, Governor of Pursat Province and Chairman of the Provincial Disaster Management Committee, this morning, February 1, 2023, at the party headquarters of Svay Daun Keo commune, brought donations of food and rice from the Royal Government of Cambodia. The Cambodian Food Reserve System Committee to distribute to 219 families affected by the dry season floods from Otapong, Svay Daun Keo and Romlech communes, Bakan district, Pursat province.
On that occasion, Mr. Khoy Rida brought a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, which both Samdech always remember and care about. The well-being of the people in all circumstances: "Where there are people suffering, there is the face of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit."
The provincial governor further reminded the people to take care of their health by eating clean, drinking clean, living clean and hygienic. Once we get the rice seeds, we must work hard to grow and rehabilitate, on the other hand, we must support the policy of the Royal Government, which brings peace, peace and continuous development for all.
Taking that opportunity, he also announced to provide 3 telephone numbers to the people to easily understand, coordinate and intervene in a timely manner in case of any need that arises locally.
(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Oknha Tea Vichet, Chairman of the Local Party Committee of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Shipping Agency, sent a GTVC ambulance to receive a patient living in Koh Rong City with severe abdominal pain for a long time. Three days to come to the hospital in Sihanoukville to rescue when received immediately upon February 1, 2023 at 12:50 p.m.
In that, Mr. Oknha Tea Vichet learned that the patient was Sam Su, a 74-year-old female living in Koh Touch Village, Koh Rong Sangkat, Samloem Island, Koh Rong City, Sihanoukville Province.
On this occasion, the representative of the patient's family thanked the tycoon for his generosity in rescuing his family by sending an ambulance and a GTVC ambulance to take the patient to the hospital. Doctors in Sihanoukville.
It should be noted that Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, has also praised the generosity of Mr. Oknha, who always cares for the people who have suffered or encountered various incidents at sea. Sihanoukville.
Authorities crack down on fishing offenses and confiscate many illegal fishing gear in Kratie City
On February 1, 2023, officials from Kratie Fisheries Administration District and Kampi Fisheries Administration Division, in cooperation with Rokar Kandal Sangkat Council, Rokar Kandal Administration Police Force and Rokar Kandal Fisheries Community, inspected and cracked down on fisheries crimes. At Boeung Romleach point, Roka Kandal commune, Kratie city, some illegal fishing gear was confiscated.
Mr. Mok Ponlok, Director of Kratie Fisheries Administration District, stated that in the operation to crack down, the joint forces confiscated exhibits including: 100 snare drums (mouse snare) with a length of 2,750 meters, 144 bamboo poles. All exhibits are kept at the Kratie Fisheries Administration to wait for the decision from the management.
He added that according to the directive of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries No. 027 dated January 22, 2019 on measures to prevent and suppress fisheries crimes by using fishing gear to swallow the tail of a mouse or swallow a pig's gut or 100 deer.
Recently, the Ministry has found that fishing activities using fishing gear to swallow rat tails or swallow pig intestines or eel 100 have been occurring in the fishing area, which is worrying because the fishing gear has just been Create new fishing methods and fishing gear that are not mentioned in the Prakas of the Ministry.
In the past, the prevention and suppression of crime by using fishing gear to swallow the tail of a mouse or swallow a pig's intestine or swallow 100 deer by the fishery authorities has not been effective yet.
Therefore, in order to prevent and suppress the above fisheries crimes effectively and ensure the sustainability of fishery resources, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries would like to advise the authorities at all levels to take strict action as follows:
At this stage, the fisheries authorities at all levels must inspire the movement to collect fishing gear, swallow rat tails or pig intestines or swallow 100 deer to be destroyed in public places and inspire people and fishermen to fish with parallel fishing gear. The law.
2. Measures for the implementation of the Fisheries Administration Law at all levels shall cooperate with the sub-national administration and the relevant authorities under the coordinated leadership of the Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Unity Command to prevent and suppress fishing offenses using traps. Mice or swallows pig intestines or swallows 100 deer.
