(Phnom Penh): Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, received a working meeting with Mr. Joseph Scheuer, Country Coordinator of the United Nations in Cambodia at the Ministry on February 1, 2023. The meeting was also attended by representatives of the World Health Organization, UNICEF and the International Organization for Migration.
In particular, the Country Coordinator thanked the Royal Government of Cambodia for providing Kovid-19 vaccine to the staff of the United Nations Agency for International Development in Cambodia and all their family members for free.
In addition, the Country Coordinator thanked the Ministry of Health for its continued support and close cooperation with UN agencies such as the World Health Organization, UNICEF, and the International Organization for Migration (IOM). Their mission was successful.
The Minister of Health expressed his deep gratitude to the United Nations, especially the World Health Organization and UNICEF, for their continued financial and technical support to the Cambodian health sector, which underscored the agency's high commitment. The United Nations to the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia, especially in the context of Cambodia's efforts to promote measures to prevent and respond to the Kovid-19 epidemic.
At the same time, the Minister also spoke in support of the above-mentioned cooperation framework for the 2024-2028 cooperation.
Diplomat: Cambodia will continue to pursue an independent and rule of law foreign policy that protects core interests, guarantees sovereignty and peace, and promotes economic ties
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, said on February 1, 2023 that Cambodia will continue to pursue an independent and law-based foreign policy that protects core interests, guarantees sovereignty and peace, and promotes relations. Economy.
He made the remarks while addressing the National Assembly's Committee on Foreign Affairs, International Cooperation, Propaganda and Information on "Cambodia's Foreign Policy in the New Context of World Order" at the National Assembly.
"In the last five years, the world has continued to evolve into an international system that is global, multi-polar and complex," he said. "This development has brought about rapid, difficult, unpredictable and dangerous changes in international relations."
In the international and regional context, the Deputy Prime Minister briefed on developments such as competition between major powers, the formation of alliances and numerous initiatives on economic security and development across the region. 19 The war in Ukraine, the crisis in Myanmar and tensions on the Korean Peninsula.
In the domestic context, the presentation also highlighted the successful management of Cambodia's Kovid-19 epidemic, the achievement of the great achievements of the ASEAN Chairmanship in 2022, the active and honest efforts in The role of chair of ASEAN and special envoy to resolve the complex and deep-rooted crisis in Myanmar, as well as international recognition of Cambodia's independent and rule of law foreign policy.
