(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, will lead a delegation to the 32nd ASEAN Coordinating Council (ACC) Meeting and the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting to be held on the 3rd. February 4, 2023 in Jakarta, Indonesia.
A statement from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, obtained by Fresh News on February 1, said that the 32nd ACC meeting will focus on continuing to monitor the "ASEAN Leaders' Statement on Membership". ASEAN of East Timor "and" Declaration on Green Economy ". The ASEAN Foreign Ministers will also discuss priorities in 2023.
Indonesia will lead the ASEAN process this year under the theme "ASEAN is important: the center of growth" to ensure that ASEAN becomes a point of cooperation that contributes to peace, stability and prosperity of the region and the world.
On the occasion of the meeting, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon expects to have separate dialogues with his counterparts from some ASEAN countries as well.
