Following is the decision: Cambodian National Council for Children holds a four-day meeting on "Protecting Children from Online Exploitation and Abuse"
(Kep): Mr. Kim Sovandy, General Secretary of the National Council of Cambodia for Children, presided over the opening ceremony of the 4-day Consultative Meeting on Training Documents on the Protection of Children from Exploitation and Abuse Online. From January 30 to February 2, 2023 at Sangkhamit Hotel, Kep Province.
He said that the purpose of this meeting is to gather input and make the content of the training package for the protection of children from online exploitation and abuse better and easier to understand.
He said that after the meeting, the draft lessons for the training will be piloted with social workers, parents and caregivers, as well as children and youth in three provinces, including Battambang, Prey Veng and Kratie.
Mr. Kim Sovandy added that in the 5th mandate of the National Assembly, examining the technological progress, especially the development of the digital industry has had many positive and negative effects on society, the General Secretariat of the National Council for Children for Cambodia. A study of the effects of these technologies on children found that children are more vulnerable to online sexual exploitation and abuse.
The General Secretariat of the National Council for Cambodia for Children has also established an inter-ministerial technical working group to review and advise on the study of child sexual exploitation online in Cambodia (OCSE TWG) through Resolution 203 NCC. December 25, 2019.
The Inter-Ministerial Technical Working Group (OCSE TWG) analyzed the initial situation of child sexual exploitation online in Cambodia (OCSE). The report of the situation analysis was approved by HE Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and Chairman of the Cambodian National Council for Children on January 10, 2020.
