Nearly 600 CMAC deminers start operations in 5 provinces in Cambodia Mine Action Fund 2025
(Siem Reap): Mr. Heng Ratana, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Cambodian Mine Action Center (CMAC), on February 1, 2023, met with officials and operational forces in the Cambodia Mine Action Fund 2025 and announced Launch mine clearance operation in Cambodia Mine Action Fund Project 2025.
The ceremony was held at the Peace Mine Action Museum in Siem Reap on the morning of February 1, 2023.
The demining operation of the Cambodia Mine Action Fund 2025 will be implemented in Kampong Thom, Pailin, Preah Vihear, Pursat and Siem Reap provinces with a plan to clear 10,600 hectares.
Mr. Heng Ratana stated that the operation involved the specialized forces of nearly 600 CMAC units, including 13 dogs, 21 mine squadrons, a machine platoon and 36 mine research and clearance teams.
Mr. Heng Ratana would like to express his deepest gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, for establishing the Cambodia Mine Action Fund 2025 and approving the budget for CMAC to clear mines affected by Mines to ensure that Cambodia achieves its goal of demining by 2025.
Mr. Heng Ratana said that the goal of Cambodia after the mines by 2025 is to turn this land of Sovannaphum and get rid of mines and remnants of war. He would like to thank the leadership of the Mine Authority for facilitating and supporting the operation of CMAC.
Oddar Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner Holds a Training Course on the Roles and Duties of Administrative Police Stations in Implementing Safe Villages and Communes Policy
(Oddar Meanchey): Oddar Meanchey Provincial Police Commission this morning, February 1, 2023, opened a training course on the skills, roles and responsibilities of the administrative police station in implementing the policy of safe villages, communes and community police.
The ceremony was held in the presence of Lt. Gen. Meas Lim Tong, Director of the Police Post Affairs Department, on behalf of Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Doeun, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police, and was attended by Lt. Gen. Huot Sothy, Oddar Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner, as well as relevant officials and officials. Police from many other districts.
