Ministry of Economy and Finance Maintains Knowledge on New Procedures for FMIS Current Budget to Civil Servants
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance participated in the mainstay of knowledge on "mainstreaming of new procedures for the full disbursement of current budget through FMIS" to the leaders and civil servants of the five ministries and institutions to prepare for the implementation of the law. The new way at the end of the first quarter of 2023.
The event was attended by Dr. Hean Sahip, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the FMIS Project Management Team, as well as the leadership of the Ministry, Finance and Budget Unit. Authorized delegates at the central level of five ministries.
The five ministries are: 1: Council for the Development of Cambodia, 2: National Audit Authority, 3: Ministry of Cult and Religion: 4: Ministry of Mines and Energy, 5: Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications.
He said that in the era of the Industrial Revolution, 4.0 countries around the world are beginning to develop more advanced technologies and digital technologies as a priority for their socio-economic development and are expanding the potential of this technology. To be increasingly useful to serve all sectors, both private and public.
