(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Public Financial Management Reform Steering Committee, stated that the Public Financial Management Reform Program is one of the core reform programs of the program. Key reforms of the Royal Government of Cambodia to strengthen governance.
This statement was made on the occasion of Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth attending the launching ceremony of the grant financing agreement dated 8 December 2022 between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the European Union to support management reform. Public Finance, Phase 4, this morning, February 1, 2023.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth said that the Public Financial Management Reform Program has an ambitious and realistic vision, namely to build the Cambodian public financial system in line with international standards and excellence, with the goal of changing the system that focuses on inputs. And centralized towards a system that focuses on output or output and decentralization.
He said that the brilliant achievements of public financial management reform from the first phase until now have allowed the Royal Government to save and allocate more funds to priority sectors, as well as greatly increase public investment resources in Districts, especially on the development of physical infrastructure, which in turn contributes to Cambodia's financial independence.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth emphasized that during the past three years of the Kovid-19 crisis, the Royal Government has sufficient funds to support the implementation of policies and interventions aimed at stabilizing the lives of the people, as well as Stabilize the private sector business, which has been adversely affected by the Kovid-19 crisis.
At the same time, the Royal Government of Cambodia has been working to address macroeconomic challenges and risks, especially the effects of the war between Russia and Ukraine, which has pushed up inflation, such as rising prices. Fuel, food, fertilizers and almost all commodities, both through fiscal policy and other key policies. This was further confirmed by Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth said that in this sense, effective and efficient management of public finances is an essential foundation for promoting national development and improving the daily lives of the Cambodian people.
Taking this opportunity, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth would also like to inform that under the Public Financial Reform Program, the draft law on the (new) public financial system has been prepared by the working group of the Ministry of Economy and Finance. And through extensive consultation with partners and stakeholders and approved by the Plenary Meeting of the Council of Ministers on January 13, 2023.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth confirmed that he will lead a high-level delegation of the Ministry of Economy and Finance to meet with the Second Committee of the National Assembly to review and discuss the draft law. He hopes that by the second quarter of 2023, the law on the public financial system will be officially promulgated.
