Mr. Mam Bunheng Recognizes the Chairman of the Youth Working Group of the Ministry of Health
(Phnom Penh): Professor Mam Bunheng, Chairman of the Party Committee of the Ministry of Health, presided over the announcement of Mr. Sok Sam Ang as the Chairman of the Youth Working Group of the Ministry of Health.
The recognition ceremony was held on January 31, 2023, after Mr. Sok Sam Ang was appointed by the Standing Committee of the Central Committee to be a member of the Party Committee of the Ministry, a member of the CPP Central Youth Committee and Chairman of the Working Group. Youth of the Ministry of Health in early January 2023.
On that occasion, Mr. Sok Sam Ang thanked and committed 5 points to the leaders of the Standing Committee, Central Committee, Chairman of the Party Committee of the Ministry of Health and the Party Youth Working Group.
At the same time, Professor Mam Bunheng praised the achievements as well as the efforts of Mr. Sok Sam Ang and all party youth, who are the successors of bamboo and a strong successor to the future.
Professor Mam Bunheng said, "All our young people have the right to freedom and professionalism and have enough time to expand their careers, especially in the field of health." "The strength of Samdech Techo Prime Minister and President of the Cambodian People's Party and the Cambodian People's Party has made our country peaceful and politically stable."
He said that the Royal Government as well as the CPP have paid high attention to the health sector, especially the youth and women. In addition, according to the instructions of Samdech Techo is to focus on the health of the people. Therefore, the efforts of our medical team have saved people from the risk of death from various diseases, especially Kovid 19.
As a doctor, we must have only professionalism and virtue that will continuously improve the health sector, and must jointly expand our health services based on coverage, so that no one of our citizens does not know and receive services. Our health at all. In particular, to meet with the people, education, prevention of infectious diseases and hygiene, encouragement and provide medicine to them, etc., according to the Professor.
On that occasion, Prof. Mam Bunheng also encouraged all members to join together to continue the work, especially to meet with the people, as well as to make people aware of the general health that we must have obligations. Take care of their health.
The decision of Samdech Techo Prime Minister in response to the request of the Association of Higher Education Institutions in the courtesy meeting and discussion this morning, Wednesday, February 1, 2023.
The Association of Higher Education Institutions is a group of higher education institutions in Cambodia that is organized to work to improve the quality of education of students and strengthen the quality of teaching at all levels and institutional sustainability.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen considers private educational institutions to be an important partner of the Royal Government in promoting the education sector in Cambodia. For this reason, Samdech Techo Hun Sen always allows leaders and members of higher education institutions to meet and discuss education work once a year.
Dr. Heng Vanda, Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Association, told Fresh News that a total of 138 leaders and members met with Samdech Techo this morning from a total of 123 educational institutions in 40 higher education institutions and educational institutions. General number 83.
According to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo's personal assistant, during this morning's meeting, Samdech Techo Prime Minister praised the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports' measures to promote online education during the Cambodian epidemic. Kovid's disease 19.
Samdech Techo also thanked all higher education institutions for their active participation in human resource training. Especially at a time when Cambodia is facing a crisis of the Kovid 19 epidemic.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also thanked the Association of Higher Education Institutions for participating in various humanitarian activities. Samdech Techo considers those humanitarian activities as contributing to the growth of Cambodian society going forward.
According to Mr. Heng Vanda, in this meeting, Samdech Techo raised many issues related to education, especially to improve the quality of education even better.
The Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Association emphasized that in order to contribute to solving the difficulties of private educational institutions, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has decided not to collect taxes from private educational institutions for another 5 years, from 2024 to 2028.
On behalf of the leaders, members and members of the association, Mr. Heng Vanda expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Prime Minister for exempting taxes for another 5 years. According to Heng Vanda, the concession has been in place since 1996.
Heng Vanda, who is also the director of the Vanda Institute, emphasized that the preferential treatment is an important contribution to enable private educational institutions to strengthen themselves to be active and improve the quality of education. Samdech Techo Presides Over the Meditation Ceremony with Dr. Chrin Sothea
The awarding of the "Stall" to Dr. Chrin Sothea on the occasion of Samdech received a delegation of higher education institutions led by Mr. Heng Vanda, Chairman of the Board of Higher Education Association at the Peace Palace on the morning of February 1, 2023.
