Villagers in Bangkong village, Siem Reap province continue to keep the tradition of fishing together for cooking, preparing for the ascension or ascension ceremony
(Siem Reap): After finishing the rice harvest, the people in Bangkong village, Ampil commune, Prasat Bakong district, Siem Reap province, always hold a joint fishing ceremony in a conservation lake for the ascension or ascension ceremony. The villagers' tradition is to do it every year and never miss it.
Mr. Pich Khin continued that the tradition of catching fish together, the villagers have prepared equipment such as: fishing net. The joint fishing tradition begins at 7 a.m., with the committee announcing the microphone and shooting the arrow.
Mr. Pheak Heang Pheng, who paid for the net at the event, said that this was the first time for him to participate in a joint fishing ceremony of the villagers in Bangkong village because he had just come to live in this village. Just a year. He said that this joint fishing ceremony creates a happy atmosphere and closer solidarity between the people in the village.
Meanwhile, Yoeut Dara said that the tradition of catching fish together is very important for the people in Bangkong village to irrigate crops and be a conservation lake. After the villagers harvested the rice, the committee decided to choose the day to catch fish Together for the Ascension or Ascension Ceremony.
