More than 20,000 officials declare assets and liabilities for 2023
(Phnom Penh): The Anti-Corruption Unit (ACU) on January 31, 2023, yesterday closed the receipt of assets and liabilities under the two-year regime for 2023 by receiving more than 20,000 documents.
According to the announcement received by Fresh News, the Department of Assets and Liabilities has received a total of 22,645 copies of assets and liabilities. New Japanese Ambassador Vows to Strengthen Friendship and Cooperation with Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ou Ino Azuzi, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of Japan to Cambodia, has pledged to contribute to the strengthening of friendly relations and good cooperation with Cambodia.
This commitment was made on the occasion of his courtesy call with Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate of Cambodia on the morning of February 1, 2023 at the Senate Palace.
Ueno Atsushi has been appointed as the new Ambassador to Cambodia, replacing Mikami Masahiro, who is nearing the end of his mission after serving as the Japanese Ambassador to Cambodia for about three and four years. Months.
In addition, the President of the Senate, as well as the people of Cambodia, expressed their congratulations on the 70th anniversary of the establishment of official diplomatic relations between Cambodia and Japan and the upgrading of Cambodia-Japan diplomatic relations to a "comprehensive strategic partner". . Samdech wished the friendship and cooperation between the two countries and peoples to last.
Mr. Ou Ino Azuzi expressed his pleasure to be on a diplomatic mission in the Kingdom of Cambodia, a country with a long history and rich culture, with Angkor Wat as a World Heritage Site.
The Ambassador emphasized that the two countries, Japan and Cambodia, have built trusting relations and cooperation through the process of seeking peace and rebuilding the country. In 2023, the two countries will celebrate the 70th anniversary of diplomatic relations, raising the level of diplomatic relations between the two countries from a strategic partnership to a comprehensive strategic partnership.
The Ambassador praised Cambodia's progress in achieving peace, security and becoming a tourist destination around the world. He also congratulated Cambodia on its success in hosting the 40.41st ASEAN Summit and related meetings, as well as the 43rd ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly.
The Ambassador praised the good relations and cooperation between the two parliaments as an important factor for strengthening the relationship and cooperation between the two countries to reach the level of comprehensive strategic partnership. At the same time, the Senate of the two countries also has a bilateral friendship group.
In addition, the Ambassador emphasized that "through his diplomatic mission in the Kingdom of Cambodia, he will strive to contribute to the strengthening of good relations, friendship and good cooperation between the Parliament, the Government, the people and the two countries." More. ”
Cambodia and Japan established formal diplomatic relations on January 9, 1953, which are now 70 years old. The two countries have agreed to raise the level of relations to a comprehensive strategic partnership by 2023, making Japan the second country after China to have the highest level of relations with Cambodia.
The remarks by a senior official of the Ministry of Culture came after the National Museum used the word "Worm" in its writings, showing the results of the connection between the two hands of Jayavarman VII. The word was published by Fresh News and criticized by some people for being misspelled.
Under the influence of Hinduism, our Khmer Kingdom was exalted to the status of a semi-deity and a half-human, an incarnation representing the ruling deity on earth, known as the "Devaraja". Therefore, the naming of the son, the king, the high-ranking officials are all names related to the deity, and those names or names end with the Western song "... Varman". For example, Jayavarman, Indravarman, Yasovarman, Suryavarman.
In addition, Professor Hun Chhun Teng, a researcher and teacher of Khmer inscriptions, posted a video on social media explaining the words "Varman" and "Varman". In a lecture organized by the Buddhist Institute, he said that the use of the word for researchers is well known, but the general public is less aware.
For Hun Chhun Teng, researchers and calligraphers wanted the word "Varman" to be used, not the French word "Varman". Due to the fact that Cambodia was under French colonization for a long time, the use of the French language and the use of what is a French heritage, but when gaining independence, the Khmer wanted to turn away from French influence until the establishment of the Khmer Rouge Commission.
"According to this review, Cambodians should write the name of their king in the style of an inscription, which is an important historical document (not written under French influence)," he said.
(Phnom Penh): Khieu Samphan, the only surviving top Khmer Rouge leader, has been transferred to Kandal Provincial Prison to serve his life sentence.
The transfer process went through discussions and after receiving confirmation from the General Department of Prisons, as well as when the Co-Prosecutors visited Kandal Provincial Prison several times. The Co-Prosecutors also know that the International Committee of the Red Cross (ICRC) regularly inspects prisons across Cambodia, including the Kandal Provincial Prison.
Khieu Samphan was arrested on 19 November 2007 and detained under the jurisdiction of the Co-Investigating Judges on charges of involvement in crimes committed during the Khmer Rouge regime. After a full investigation, the Co-Investigating Judges decided to send him to trial. After examining the seriousness of the crimes committed and the age of the accused, the charges against Nuon Chea and Khieu Samphan were split into two separate trials.
The first trial in Case 002/01 began in November 2011 and ended in July 2013. The Trial Chamber issued a verdict in August 2014 convicting Nuon Chea and Khieu Samphan of crimes against humanity on charges of persecution, murder and other inhumane acts committed during When forcibly evacuated civilians from Phnom Penh and other towns.
Both defendants were sentenced to life in prison for their role in these crimes. The Supreme Court Chamber upheld the appeal of a life sentence in November 2016.
Both defendants were sentenced to life in prison in the second trial. On 22 September 2022, the Supreme Court Chamber upheld Khieu Samphan's sentence of life imprisonment. (Nuon Chea passed away in August 2019, leading to the termination of his proceedings).
