Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth provides important recommendations to the General Department of Taxation to strengthen tax collection more effectively.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, on January 31, 2023, chaired a meeting to review the results of tax collection for December and 2022 and the direction for Implementation of the General Department of Taxation for 2023.
On that occasion, General Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth provided a number of important recommendations to the General Department of Taxation to strengthen the work of collecting tax revenue more effectively.
He provided new perspectives on socio-economic as well as new developments in the global economy, geopolitical tensions and crises that could have a negative impact on the Cambodian economy. Some sectors may stagnate and continue to decline, but others can expect growth.
The Deputy Prime Minister supported the tax measures set by the General Department of Taxation as a direction for further implementation for 2023.
At the same time, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth advised the General Department of Taxation:
* Continue to review and clean up the draft tax law to be ready for submission to the Council of Ministers and for review and approval by the National Assembly in the near future.
* Continue to develop revenue collection policy for the Royal Government of the 7th legislature, with the General Department of Taxation and the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia as the core General Department in charge of revenue collection management.
Timely preparation of informal economic policies and implementation before the end of 2023 to develop and promote the informal economy to grow within the framework of a formal economic system.
* Continue to build physical infrastructure to support, including the construction of new tax branches and the search for locations in towns, towns and districts for the preparation of district-municipal tax offices to strengthen the provision of services to taxpayers and bring services closer to taxpayers. Such as considering the efficiency and comfort of the work of tax officials
* Take additional measures of the Royal Government that have just been introduced to continue to manage the impact and support the recovery of the tourism sector in the Kingdom of Cambodia in order to continue to reduce the impact on the socio-economic situation and continue to support and restore business. And business recovery
Strengthen the management of tax revenue collection in line with the targets set out in the Financial Law for 2023 to meet the needs of the Royal Government's expenditures and investments in order to implement various programs to meet the policy priorities of "People and Growth". »Including salary increases, social assistance programs, election planning and SEA Games events.
* Continue to implement and further improve the Information Technology Nursery (CamDx) registration to facilitate trade and business in Cambodia.
* The National Bank of Cambodia's Bakong payment system will be an important advantage for the General Department of Taxation in the payment management mechanism.
* Continue to further improve the modernization and capacity building of officials, which is an important factor in contributing to the promotion of tax compliance and the provision of services to taxpayers.
* Continue to promote and mainstream the tax culture by raising awareness, training and disseminating tax laws and regulations to taxpayers and the public to explain and address the difficulties and questions of the people.
* Continue to train and strengthen the capacity of officials in order to strengthen the capacity of tax service institutions to better serve through the reduction of tax evasion.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth highly appreciates and encourages the leaders and tax officials at all levels in the units under the General Department of Taxation who have been actively involved in the efforts to collect good results. Well, this is a success and a common achievement of the General Department of Taxation as a whole.
