7th River Festival in Kampong Thom focuses on education from tourism, culture, history, environment, sports
(Kampong Thom): The 7th River Festival, which is planned to be held in Kampong Thom province, focuses on education, tourism, culture, civilization, history, environment and people living in the rivers and streams in the region. From the SEA Games.
During the meeting of the Inter-Ministerial Commission for the 7th River Festival on the afternoon of January 31, 2023, Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, said that the 7th River Festival aims to promote and promote The potential for tourism in the provinces along the river, especially to encourage people in those provinces to actively participate in the development of riverside cities, community tourism development work.
He reminded that in Cambodia, there are many provinces with riverside cities and rich in potential for cultural tourism, agro-tourism, rural tourism, ecotourism, community-managed ecotourism.
"We want to highlight the culture, history, civilization, nature, people's lives and educate tourism operations, tourists, people, youth, students to understand all these points," he said.
Meanwhile, Mr. Tith Chantha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, also said that Kampong Thom had a history as the ancient capital of the Chenla period called "Isan Bora" and has left a large heritage site to the present, the Sambor Prei Kuk temple. Which has become a UNESCO World Heritage Site.
The Secretary of State continued that the tourist destinations in the area of Sambor Prei Kuk temple, as well as in Kampong Thom province, also connected with the tourist destinations in the Angkor resort area of Siem Reap province and the Preah Vihear temple area in Preah Vihear province. If tourists come from these two provinces, Kampong Thom is also a destination to connect to Phnom Penh.
Mr. Tith Chantha continued that before the festival and during the festival, there will also be educational and training workshops on improving the quality of tourism services, hygiene, cleanliness, cost-effective tourism services to business owners, tourism operations, students in the province. Also. In addition, there is education about the promotion of the environment, nature, culture, community, ecotourism.
Mr. Vath Chamroeun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism and Secretary General of the NOCC, said that the River Festival will also cover the May 2023 SEA Games and the contents of the road to the SEA Games to the people in Kampong Thom province. Well.
Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, together with the report on the preparation of infrastructure in the city and along the river, also urged people to participate in cleaning the environment in homes, villages, decoration of all public and private institutions, sports activities. Many have assigned the provincial Department of Education to co-organize sports teams to promote activities leading up to the upcoming SEA Games.
