Director General of Taxation sets out key measures to achieve $ 3,571 million in tax revenue by 2023
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kong Vibol, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Taxation, on January 31, 2023, strongly committed and made every effort to manage and collect tax revenue in accordance with The legal plan for finance for the year 2023 is 14,645.38 billion riels, equivalent to approximately 3,571.69 million dollars.
The statement was made at a meeting to review the results of tax collection for December and 2022 and the direction for further implementation for 2023 under the chairmanship of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance.
In order to achieve the 2023 tax revenue collection plan, Mr. Kong Vibol emphasized the need to continue to strengthen the implementation of fiscal measures and policies, including the following key measures:
* Continue to push for the completion of the review of the draft of the new fiscal law, which will ensure the coherence and updating of tax regulations.
* Continue to modernize the online tax filing management system (E-Filing) and information technology systems of the General Department of Taxation, adhering to the proactive spirit, making it easier to fulfill tax obligations, but difficult to avoid through Continuing to develop a number of input functions received from users from all walks of life to be more comprehensive and easy to use.
* Establish digital administration (E-Administration) and support infrastructure to enable fiscal administration to perform hierarchical tasks using digital formats, ensuring speed and efficiency in the performance of work.
* Continue to implement measures to collect and tighten tax debts in accordance with the procedures in force for enterprises that owe tax debts and do not come to pay or settle properly.
* Continue to cooperate to improve and promote the registration of enterprises in the Information Technology Nursery (CamDX) to be more efficient and comprehensive.
* Continue to strengthen and expand the scope of implementation of the mechanism for printing invoices on property tax and unused land tax and distributed to taxpayers' homes to all taxpayers.
* Continue to modernize information technology systems and applications with a proactive spirit through the development and updating of new systems and applications.
* Continue to invest and develop information technology systems and infrastructure to support and strengthen the capacity of data analysis functions to further promote fiscal compliance.
* Continue to implement the necessary measures as set out in the circular on the implementation of the Law on Finance for the year 2023 and continue to implement with attention to the revenue collection strategy 2019-2023.
In addition, Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, paid attention to the management of tax revenue collection, which always guides wisely and sharply plans for the implementation of key reforms and strategic measures in the future. In the past, it has promoted and promoted fiscal compliance and ensured fair competition among the investment environment.
On that occasion, Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth highly appreciated the efforts of all levels of leaders and tax officials to contribute to the task with all their strength and achieve the results of tax revenue management. Achieving the plan, despite the difficult situation, risks and uncertainties of the global economic and political situation.
