711 Search and Rescue Task Force Starts a Weekly Diving Training in Sihanoukville After Receiving Materials from Samdech Techo
(Preah Sihanouk): After receiving a material donation from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on January 31, 2023, the Search and Rescue Operation Unit 711 of the 70th Brigade organized a diving training. One week to strengthen the ability to rescue victims in the water while the training exercise was held at Prek Treng Beach, Village 3, Sangkat 1, Sihanoukville.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice-Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, emphasized that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister and Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, provided funds to provide relief equipment for surface rescue operations such as: : Lakes, rivers, streams and the sea.
Senior Minister Kun Kim expressed his deep gratitude for the consideration of the 17 search and rescue units in order to make the interventional operations more effective.
In addition, Senior Minister Kun Kim confirmed that the provision of such material assistance is in response to the needs as well as the situation encountered in the past during the rescue operation and search for victims who drowned in the accident.
Senior Minister Kun Kim said that Cambodia is affected almost every year by floods, droughts, strong winds, landslides and other disasters. The senior minister said, however, that the Royal Government has given priority to disaster management work, overcoming all obstacles, fighting on all fronts, mastering all aspects and under all circumstances.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Secretary General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC), affirmed that in order to maintain the resilience of the economy or the resilience of investment, it is necessary to train more skilled workers. .
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea said that in the future, investors who come to invest and set up factories in Cambodia will need skilled and knowledgeable workers, so it is very important that we strive to train skilled workers.
"We know that in the future, those factories and investments will need more and more skilled workers, so ministries and institutions must work hard," he said.
He said that investment and investment attraction, investment services are not the only role of the Council for the Development of Cambodia. The Council for the Development of Cambodia can only function without the support of the relevant ministries.
He said that in 2023, all ministries have action plans. Especially in 2023, Cambodia will have parliamentary elections. It is the Royal Government's intention to make Cambodia a high-middle-income country by 2030, because today Cambodia is a low-middle-income country, so there must be annual activities.
Recognizing the importance of vocational training needed to help the economy, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen recently unveiled a vocational and technical training program for young and vulnerable families. Fees and additions with allowances.
The implementation of this program may take place at the end of 2023 or early 2024, the human resources to receive this training is about 1.5 million people.
It should be noted that in 2022, the Royal Government of Cambodia has approved a total of 186 investment projects under the investment capital of 4,032 million US dollars and can create 144 thousand jobs. 186 investment projects, including 175 new projects and 11 production expansion projects.
Of these 186 investment projects, 163 are in the industrial sector, 9 in the agricultural and agro-industrial sector, 9 in the infrastructure and other sectors, and 5 in the tourism sector.
Six rice farming communities in Banteay Meanchey province sign agricultural contracts with exporters on 8,533 tons of rice on 1780 hectares
(Banteay Meanchey): Sick Nether Asia, a rice exporter this morning, January 31, 2023, signed an agricultural contract with 6 rice farming communities on 8,533 tons of rice on an area of 1,780 hectares. And has 187 members.
The ceremony was presided over by Dr. Yang Saing Koma, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Secretary of State for the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, representing Mr. Dith Tina, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries. The ceremony took place at the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Banteay Meanchey.
This agricultural contract is the result of a coordination between the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and the Cambodian Rice Federation.
This signing event is another new achievement for 2023 in Banteay Meanchey province and is very important for farmers, rice producers, mills and the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to continue to promote cooperation and construction of rice production chains. Rice.
On that occasion, Dr. advised to continue to cooperate in compiling and strengthening agricultural communities and preparing to compile production data.
Taking this opportunity, Dr. also recommended to the community to reduce the cost of rice production through the use of pure seeds, the use of natural fertilizers mixed with chemical fertilizers, soil preparation and water management.
It should also be noted that the rice production community also receives the supply of inputs from companies such as fertilizers, pesticides and rice seeds, with farmers purchasing and paying at harvest time.
