Kampong Chhnang Municipality Calls on Local Vendors to Cooperate to Organize Tidiness and Aesthetics
(Kampong Chhnang): The Kampong Chhnang Municipal Administration has issued a notice to vendors who live on the paved streets in Kampong Chhnang to cooperate with the municipal administration to maintain order, beauty, hygiene and environment in Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Chhnang. Each.
According to the above announcement, the Kampong Chhnang Municipal Administration informs all the residents who live on the paved streets in Kampong Chhnang City that the Municipal Administration must organize the beauty of Kampong Chhnang City to have order and a good environment as a beautiful city. And clean to participate in the upcoming clean city race.
Therefore, in order to make the city clean and beautiful, we would like to ask the people and traders to sell on the streets, paved with rubber, along the fences of various departments and units in Kampong Chhnang City, who have built a porch and put up signs or put up stalls or sell other goods on the corolla or land. These roads shall be cut and dismantled, leaving a 3-meter pedestrian gap from the date of this announcement until February 6, 2023.
He added that the municipal administration has already distributed the notice to the vendors and landlords who rented the location to the vendors at the above point and also copied it to the provincial administration and the provincial court.
This notice is given to them for one week, in case they do not comply with the above notice, the Kampong Chhnang Municipal Administration will issue a notice giving them another week on the last deadline. Still refuse to comply, the municipal administration will follow the administrative procedures.
Mr. Hing Phop Menea, Governor of Kampong Chhnang City, also confirmed to Fresh News that by following the instructions of the Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, the order, beauty and environment in Kampong Chhnang City must be well organized to compete for a clean city. In the coming days, the Kampong Chhnang Municipal Administration has started to implement the first step, starting from February 2023 onwards, in stages and sequentially.
On this occasion, the mayor also called on all business people in Kampong Chhnang to cooperate with the municipal administration to improve the beauty, order, hygiene and environment in our city.
The Municipal Administration would also like to ask for the understanding and tolerance of the people and traders in Kampong Chhnang City. That understanding.
Mr. Chea Chanto praised the active contribution of the United Nations in Cambodia to the development of the financial sector.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, highly appreciated the active contribution of the United Nations agency in Cambodia to the development of Cambodia's financial sector in the past.
The assessment of the Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia was made on the occasion of allowing Mr. Joseph Soyer, the new United Nations Resident Coordinator in Cambodia (UN) to pay a courtesy call and introduce himself, accompanied by the United Nations Agency for International Development (UNHCR). Cambodia on January 30, 2023.
Mr. Chea Chanto welcomed the second presence of Joseph Soyer in Cambodia after his role as Director of the United Nations Development Program (UNDP) in Cambodia from 2007-2010 and praised his contribution. The United Nations agency in Cambodia has been active in contributing to the development of Cambodia's financial sector in the past.
The Governor requested the United Nations in Cambodia to continue to prioritize work in the financial sector, especially to improve the financial environment, financial literacy and research.
Mr. Joseph Soyer mentioned the good cooperation between the National Bank of Cambodia and the United Nations in Cambodia in the past, in which the United Nations agency in Cambodia such as UNCDF has helped strengthen the work related to the survey on the financial environment. UNDP contributes to the study of securities, co-organizes macroeconomic conferences, and studies to promote the use of the riel in the garment industry and the microfinance sector.
UNESCAP, on the other hand, provides financial literacy training to Cambodians, especially women, and promotes financial literacy.
Mr. Joseph Soyer expressed his appreciation for the good cooperation that is taking place today and expressed his commitment to continue to contribute to the development of Cambodia even better.
In fact, in March 2023, the United Nations in Cambodia will organize an annual forum with the government to identify priority areas for better economic development in Cambodia.
