Cambodia transfers chairmanship of ASEAN Business Advisory Council to Indonesia
(Indonesia): Cambodia transferred the chairmanship of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council to Indonesia on January 30, 2023 yesterday.
Neak Oknha Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Chairman of the Business Advisory Council 2022, made an online speech transferring the chairmanship of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council from Cambodia to Indonesia to Arsjad Rasjid. Chairman of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council 2023.
The official handover ceremony was presided over by Dr. Zulkifli Hasan, Minister of Commerce of the Republic of Indonesia, and was attended by Mr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, Member of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council, Ten Business Councils. Mixed representatives of relevant institutions and many international guests.
Speaking on the occasion of the handover ceremony, Duke Kith Meng highlighted the significant achievements made during 2022 as the Chairman of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council in promoting and enhancing the role of the private sector to become a good partner. It is important to participate in building the ASEAN Economic Community, despite the challenging circumstances of global economic and geopolitical issues.
The Duke thanked all stakeholders for their support, which led to many successes and achievements during Cambodia's hosting of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council. In addition, the Duke requested the full support of the Chairman of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council 2023 for the common benefit of the private sector and wished the new Chairman success in leading the ASEAN Business Advisory Council.
