The DG-ECHO-funded Humanitarian and Community Health Promotion Program, funded by the Finnish Red Cross, runs for three years from April 2022 to May 2025 in four target provinces, including Kandal, Tbong Khmum, Banteay Meanchey and Bailin. Gradually implemented in 2022 after receiving the high approval of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross during April 2022.
The above program aims to prevent and respond to various epidemics in the community, manage the risk of disasters, climate change, promote institutional development, and promote community participation and accountability.
The Finnish Red Cross also supported the Cambodian Red Cross through the International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies (IFRC) and with direct cooperation from 1990 to 2020, and this cooperation was temporarily suspended due to budget constraints and Global Risk of Kovid 19 Disease. During direct cooperation with that partner on community health and disaster reduction.
