(Phnom Penh): Honorary General Hing Bun Heang said that because the country is peaceful, women have the opportunity to gain knowledge and human resources and have full rights to actively participate in socio-economic development.
Honorary General Hing Bun Heang, Deputy Director of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's Cabinet, said this on the occasion of joining the 112th Anniversary of International Women's Day on March 8 under the theme of Peace, Gender Equality and Conversation. Female military family of the bodyguard command on the afternoon of January 30, 2023.
"If our country is at war, there is political instability, there is no peace, we do not think about the development of villages, communes, communities, women, gender, women's rights, children's rights, human rights," he said. The key is to keep the peace and keep the peace, and women also have a role to play in maintaining peace, which is beneficial for themselves, their families and society.
He added that the United Nations commended Cambodia as a model country that sent blue hat women above the quota of 15% to 17% to participate in UN peacekeeping. Progress of Women in Education Gender gap between boys and girls in primary and secondary education is at its lowest point, gender gap is still small at the upper secondary level, and at the tertiary level, the gender gap is gradually narrowing.
Regarding women's health, Samdech Bun Rany Hun Sen has actively contributed to reducing maternal and infant mortality. Cambodia, one of the top 10 countries in the world, has achieved the 2015 Millennium Development Goals in the health sector to reduce maternal and infant mortality.
In the economic sector, compared to other countries in the region, Cambodia has a high participation rate of women in the economy with a high workforce of 80%. Small and medium enterprises have a population of nearly one million, of which 65% are women.
