The CPP adheres to the implementation of an independent foreign policy based on laws aimed at protecting the core interests of the nation, respecting the norms, objectives and principles of the UN Charter. And ASEAN
(Phnom Penh): The ruling Cambodian People's Party (CPP) has decided to adhere to the implementation of an independent foreign policy based on laws aimed at protecting the core interests of the nation, respecting the norms, objectives and principles of the UN Charter. And ASEAN.
This is according to the 11 decisions of the Extraordinary General Assembly of the National Representative of the Cambodian People's Party for 2 days on January 28-29, 2023, which was presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, Samdech Heng Samrin Honorary President of the Cambodian People's Party and 4 Vice Presidents.
At the same time, in an environment where the regional and international situation is evolving in a complex, uncertain and dangerous situation, the Cambodian People's Party also called on the states involved in conflicts to increase tolerance and strengthen cooperation. Let's work together to find a peaceful solution to ensure lasting peace and prosperity for humanity.
The Cambodian People's Party promotes the implementation of the strategy "Cambodia is mine-free by 2025 and minimizes unexploded ordnance"
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian People's Party (CPP) has promoted the implementation of the strategy "Cambodia is mine-free by 2025 and reduce unexploded ordnance to a maximum."
The commitment to implement this plan was made at the Extraordinary General Assembly of the Cambodian People's Party, which was held for two days at the 7 January Palace, Phnom Penh on 28-29 January 2023.
Implementing the "Cambodia Mine-Free by 2025 and Minimizing Unexploded Ordnance" strategy is one of the five strategies set by the Cambodian People's Party for the next five years to achieve great achievements. In all areas and continue to achieve the vision of Cambodia 2030 as a high middle income country.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Deputy Chief of the Mine Authority, said that with the support of the Samdech Techo Mine Action Project, the Cambodian Mine Action Fund 2025 and its development partner, the Mine Clearance Plan for 2023, covers an area of approximately 411 km. Square meters. Therefore, after 2023, Cambodia will have 18 capitals and provinces to declare mines.
Next, 7 provinces will be included in the demining plan by 2025, including: Koh Kong, Pursat, Battambang, Pailin, Banteay Meanchey, Oddar Meanchey and Preah Vihear. At the same time, the Mine Authority is confident in achieving the vision of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to complete the work of demining and declare Cambodia mine-free by 2025.
The Extraordinary General Assembly of the Cambodian People's Party fully supports Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Prime Minister candidate for the 7th term and Hun Manet as the future Prime Minister candidate.
(Phnom Penh): The Extraordinary General Assembly of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) fully supported Samdech Tey Techo Hun Sen as the Prime Ministerial candidate for the 7th legislature of the National Assembly and supported Dr. HUN Manet as the future Prime Ministerial candidate.
This joint show of support was made during the decision of the Extraordinary General Assembly of the Cambodian People's Party, which was held for two days on January 28-29, 2023 at the 7 Makara Palace in Phnom Penh.
The decision received by Fresh News stated that the General Assembly was held in accordance with the party's statutes and internal regulations in the spirit of high unity and issued the following decisions:
1: The General Assembly proceeded according to the agenda and achieved the following results:
A- Discuss and approve the report on the results of the implementation of the political program of the party from 2018 to 2022 and the direction of tasks for 2023.
B- Discuss and approve "Political program of the Cambodian People's Party for the construction and defense of the motherland 2023-2028"
C- Evaluate the performance of duties towards the 7th National Assembly election
Fully support Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen as the Prime Ministerial candidate for the 7th legislature of the National Assembly and support His Excellency Hun Manet as the Prime Ministerial candidate for the future. Closed days
(Phnom Penh): The two-day Extraordinary General Assembly of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) closed on the evening of January 29, 2023. With this closing ceremony, the Cambodian People's Party held a press conference and announced 11 decisions.
The two-day Extraordinary General Assembly of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) was held to review the results of the implementation of the party's political program from 2018-2023. And protect the motherland in 2023-2028 and so on.
Representatives attending the General Assembly include members of the Central Committee, party officials, members of the National Assembly, the Senate, the Royal Government, senior officials and representatives of party committees, ministries, institutions, capitals, provinces, municipalities, districts and Khans, as well as party organizations. A total of 3,558 people.
China announces resumption of general visas for Japanese citizens over dispute over Kovid 19
TOKYO: The Chinese Embassy in Tokyo announced on Sunday that Beijing has decided to renew the issuance of general visas for Japanese citizens traveling to China. This was released by the AFP news agency on Sunday, January 29, 2023.
During the previous suspension, the Chinese government issued visas to some Japanese travelers, but these were made under the exception of diplomats, government officials and business people with urgent duties. Beijing has also stopped issuing short-stay visas to South Korean travelers for reasons related to the 19-unit Kovid.
South Korea reports to North Korea immediately after its soldiers mistakenly fired machine guns at the border
SEOUL: A South Korean soldier accidentally fired a machine gun near the North Korean border, prompting a Seoul alert, local media reported on Sunday. Immediately to Pyongyang that the act was done unintentionally. This was released by the AFP news agency on Sunday, January 29, 2023.
Yonhap news agency, citing a South Korean military source, said four live ammunition was fired from a machine gun during a training exercise along the inter-Korean border in Gangwon province on Saturday night. While there were no plans to practice shooting live during the training.
However, all the bullets landed directly on South Korean soil and no damage was reported. The above happened unintentionally and North Korea did not seem to show any abnormal signs after the incident.
The two Koreas are, in fact, still at war after fighting ended through a 1953 ceasefire. The two countries are separated by a buffer zone called the DMZ, which is 4 km wide and runs across the Korean Peninsula for a total length of 250 km.
The last time the two sides exchanged fire in the border area was in May 2020, when four bullets flying from North Korea hit a South Korean guard post, prompting South Korea to fire. Reply back. In 2017, North Korea also fired on one of its own people who ran across the border to surrender to South Korea, but South Korea did not fire back.
Banteay Meanchey Province: This year, the yield is high, but the market sales are cheap
(Banteay Meanchey): At the same time, in the autumn, farmers in Banteay Meanchey province continue to struggle to grow all kinds of vegetables, such as vegetables, fruits and vegetables, yielding a remarkable yield, although some farmers have abandoned their farmland. Leave it because you can not stand the goods that are soaring.
According to the farmer living in Kang Va village, Pong Ror commune, Serey Sophorn city, Banteay Meanchey province, which has an area of 1 hectare near the Kang Va mountain area, said on January 29, 2023 that he and some other farmers Planted vegetables, fruits and vegetables last year, sold at a relatively high price, 1 kg can be sold to the market for two thousand to three thousand riels per kilogram.
He said that this year, the crop received a lot, but the market was cheap, with 1 kilo at eight hundred riel per kilogram can continue to go down, they continue to plant, and this year they did not give up. Do not leave this land vacant because now people and markets still need to eat vegetables.
Separately, Mr. Pang Vanna Set, Director of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Department of Agriculture, claimed that this season is the dry season, so his farmers grow a variety of vegetables. For Banteay Meanchey this year, the prices of some vegetables have dropped, such as squash. Sometimes farmers grow more, eat less, buy less, so the price goes down.
He said that some vegetables are sold at a higher price because consumers like to eat more, and now farmers are harvesting a large number of crops, and in the district that grows a lot of vegetables this season, such as in Phnom Kangva. Serey Sophorn City, Mongkul Borey District, Preah Net Preah District.
