The ruling party is committed to eradicating politics and extremist activities from Cambodian society, without allowing this trend to divide the nation.
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian People's Party (CPP) is committed to eradicating all forms of politics and extremist activities from Cambodian society, not to allow this trend to divide the nation, to strengthen national unity and ensure a peaceful living environment for the people.
Confirmation of the commitment of the Cambodian People's Party was made at the Extraordinary General Assembly of National Representatives for 2 days on January 28-29, 2023, chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party and Samdech Heng Samrin Honorary President of the Cambodian People's Party and 4 Vice Presidents.
The decision of the Extraordinary General Assembly of the Cambodian People's Party, which was received by Fresh News, stated that the General Assembly reaffirmed the CPP's commitment to maintaining peace, political stability and security in Cambodia. Under all circumstances, promote the strict observance and implementation of the law and resolutely oppose any hostile activities that undermine peace, democracy, the rule of law and development in Cambodia.
"In this spirit, it is necessary to get rid of all forms of politics and extremist activities from Cambodian society, not to let this trend cause national divisions, to strengthen national unity and ensure a peaceful living environment for the people." At the same time, continue to improve the implementation of the policy of safe villages, communes, sangkats in accordance with the direction set by the Royal Government. According to the announcement.
The General Assembly also reaffirmed its unwavering position in safeguarding the constitutional monarchy. At the same time, continue to strengthen liberal, multi-party democracy and promote respect for human rights in Cambodia, which is an important basis for strengthening peace, stability and promoting socio-economic development.
The Extraordinary General Assembly of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) has set five strategic goals to achieve great achievements in all fields and achieve the vision of Cambodia by 2030.
(Phnom Penh): The Extraordinary General Assembly of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) has set five strategic goals to achieve great achievements in all fields and achieve the vision of Cambodia 2030 as a middle-income country. High.
The five strategic goals include:
First, protect peace, protect independence, sovereignty, territorial integrity and protect all achievements of the society to be stable.
Second, to build the Kingdom of Cambodia into a liberal, multi-party democracy that is progressive and strong, based on the rule of law, has a sustainable and equitable economic growth, and the people have a prosperous life, live in harmony, with dignity and respect for human rights. .
Third, to build a social protection system that is environmentally efficient and financially sustainable, which ensures the provision of protection to the people in response to economic risks, public health risks and other vulnerabilities arising from changing working conditions. And living.
Fourth, to promote the implementation of "Cambodia is mine-free by 2025 and reduce the number of unexploded ordnance to a maximum."
Fifth, continue to pursue an independent foreign policy based on the law, build friendship and better cooperation between the Kingdom of Cambodia with all countries in the world and international organizations, and actively participate in the cause of peace, stability, security and prosperity in the region. And the world.
