As we all know, in addition to the local beliefs, customs and traditions of the Khmer people, we are also influenced by the early Indians, such as religion, language, script, etc., including the use of Pali, Sanskrit for religion, administration, literature, art, architecture. And so on.
Under the influence of Hinduism, our Khmer Kingdom was exalted to the status of a semi-deity and a half-human as an incarnation representing the ruling deity on earth, known as the "Devaraja". Therefore, the naming of the son, the king, the high-ranking officials are all names related to the deity, and those names or names end with the Western song "... Varman". For example, Jayavarman, Indravarman, Yasovarman, Suryavarman.
