(Kampong Speu): Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu Province, urged people to grow vegetables in addition to farming to supply the local market. He said that the cultivation efforts have provided benefits not only to meet the needs of the family, but it can be sold to the market to earn extra income to support the family more than withstand a part of the situation. Kovid 19 also spread.
The provincial governor made this urge when he led a team to inspect the vegetable cultivation of the Omlaing community in Thpong district, Kampong Speu province, on the afternoon of January 27, 2023.
The governor of Kampong Speu province said that the Royal Government as well as the Ministry of Agriculture, including the provincial administration, have encouraged farmers to expand animal husbandry, farming and other crops to supply special markets to earn more income.
He said, "Today, the Royal Government, as well as the Ministry of Agriculture, has made efforts to compile documents to train the farming community and also to provide experts to train at the local level, how to make your cultivation. "More, less costly and safer for consumers as well as growers. In general, farmers should reduce the use of chemical fertilizers."
Regarding the encouragement to cultivate, Mr. Suong Veng, President of Omlaing Vegetable Market Community, said that he and other community members have been growing safe vegetables for 3 years. The livelihood of the family and the education of the children are largely dependent on this cultivation.
He said that now the market for good vegetables can be grown by brokers, sometimes his community can not produce enough to fill the market, in which all vegetables produced other than local sales are A large number are to supply the market in Phnom Penh, especially in supermarkets.
(Preah Vihear): The new administrative building and meeting hall of Rovieng District Administration, Preah Vihear Province, a project of the Ministry of Interior, was officially inaugurated on the morning of January 27, 2023 to provide a place for people to work. Citizens of officials to be more convenient.
The ceremony was held in the presence of Mr. Ouk Kimsan, Deputy Governor of Preah Vihear Province and Chairman of the Provincial Working Group on Rovieng District, representing Mr. Kim Rithy, Provincial Governor, with the participation of Mr. Hor Bun Hour, Governor of Rovieng District, as well as district leaders and civil servants. Armed forces and many other citizens.
Mr. Ouk Kimsan said that the new administration building and meeting hall of the Rovieng district administration, which is currently being laid, is a project of the Ministry of Interior.
He said that under the leadership of the Royal Government, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, administrative buildings in the capital, provinces and districts throughout the country have been built to facilitate. Performing duties of officers.
Deputy Governor of Preah Vihear Province, as the Chairman of the Provincial Working Group to Assist Rovieng District, instructed the civil servants in Rovieng District to work harder to fulfill their duties and responsibilities, especially in providing public services to the people. As soon as possible, in accordance with the instructions of Mr. Kim Rithy, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, as well as the instructions of the Ministry of Interior and the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Please note that in this ceremony, there is also a sacrifice by arranging offerings, candles, incense and many other items according to the ancestral tradition to ask for happiness from the owner of the land to the group of craftsmen who have been building Administrative building and administrative hall of Rovieng district on this occasion.
