Ministries and Institutions Related to Cambodia's Coastal Areas Committed to Strengthening, Managing and Reducing Marine Waste
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism and relevant ministries and institutions, including the provincial authorities of the four coastal areas, organizations as well as tourism associations related to the coast of Cambodia, are committed to strengthening the management and reduction of marine waste (Marine Debris), especially plastic waste in the target. Coastal tourism.
Secretary of State Ny Phally stressed the need to manage marine debris (Marine Debris), especially plastic waste in coastal tourism destinations, requires the participation of all stakeholders to work together to maintain a clean beach. Good environment and good water quality to increase the attractiveness and warmth of national and international tourists and contribute to the promotion of social well-being.
The Secretary of State took the initiative to compile and establish a joint nursery between the network of ministries, institutions, local authorities, organizations, associations, communities and tourism associations in the coastal areas to increase the efficiency of the mission along the common goals. Manage and reduce marine waste.
The meeting agreed to strengthen cooperation in the implementation of data and technology exchange, and to jointly develop and implement the Inter-sectoral Integration Plan for Marine Debris Management and Reduction, especially to support the establishment of a joint forum to support Implement the above projects and plans.
