* Arrange the location properly to stop and make adjustments for vehicles that are not technically correct.
* Prepare means, tools, materials and letters for inspection operations.
* Perform practical inspections at each target to find vehicles with technical defects in order to take measures to correct vehicles with technical defects according to each specific crime case at the pre-arranged location.
* Make a record of confiscation of exhibits and impose fines in accordance with Sub-Decree No. 85 dated 08 July 2015 on Transitional Penalties for Offenses and the Law on Road Traffic and check the necessary documents according to the procedures.
* Instruct the owner of the vehicle that is not technically correct about the obligation to find a technician to correct the technical condition of his vehicle in accordance with the law, pay the service to correct this technical condition and be responsible for the management of goods or materials contained in Its vehicles.
* Within 3 days, if the owner of the vehicle that is technically wrong refuses to correct the technical condition as instructed by the authorities, the case shall be prepared and sent to the Provincial Prosecutor for legal action. In this case, the vehicle owner has to pay the parking location fee according to the storage fee set by the state.
