(Kandal): Mr. Kong Sophorn, Governor of Kandal Province, officially inaugurated the 1,000-meter-long, 7-meter-wide and 0.15-meter-thick concrete road in Chong Bongkol village, Thmey village, Monorom village, Prey Tonleab village and Borey Kamakor village in Bek Chan commune. Ang Snoul district on the afternoon of January 27, 2023 yesterday.
On that occasion, Mr. Kong Sophorn stated that this concrete road is a great new achievement with many other achievements of Bek Chan commune, Ang Snoul district in the field of socio-economic beauty, comfort, equity and consistent environment. According to the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategic Policy.
The provincial governor added that under the wise and skillful leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia has set people, water, roads, electricity as a priority to improve the comfort and living conditions of the people, that is, there are roads. Bridges have hope and development in all areas.
With the achievement of this new concrete road, the people living in Bek Chan commune expressed their deep gratitude to Mr. Kong Sophorn and Mr. Khon Serey Ratha, Governor of Ang Snoul District, for accepting the people's request to build a concrete road. 7 meters wide, 1 kilometer long.
The people expressed their happiness and gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen for leading the country to peace and prosperity, and also thanked the wise leadership of the Governor and Mr. The governor of Ang Snoul district, who has taken care of the well-being of the people.
During the ceremony, Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, extended a warm welcome to all business and investors who took the time and honor to participate in this important business and investment forum and commended the Embassy. Cambodia in the Republic of Korea in organizing this important forum.
He also praised the good cooperation between the two countries in the past, which has contributed significantly to the development of all sectors, especially the economy, trade and investment, especially the achievement of trade agreements. Free Cambodia-Korea, which came into force on December 1, 2022.
At the same time, Mr. Pan Sosak also highlighted the need for close and active cooperation between the private sector, especially the Chamber of Commerce and business associations from the two countries to expand opportunities and establish business and investment networks through Dialogue between companies, business matching, trade fairs, etc. aims to better understand exports, market demand and promote joint ventures.
He also praised the good relations between the two countries, especially in trade, investment and human resource exchange.
The Korean Minister of Commerce is confident that the entry into force of the Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement will increase confidence and further boost trade and investment between the two countries. Some policy directions include expanding and strengthening the supply chain between the two countries, cooperation in the digital economy and green economy, including clean energy.
The Korean Minister of Commerce also praised and praised the great success of Cambodia's chairmanship of ASEAN in 2022, especially commended the Minister himself for his successful chairmanship of the meeting. The ASEAN Economic Ministers and the relevant meetings were a source of pride.
At the same time, the Deputy Minister of Foreign Affairs of Korea also highly appreciated the organization of the forum and expressed optimism that the Cambodia-Korea Bilateral Trade Agreement, the Comprehensive Economic Agreement and the new Cambodian Investment Law will participate. The promotion of trade and investment between the two countries.
The Minister also informed that in 2022, Cambodia ranked first in receiving official development assistance (ODA) from Korea and also stated that Cambodia is a good partner in the ASEAN and Mekong region.
During the meeting, the Minister highly appreciated KOTRA's role and contribution to Cambodia's economic development. The Minister also informed about the entry into force of the Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement (CKFTA) and stated that this is an appropriate time to discuss trade and economic stimulus and increase the use of the CKFTA.
The Minister also requested the Korean side to invest in the processing and packaging of Cambodia's main agricultural products, including cassava, rubber, banana, turmeric, mango and other tropical fruits, to promote Cambodia's export of rich and quality agricultural products. Korean people.
He added that more than 200 Korean companies are currently investing in Cambodia, and KOTRA is attracting more investors, especially in the above areas and the auto or vehicle parts and wood and wood products sectors.
President of the Khmer National Unity Party understands that the arrest of Thach Setha is not a political matter, it is a pure criminal matter
(Phnom Penh): The President of the Khmer National Unity Party, Mr. Un Chim, stated that the arrest of Mr. Thach Setha, the Vice President of the Candlelight Party, is a purely criminal matter related to the issuance of checks, not a political matter.
He said this when the Khmer National Unity Party held a press conference announcing its participation in the upcoming parliamentary elections in July at the party's headquarters on January 26, 2023.
In the same press conference, the President of the Khmer National Unity Party also affirmed that it is an ethical political party, that is, it does not insult or paint other parties in accordance with the Cambodian Constitution, which implements a liberal, multi-party democracy. The party has even committed and reprimanded its activists for campaigning, citing the party's policy of not attacking other parties to seek votes.
The president of the Khmer National Unity Party expressed outrage at some politicians and a small number of analysts who were obsessed with opposition and the desire to destroy their rivals, who always understood that if they did not swear and did not accuse the leaders, they would all be puppets. Back. This is a dangerous point for the true democratic political struggle in Cambodia.
Mr. Un Chim raised some political issues. He said some parties claiming that the ruling party was formed because of Vietnam were unethical politics. The unsubstantiated allegations are defamation facing the law, which is why the Khmer National Unity Party does not allow political activists to attack other parties.
When asked what he thought of the Khmer National Unity Party's choice of Hun Manet as the ruling party's successor, Un Chim replied that the party's internal affairs should not be criticized or commented on by other parties. He added that the selection of candidates for the parties' turn was the right thing to do.
"The ruling party electing a successor is not a transfer of power to lead a country like North Korea," he said. Cambodia changes leaders through elections in line with liberal, multi-party democracy. "If Cambodia transfers power like North Korea, it will be called a dictatorship." This is according to Mr. Un Chim.
Interior Ministry spokesman: 40 people arrested for criminal and drug offenses on 27 January
(Phnom Penh): At least 40 suspects were arrested in criminal and drug offenses across Cambodia on January 27, 2023 yesterday. This was confirmed by General Khieu Sopheak, spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, to Fresh News on January 28, 2023.
General Khieu Sopheak added that of the 40 suspects, 16 were arrested in 12 criminal cases and 24 were arrested in eight drug offenses.
