The Royal Government of Cambodia has set a goal to increase exports to 1,600 million dollars (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Through the roadmap for the development of automobiles and electronics in Cambodia, the Royal Government has set a goal to increase the volume of exports in the field of electronics. Achieve 1.6 billion US dollars and create more than 10,000 new jobs by 2027.
Japan and China are the main sources of investment in the electronics sector in Cambodia, while the main export markets are: the United States, ASEAN, China, Japan and South Korea. Increased investment in the sector has boosted the workforce to 70 times in the last 10 years, now totaling about 30,000.
According to the roadmap, "the growing demand for electronics worldwide has been giving Cambodia more opportunities to capture market share of other high-demand products."
The production of electronic components in Cambodia has grown significantly, with exports growing at a rate of 20% per year from 2015 to 2019, mainly driven by the production of electrical components, cables, motors and light bulbs. LED, which is a labor activity.
However, there are also positive signs of growth potential in the production of parts, components, or printed circuit boards, as well as the assembly of other consumer products, such as speakers and cameras.
Dr. Ky Sereyvath, an economist at the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that now is the time for Cambodia to switch from the garment sector to the food sector to the electronics sector. Expertise in the field of electronics. Therefore, workers can also learn professional techniques in a short time so that workers know how to work in the field of electronics.
Mr. Oknha Lim Heng, Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, said that the electronics sector is very proud that Cambodia has attracted investment in this sector, especially in recent years. Therefore, the goal of exporting 1,600 million dollars is not really difficult in the current situation, after Cambodia reopened its economy, make the production chain run smoothly and unhindered.
"What aims to attract more investment is that Cambodia has a new investment law that provides a lot of incentives for investors to come to Cambodia, which makes investors do not hesitate to invest, in fact, there are Chinese, Japanese, Korean and "Other countries come to invest in Cambodia and this is a model for other investors to invest in Cambodia."
