Minister of Culture recommends six points to promote the work direction set for better progress in 2023
(Phnom Penh): The program to summarize the work of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts for 2022 and work directions for 2023 for two days from January 26-27, 2023 at Chaktomuk Conference Hall closed with the process. Smoothly.
In order to promote the work direction set for better progress in 2023, she recommended the following key recommendations:
First, the strengthening of the quantity and quality of work based on the work results achieved by the Ministry before the outbreak of Kovid-19 disease, including 97% work done in 2022 recently, we can conclude. The Ministry is capable of achieving 90% of its work per year compared to the total number of activities.
The Conference noted that the employment growth of ministries and governments has been steadily increasing as Cambodia continues to deepen its regional and global integration.
Due to the increase in employment, but the budget and the number of officials have not yet responded, she suggested the following:
Third: Lack of legal standards
The meeting noted the lack of many laws and regulations that are up to date with the current social situation. The meeting also noted that the draft amendments to the Law on Copyright and Related Rights have been drafted at the professional level. Therefore, she suggested that the necessary procedures be expedited to be able to implement this law as soon as possible.
* Record of partner budget: The meeting noted that the summary of partner budget data of more than 4 million US dollars in 2022 does not yet reflect the actual size of the partner budget contributed to the cultural sector. Once again, she requested that all units continue to keep a clear record of the partner budget and send it to the Ministry for a full summary for reporting at next year's convention.
Strengthening, monitoring and evaluating the recommendations of the conference: The meeting organizing committee of the Ministry must review, summarize and distribute the recommendations issued in the conference in both 2022 and 2023 to the leadership and competent units to implement. Establish a monitoring and evaluation system for reporting at next year's convention.
For units that need to intervene in the conference in the following years are:
* Prepare a presentation on the progress of the implementation of the recommendations issued * Propose figures on the magnitude of the main challenges that the organization faces each year as a basis for comparing fluctuations rather than Challenges in overview too.
Fifth: Inputs for organizing the government's political program in the next mandate
This year 2023 is the last year of the mandate of the Royal Government of the 6th legislature of the National Assembly. Therefore, the Conference identified the leaders, program managers and unit heads to be prepared to provide input into specific perspectives and action plans, focusing on three priority areas: human resource development, sustainable and environmental development, and diversification. Economy in the digital context to help achieve the vision of Cambodia 2030 and 2050.
For the development of human resources in the field of arts and culture, she suggested that attention should be paid to increasing the quality beyond quantity, focusing on productivity and competitiveness. At the same time, consideration must be given to providing scholarships to poor students in heritage areas.
Sixth: Cooperation from relevant ministries and institutions
The meeting examined and discussed many challenges, suggestions and directions, including some tasks that require more cooperation from ministries, institutions, capital-provincial administrations, and other stakeholders. .
Therefore, she would like to request representatives from ministries, institutions, capital-provincial administrations, and all stakeholders to help promote the following work:
* Request the Ministry of Public Function to review, advise and coordinate on the problem of misidentification of officials to prepare a new form of civil servant card (Smart Card). The meeting noted that this issue is a priority because there are many ministry officials who have a problem with identity. As a direction, we have to solve what is easy first and what is complicated must be considered as a special case later.
