Minister of Culture proposes to produce more quality short and long films
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Pheung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts, on January 27, 2023, proposed to produce more quality short and long film.
The Minister's proposal was made at the closing ceremony of the Ministry of Culture's work review meeting for 2022 and the work direction for 2023 for two days from January 26-27, 2023 at the Chaktomuk Conference Hall.
Ms. Phoeung Sakona expressed her satisfaction with the Cambodian film industry, especially the number of TV series. However, she understands that this number is not good yet, especially she wants to see the production of quality short and long films.
"The Cambodian film industry, especially TV series, is also growing, but at a level that we are not completely satisfied with, we must continue to push for this," she said. In addition, especially to promote the production of quality short and long films even more.
Meanwhile, Pok Borak, director of the Department of Film and Cultural Promotion of the Ministry of Culture, said that at least 30 Cambodian films could be produced, but a maximum of two could be exported to foreign markets.
Officials at the Ministry of Culture have said that most of the current Cambodian films are of poor quality due to limited production capacity as well as a lack of production budgets.
Sin Chansaya, an adviser to the Ministry of Culture, said the film was now limited in sound, image, screen size and comfort. Production problems, production capacity and lack of funds are all big issues. According to a senior official of the Ministry of Culture, the cinema in modern Cambodia is good, but most Cambodian films can not be screened due to the limited level of films.
An adviser to the Ministry of Culture sees that the capacity of producers is still limited because when entering the field, he understands that there are many difficulties. Today, there are very few highly trained and talented producers. Due to lack of funds, some producers have to perform themselves and film themselves, which is different from his skills, he also makes the results of the film is not good.
At the same time, Mr. Ek Buntha, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Cultural Technology of the Ministry of Culture, said that the production of each film is not simple and only a very talented producer is worth producing. Therefore, the Ministry of Culture has been working hard to find the next generation of young people who can help promote this sector to grow.
