(Siem Reap): Angkor Hospital for Children of Siem Reap Province will organize a training course for village health support team in Kralanh district to improve community health and reduce serious illness and death on 27 February. The coming year 2023.
Angkor Hospital for Children is a non-profit NGO located in Siem Reap. Since 1999, Angkor Hospital for Children has provided high quality, compassionate and free medical care to more than 2.5 million children.
During 2022, Angkor Hospital for Children organized a series of training sessions for village health support teams in Kralanh district in response to the survey results. The village health support team used the acquired knowledge to continue to provide health education to the villagers. The basic health training was conducted to 1,789 village health support groups and disseminated knowledge to an additional 36,449 villagers.
The trained health support team discusses two major challenges: malnourished children and understanding the importance of breastfeeding. In addition, the village health support team examined the nutritional status of 2,800 children and found 160 malnourished children. Following the discovery of malnourished children, the community health team provided treatment to the children.
In addition, your participation is an important part of improving the health care of Cambodian children. Angkor Hospital for Children, Siem Reap Province, all leaders and staff will continue to work to save the lives of children in the community in 2023. CPP in Kampong Leng district no longer meeting to set the direction towards the election
