A traffic police officer who drives a motorcycle to stop a car in the middle of the night must be disciplined and transferred to work in the intervention force
(Phnom Penh): Brigadier General San Sok Seiha, spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, confirmed to Fresh News on January 26, 2023 that for a traffic police officer who drove a motorcycle to chase a car in the middle of the night. Distributed on social media, the Phnom Penh Municipal Police decided to discipline and request the principle of reducing the rank of a rank and transfer duties to work in the intervention force.
"Regarding a traffic officer riding a motorcycle to stop a car on the night of January 19, 2023, at around 2:00 AM at the Chamkarmon traffic light, the officer was disciplined," the spokesman said. "The force transferred from the traffic office to the intervention force, in particular, asked the leadership to reduce the rank from lieutenant to lieutenant."
At the same time, Brigadier General said that on that day, Lieutenant Colonel Chim Salin, ID 78665, an officer under the Office of Road Traffic Bureau, left home with the intention of meeting at the Phnom Penh Municipal Police.
He continued, "This visit does not have any principles or regulations from the head of the unit, and this is not in accordance with the law enforcement hours, so the Phnom Penh Police Commission decided to discipline and ask the management to reduce the principles. "A rank of rank and transfer the duties of this traffic officer to work in the intervention force."
The Minister of Education chaired a meeting of the National Scout Council of Cambodia to discuss and consult on the draft of the National Scout Strategic Plan of Cambodia 2023-2027.
