Thais in Bangkok are advised to work from home and wear masks due to air pollution (Bangkok): Thais living in Bangkok are advised to do their work from home if possible. As well as wearing a mask when traveling out due to air pollution in the city has deteriorated to a level that can be dangerous to health. This was released by the AFP news agency on Thursday, January 26, 2023.
Bangkok authorities say people have been asked to use public transportation rather than private vehicles, and authorities will try to reduce sources of pollution, such as burning objects in the courtyard and construction activities. Well. Air purifiers will be distributed to vulnerable groups. However, the school has not yet been closed.
Burning of agricultural waste and wildfires are a major cause of air pollution in Thailand, which has deteriorated sharply in recent years, especially in the northwestern part of the country during December. To April. Pollution from these factors also affects Bangkok, which is already facing air quality problems due to factory activities, construction sites and traffic in the city.
The number of patients suffering from air pollution in the last week has more than doubled to nearly 213,000 from 96,000 a week ago, the health authority said. That. The mayor of Bangkok said the situation would be closely monitored from now until the end of February and was expected to improve in March.
International Customs Day! Director General of Customs of Cambodia considers young officials have the potential to perform their duties but need to share knowledge, skills and working methods from previous generations
(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia (ACC) on January 26, 2023 celebrated the International Customs Day under the presidency of Dr. Kun Nhim, Deputy Prime Minister of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia. With the participation of leaders and officials of Customs and Excise and the best business representatives.
Dr. Kun Nhim said that every year on January 26, the customs administrations of the 184 member countries of the World Customs Organization (CTO) hold a ceremony to celebrate and commemorate the establishment of the current Customs Cooperation Council. Named the World Customs Organization (WCO).
"We recognize that young officers have the potential to carry out their day-to-day work and contribute to the mission and vision of the customs administration, but they also need to share knowledge, skills, techniques and procedures from The previous generation, like the slogan "Boat to Kampong Nou."
The General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia strongly hopes that the celebration of International Customs Day will continue to support the General Department of Customs and Excise of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, as well as contribute to the promotion of culture. Of sharing more knowledge and pride of the customs profession.
Kampot Governor Continues to Lead Officers to Resolve Disputes in Kampong Trach District
(Kampot): Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Kampot Province, said that now all the people are living under the shadow of complete peace, and this peace is due to Samdech Techo who has sacrificed everything to bring To the people as well as the whole of Cambodia.
This statement was made while the provincial governor led the civil servants, forces, forces, authorities and stakeholders to resolve disputes outside the court system in Kampong Trach district on January 26, 2023.
On that occasion, the provincial governor stated that under the shadow of complete peace in the country, the head of the Royal Government always considers the well-being of the people and the mechanism of out-of-court dispute resolution has been put in place for sub-national authorities to implement. To mediate and end all disputes of citizens through win-win mechanisms, as well as to facilitate various expenses.
Therefore, for all your small grievances at the local level, please open your heart to listen to the reasons, acknowledge the facts and accept the solution outside the court system through a win-win mechanism together to end all problems.
The provincial governor continued that the people who came to receive the resolution said that the mechanism of out-of-court dispute resolution of the provincial governor under the winning mechanism made the people get the truth, accuracy and justice. Take both sides between conflicting pairs. Residents said that coming down to solve the problem directly made them happy and did not have to spend time and money to solve it.
Please be reminded that this is the second time for Kampong Trach district that the provincial governor came to resolve disputes outside the court system. On January 19, 2023, 25 cases were resolved and now there are 32 cases to Resolve further.
According to the Governor of Kampot Province, he said that he will lead the civil servants, the Armed Forces, the authorities and the relevant subordinates to resolve all disputes outside the court system at the local level in all cities and districts in Kampot Province. .
Lt. Gen. Hun Manet and Senior Minister Ly Thuch Sign a Demining Agreement Supported by the Cambodian Mine Action Fund 2025
(Phnom Penh): Lieutenant General Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the Army and Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Deputy Chief of the Mine Authority, on the morning of January 26, 2023, signed a contract for clearance. Mines Supported by "Cambodia Mine Action Fund 2025" The signing took place after receiving the high permission of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch said that with the support of the Samdech Techo Mine Action Project, the Cambodia Mine Action Fund 2025 and its development partner, the Mine Clearance Plan in 2023, covers an area of approximately 411 square kilometers. Therefore, after 2023, Cambodia will have 18 capitals and provinces to declare mines.
Next, 7 provinces will be included in the demining plan by 2025, including: Koh Kong, Pursat, Battambang, Pailin, Banteay Meanchey, Oddar Meanchey and Preah Vihear.
The diplomats were expelled for various reasons, including those directly involved in the situation in Ukraine, as well as allegations of misconduct with diplomatic roles. Of those, Bulgaria was the country that expelled the most Russian diplomats at 83.
Forty-five were then deported from Poland, 40 from Germany, 35 from Slovakia, 35 from France, 33 from Slovenia, 30 from Italy, and 28 from the United States. A total of 29 European countries, as well as the United States and Japan, have taken steps to expel Russian diplomats. In addition, 19 Russian personnel were expelled from the Russian mission to the European Union.
Since Russia launched its invasion of Ukraine on February 24, 2022, European countries such as Latvia, Estonia and Lithuania have reduced the level of diplomatic relations with Moscow. Russian consulates in Bulgaria, Latvia, Lithuania and Estonia are closed. Diplomatic relations between Russia and Ukraine were severed by the Ukrainian president on the day of the invasion.
