* First: Mr. New Saem, No. 2 on the official election results list of the National Election Committee, as Chairman of Kampot Provincial Council, replacing Mr. Chheng Phalla.
* Second: Mr. Ok Samnang, the fourth person in the official election results list of the National Election Committee, is a member of Kampot Provincial Council, replacing Mr. New Saem.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Deputy Prime Minister and Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, expressed such concern at a public forum on macroeconomic management and the Law on Finance for 2023 on January 25. 2023.
Of the more than $ 50 billion in private loans, 25 percent, or about $ 13 billion, was given to households, according to a senior official at the Ministry of Economy and Finance. 75% or about $ 40 billion is given to the company. Of these, 83% are provided by commercial banks and 17% by microfinance institutions.
Mr. Vongsy Visoth added that the increase in private debt requires a solution to prevent the burden of citizens and the national economy, while now international interest rates have risen steadily.
"The rise in private debt, on the one hand, sustains the economy on the other, creating risks as interest rates have risen further now and now some sectors are beginning to be affected, especially real estate and construction," he added.
However, he hopes that in the future the US Federal Reserve will stop raising interest rates, whether at a slower pace or at a slower pace due to lower inflation.
"I believe that in Cambodia, although some microfinance institutions keep interest rates the same or decrease some, there is a slight increase, but I do not think this increase is as high as the international market," he said. At the lowest level or keep the same.
He said that despite the increase in lending rates, there would be no reduction in the number of borrowers, which is expected to continue to grow in 2023 and increase deposits to a certain extent. Let microfinance institutions use this cash to provide loans to citizens who have been loaned to expand or rehabilitate their businesses.
