77 families affected by the collapse of Prek Thi in Takhmao City request the provincial governor to give them one plot of land
(Kandal): All 77 families affected by the collapse of Prek Prek Thi were evacuated by the provincial administration to live in temporary tents on privately owned land, requesting the provincial governor to help find land. Give each of them a plan because they do not want to live on their land.
The request was made when Mr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province, visited and chatted with them and distributed donations from the provincial administration to those affected by the floods. Prek Thi is located in Sangkat Roka Khpos, Takhmao City, Kandal Province on the afternoon of January 25, 2023.
The victims thanked the authorities and authorities at all levels for coming to their rescue and even distributed gifts. However, living here is not sure to be able to live forever because it is privately owned land and they want their own land, but please do not be too far from Takhmao City.
In response, Mr. Kong Sophoan said that he would take the proposal into consideration and let the people living here temporarily wait for consideration later, because now the budget of the provincial administration is limited, so living here is very good because the provincial administration Shelter, water and electricity are ready.
It should be noted that the donation of Kandal Provincial Administration was distributed to 43 families in Prek Thi Village, Sangkat Roka Khpos, Takhmao City, including: 1 family received 20 kg of rice, 1 case of noodles, 1 case of pure water and 200,000 Riels.
