March 18, 1970 was a military coup carried out by General Lon Nol to oust Norodom Sihanouk as head of state. The coup marked the beginning of a long civil war in Cambodia that fell into the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, killing nearly 3 million people and destroying human resources and infrastructure.
