Report: Half of all large-scale attacks in the United States are caused by personal problems and workplace conflicts (Video inside) (Washington): Half of all large-scale armed attacks in the United States from 2016 to 2020 Caused by personal problems and workplace conflicts, according to a new report by the US Secret Service. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Wednesday, January 25, 2023.
The 70-page report, released Wednesday by the US National Intelligence Service's National Threat Assessment Center, looked at 173 incidents in which three or more people were injured. The attack targeted workplaces, schools, religious institutions and public transport, killing 513 people and injuring 1,234.
The report states that the majority of perpetrators are men and often have mental health symptoms, financial insecurity or a history of involvement in domestic violence, while rifles are the weapon of choice for operations.
The report comes days after two major shootings in California that killed 18 people as authorities sought the motive behind the deadly attack.
The United States has seen a sharp increase in large-scale shootings in recent decades, but U.S. lawmakers from the two major parties have yet to find a common solution. Democrats have called for more gun control measures, while Republicans are focusing on mental health and improving security measures.
