(Phnom Penh): For hosting the 32nd SEA Games and the 12th ASEAN Para Games, which Cambodia will host in the near future, the Royal Government of Cambodia will use more than 20,000 troops to maintain security and order. And safety in this big sporting event.
This was said by General Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner and Chairman of the Security and Order Committee of the CAMSOC National Committee in the afternoon meeting on January 25, 2023 to disseminate security plans in the ceremony. The 32nd SEA Games and the 12th Paralympic Games 2023.
Speaking on the occasion, General Neth Savoeun affirmed that the first purpose is to ensure absolute safety and security when celebrating the SEA Games and the ASEAN Para Games in Cambodia before and after the Games. The second purpose is to enhance Cambodia's prestige on the international stage.
The General Commissioner of the National Police requested all Capital and provincial authorities to work together to strengthen safety and security for Cambodia to be successful in hosting the SEA Games and Paralympic Games. In particular, the capital-provincial authorities must be fully prepared to prevent and control hostile tactics.
The SEA Games were first held in Bangkok, Thailand in December 1959. The sport is held every two years, with the 11 member states taking turns to host the tournament.
Cambodia has been a member since the sport was established in 1958. Cambodia has been tasked with hosting the event many times, but due to the political crisis, war and economic situation, Cambodia has given up the task of hosting the event.
In that, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, asked for the understanding of the member countries of the Sports Commission not to organize this competition many times because Cambodia has not been able to afford and need funds to develop the country.
It was only in 2023 that Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to take on the task of organizing the Southeast Asian Games after Cambodia had adequate infrastructure in terms of sports infrastructure, competition services, budget and human resources.
From January 25, 2023, there are only 100 days left. To inspire Cambodians across the country to join in the celebration of this historic event, the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to organize a countdown to the SEA Games on the evening of January 25, 2023.
Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara chaired a meeting to discuss the provincial administration's request to adjust the boundaries of the two areas of the Tonle Sap region in Pursat province.
(Pursat): Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, on the afternoon of January 25, 2023, chaired a meeting to review the provincial administration's request to adjust the boundaries of the two Tonle Sap area in Pursat province. .
The meeting was held at the Provincial Hall with the participation of Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment, Mr. Keo Rattanak, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Director General of Electricity of Cambodia and Chairman. The Royal Government team visited Krakor and Kandeang districts and Mr. Khoy Rida, the governor of Pursat province, as well as the inter-ministerial delegates and other relevant local authorities.
It should be informed that the Head of the Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, at the closing of the annual meeting of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, ordered the officials to continue to address the people living around the Tonle Sap Lake by updating the map in each province accordingly. The situation where the government has redefined the boundaries of Zone 2 and Zone 3 and cut off the land where people live in both areas by the end of May 2023.
