This public debt is claimed by a senior official of the Royal Government of Cambodia to be low at only about 34% of gross domestic product (GDP) and compared to other ASEAN countries, Cambodia has the lowest public debt after Brunei. As a country, there is no foreign debt.
The Minister also stated that the budget that Cambodia plans to borrow from foreign and domestic $ 1.8 billion in 2023 is not equal to 20% of the total expenditure in 2023, different from 1995, when Cambodia relied on the budget from Up to 75% outside, but now Cambodia has up to 83% of its own budget, relying on external budget only more than 17%.
He added that this small number shows that Cambodia is independent, highly dependent on Cambodia's internal income , which has increased and reduced dependence on foreign budget.
By the end of 2022, Cambodia had foreign public debt of $ 9,955.08 million, of which 40% was from China, 21% from the Asian Development Bank, 22% from bilateral debt and 9% from the World Bank. Percent, heirloom debt 6 percent and multilateral debt 2 percent. Meeting of the Council and Executive Committee of the Association of Municipal, District, Commune and Sangkat Councils of Rattanakiri Province
