The speaker who attended the press conference was a representative of the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Administration. Long live Cambodia in the era of peace! This evening, Cambodia prepares for the countdown to hosting the SEA Games after 64 years of waiting
(Phnom Penh): With only 100 days left, it is time for Cambodia to take on the task of organizing the Southeast Asian Games or the SEA Games. This is another new historical event for Cambodia after waiting for about 64 years.
Cambodia has been a member since the sport was established in 1958. Cambodia has been tasked with hosting the event many times, but due to the political crisis, war and economic situation, Cambodia has relinquished its responsibility to host the event.
In that, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, asked for the understanding of the member countries of the Sports Commission not to organize this competition many times because Cambodia has not been able to afford and need funds to develop the country.
It was only in 2023 that Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to take on the task of organizing the Southeast Asian Games after Cambodia had adequate infrastructure in terms of sports infrastructure, competition, budget and human resources.
From January 25, 2023, there are only 100 days left. To inspire Cambodians across the country to join in the celebration of this historic event, the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to hold a countdown to the SEA Games on the evening of January 25, 2023.
The event was held at the Moradok Techo Stadium under the presidency of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Defense and Chairman of the National Organizing Committee for the 32nd SEA Games 2023 (CAMSOC).
The event will be accompanied by art shows and programs such as fireworks, bokator performances, taekwondo performances, dance performances, sportswear shows, all kinds of sports mascots and souvenir mascots. Chiefs of all kinds of missions and delegates of Khmer martial arts, Southeast Asian national dance performances, as well as the sound of drums, countdowns, fireworks, congratulations and so on.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen considers the event to host Cambodia's first SEA Games as an honorable event as well as promoting national prestige.
The Prime Minister called on the media as well as all Cambodians to participate in covering the countdown to the SEA Games. This promotion is a contribution to inspire the Cambodian people to support this proud event to be successful.
Please be informed that in order to ensure the success of this historic SEA Games, the Organizing Committee, chaired by Samdech Pichey Sena, has prepared the highest level of responsibility.
Cambodia plans to spend more than 100 million US dollars for the 32nd SEA Games and the 12th ASEAN Para Games.
