French investment delegation tells Samdech Techo Hun Sen that they have confidence in investing in Cambodia because there are many middle-income people (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): A group of investment delegates led by senior French officials told Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Director Cambodian Minister, they are confident in investing in Cambodia because Cambodia has a large middle-income population, plus a number of favorable factors.
During his visit to Cambodia, Mr. Olivier Becht, Minister of Delegation of the Ministry of Europe and Foreign Affairs of France in charge of Foreign Trade, Attracting Foreign Investors and French on Wednesday morning, January 25, 2023, led A group of French investors paid a courtesy call and discussed investment work with Samdech Techo Hun Sen and senior Cambodian officials.
According to Eang Sophalleth, the Prime Minister's personal aide, during the meeting, Olive Bich informed Samdech Techo that the French investment delegation had confidence in investing in Cambodia on the grounds that Cambodia Starting at zero and breaking the record of economic growth of about 7% for 20 years, Cambodia continues to reform, creating a favorable environment for investment, Cambodia has a large middle-income population.
Olive Bich told Samdech Techo that it was for these reasons that French investors decided to work with Cambodia to seek investment in high-speed rail, inland and air transport, construction, energy and other sectors.
Samdech Techo welcomed and informed the whole French investment delegation that Cambodia allows foreign investors to invest 100% for the high-speed railway from Phnom Penh to Ho Chi Minh City. The other two lines are to be expanded, encouraging private sector investment in the form of BOT.
Regarding clean energy, the Prime Minister emphasized that Cambodia is already using about 62% of clean energy and is attracting more investment. However, it is not allowed to build new coal-fired power plants or build dams across the Mekong River.
Samdech Techo also said that Cambodia is encouraging the use of solar energy, which is an opportunity for investment in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo also informed the delegation on the investment sector about some other priority sectors of Cambodia, including the promotion of industry, the promotion of investment in the high-tech industry, the promotion of investment in the processing industry, Cambodia has raw materials such as cashew, rubber, cassava, rice. Etc. For processing not only for the Cambodian market, but can be exported to other markets that are partners of Cambodia.
Please be reminded that Mr. Olive Bich is visiting Cambodia to strengthen economic cooperation between France and Cambodia. The visit lasts for two days, January 24 and 25.
The visit follows a meeting between Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen and French President Emmanuel Macron in Paris on December 13, 2022.
During the visit, the Minister will have various meetings with the French community in Cambodia, especially representatives of the vibrant French business community. The 5,000 French citizens living in Cambodia are registered with the embassy.
The Minister will also attend the groundbreaking ceremony for a memorial to the Cambodian and French martyrs of World War I, as decided by the Royal Government of Cambodia, in the presence of Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara. Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and Mrs. Pheung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts.
In addition, Olivier Beck will inspect the construction of the Bak Kheng water treatment plant, which is financed by the French Agency for Development (AFD), the European Investment Bank and the European Union.
Olive Beach will also visit the Angkor temples, especially the Western Mebon site, funded by France.
The French Embassy highlighted that the visit demonstrates France's growing commitment to ASEAN, reflected by the French President's participation in the G20 Summit in late 2022 in Bali and Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) Meeting in Bangkok.
Southeast Asia is an important area of French strategy in the Indo-Pacific, as it is the most vibrant location in the world in terms of economic growth, and ASEAN is the EU's third largest trading partner. Notice! Authorities set a three-month deadline for seafood business owners on Street 598, all car and motorcycle owners in Toul Kork to immediately stop using sidewalks and sidewalks.
