Mr. Ker Salem and Mr. Moan Chantharo have been announced as Deputy Governors of Baray District, Kampong Thom Province.
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Ker Salem and Mr. Moan Chantharo were announced as Deputy Governors of Baray District, Kampong Thom Province in the presence of Mr. Chan Dara, Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Province on January 25, 2023 at Baray District Hall. Oung Saroeun, district governor, commune authorities, armed forces, district officials and many people.
After listening to the brief report of Mr. Oung Saroeun, Governor of Baray District and the commitment of the Deputy Governor to be announced to take office, Mr. Chandara congratulated Mr. Ker Salem and Mr. Moan Chantharo. The Interior Ministry gives the trustee the role of the new Deputy Governor.
He stressed that the recent achievements of the Royal Government under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, have successfully fought the Kovid 19 epidemic, maintaining peace, social stability, security, public order, development in all areas and protection. Absolutely sharpen the territorial integrity.
He asked the district governors to understand the roles and responsibilities of the division in solving transparently, strengthen security and public order to ensure the safety of the people, especially to eliminate all forms of illegal gambling in their district because gambling affects Family life will cause insecurity to the society, contrary to the policy of safe villages and communes.
Mr. Chandara encouraged the development and construction of new achievements at the local level, especially the provision of public administration services in the communes, promote the implementation of the reform programs of the Royal Government, continue to work hard to strengthen internal unity, strengthen its role and responsibilities. Effective and strengthen the capacity of subordinates to perform daily administrative tasks better.
Cambodia lowers its economic growth forecast for 2023 from 6.6 percent to 5.6 percent (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Deputy Prime Minister and Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance According to the latest assessment, in 2023, the Cambodian economy is projected to grow by only 5.6 percent, up from 6.6 percent previously. However, the new figures are still good for the economy. Cambodia.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth's remarks were made at a public forum on macroeconomic management and financial law for management 2023 on January 25, 2023 at Sofitel Phuket Tra Phnom Penh.
Mr. Vongsy Visoth said, "Cambodia's economy is expected to grow by 6.6 percent this year, but according to the latest assessment, the Cambodian economy is projected to grow by only 5.6 percent," said new Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Approved for use and the most realistic figures, as well as figures similar to the assessments of major international institutions.
He said that according to the assessment of Cambodia's economy in 2022 growth of 5.2 percent and the sector to drive economic growth in Cambodia, tourism, domestic consumption through wholesale and retail and manufacturing industry. Strength, increase in garment exports.
He added, however, that the construction and real estate sectors were still in a slump in both 2022 and 2023, with the slowdown likely to continue if foreign investment conditions slow down. Mine Authority: As of December 2022, Belgium's APOPO has cleared more than 23 million square meters of landmines and explosive remnants of war and benefited nearly 40,000 people.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Senior Minister Ly Thuch praised and appreciated APOPO's participation in the clearance of landmines and explosive remnants of war in Cambodia since 2014, and thanked them for their contribution to the liberation. Land for local people and reduction of accident rates in Cambodia.
The Senior Minister said that APOPO currently has a total of 95 staff working to clear mines and mines using rats and dogs in Ratanakkiri, Preah Vihear, Siem Reap and Battambang provinces under good partnership and cooperation with CMAC and MAG.
APOPO is a Belgian non-profit and humanitarian demining organization that has received official recognition and license from the Mine Authority for mine / demining operations in Cambodia.
