National Assembly President Urges 10 Newly-Appointed Cambodian Ambassadors to Protect and Promote National Values on the International Stage
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia, has instructed 10 newly appointed Cambodian Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary Ambassadors to work to preserve and promote national values on the international stage.
The 10 newly appointed ambassadors paid a courtesy call on National Assembly President Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin at the National Assembly building this morning, January 25, 2023.
Mr. Koy Kuong, who has been appointed by the Royal Government as the Ambassador to India, expressed his deepest gratitude to the President of the National Assembly for allowing him and all his colleagues to pay a courtesy call. Recommendations to carry out work to serve the nation on the international stage.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin welcomed and congratulated the 10 Ambassadors who have been entrusted by the Royal Government to be the Ambassadors of Cambodia to 10 of Cambodia's friendly countries.
Samdech stated that from now on, you are a high-ranking official representing Cambodia abroad and play an important role in promoting friendly relations and cooperation in all fields with those countries, especially the promotion of national prestige and independence. And the protection of our national sovereignty.
The National Assembly President stressed that the Ambassador has a lot of important work to do on foreign policy in the context of the changing world in the new context of the world order. In the current circumstances, rapid socio-economic recovery is an important and necessary factor to contribute to the national economy.
(Phnom Penh): The National Assembly delegation led by Mr. Sous Yara, Chairman of the Foreign Affairs, International Cooperation, Propaganda and Information Committee of the National Assembly, on January 25, 2023, met with Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information and colleagues to find out The media in Cambodia.
This meeting was held at the National Assembly of Cambodia in accordance with the Constitution, Article 97, New Rules of Procedure of the National Assembly, Article 34 New and Decision No. 005, dated January 09, 2014 on the Roles and Duties of the Committee on Foreign Affairs, International Cooperation, Propaganda. Minister of Agriculture urges Kratie-Stung Treng Fisheries Administration to have a clear strategy to address dolphin conservation challenges
(Kratie): Mr. Dith Tina, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on January 25, 2023, urged the Fisheries Administration to have a clear strategy for dolphin conservation in Kratie and Stung Treng provinces. Be effective with what remains.
This promotion was made on the occasion that Mr. Dith Tina, the leader of the Ministry, inspected and strengthened the conservation work of Mekong River dolphins in Prek Kampi, Kratie Province. The ceremony was held at the Kampi Dolphin River Conservation Post on January 25, 2023.
In the activity of inspecting and strengthening the conservation of Mekong dolphins, Mr. Dith Tina recommended to the Fisheries Administration on the conservation of dolphins, with a clear strategy to address the challenges of working effectively with what is still special. Aim to protect dolphin treasures and reduce fishing by turning fishing into something less expensive but more efficient.
In addition, Mr. Dith Tina also called for the prevention of fishing with illegal equipment, he will provide radios, flashlights, binoculars and high-speed boat engines for cruising dolphins, as well as study the location of fishermen. It is illegal to identify the perpetrator in order to follow the procedure.
At the same time, Mr. Dith Tina said to provide additional input from the geographical location and the use of force at core locations such as Kampi, which is rich in dolphins in the dry season. Minister Dith Tina also praised the willingness of all officials to fulfill their duties and continue to work with partner WWF, as well as try to find projects to support the guards and the community.
However, the Minister reminded not to have illegal fishermen in both the dry season and the rainy season, because it is a central location for growing fish. He hopes to preserve dolphins by continuing to conserve and develop dolphins and fish habitats.
Mr. Mok Ponlok, Director of Kratie Fisheries Administration, said that Kratie Province is located in the plateau of the Northeast Zone with a total area of 11,094 square kilometers, with the Mekong River flowing about 140 kilometers along the river Sambo Anlong fish sanctuary. There are 62 canyons.
The Mekong River Dolphin Management and Protection Area in Kratie Province extends from the head of Koh Trung in Kratie City to the border of Stung Treng Province with a length of 85 km and is divided into a core area and a buffer zone.
Along the Mekong River are rich in aquatic plants and small and large floodplain forests growing on the waterfront, large rock formations and small reefs, sand islands, etc. From the border of Kratie province in O'Mreah commune, Siem Bok district to the Cambodia-Laos border, there are 35 canyons, including 4 fish and dolphin sanctuaries, which are classified as protected areas of Tbong Khla, Anlong Koh Kon Sat and Anlong Koh Santak.
