Thailand to receive 11.15 million foreign tourists in 2022, higher than government target
BANGKOK: Thailand will receive 11.15 million foreign tourists in 2022, up from about 428,000 in 2021, when travel restrictions were imposed, Thai Tourism Ministry data showed on Tuesday. To prevent Kovid infection. According to the Bangkok Post.
The Bangkok Post reports that the government's higher-than-expected figures reflect a strong shift as Thailand seeks to revive its key tourism industry, which has been hit hard by austerity measures. Kovid disease.
Prior to the pandemic in 2019, the kingdom received nearly 40 million foreign tourists for the entire year.
Malaysia, India and Singapore were Thailand's three largest markets last year, according to the Thai Ministry of Tourism and Sports.
By 2023, the Thai government is expecting 25 million international visitors, including at least 5 million from China, Thailand's largest source market before the outbreak. According to the Bangkok Post.
