(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly, Chairman of the Council for Agricultural and Rural Development, representing Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on January 24, 2023, made seven recommendations to the Ministry of Rural Development to continue its work. High responsibility.
The seven-point recommendation was made on the occasion of Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly presiding over the closing ceremony of the 2022 work review meeting and the 2023 work direction of the Ministry of Rural Development. The ceremony took place at the Sokha Residence Hotel in Phnom Penh on the afternoon of January 24, 2023.
Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly said that in this situation, the Ministry of Rural Development must continue to work responsibly to respond to changes in sustainable socio-economic development in rural areas.
On the occasion of closing the meeting to review the work results in 2022 and the work direction in 2023 of the Ministry of Rural Development, on behalf of the Royal Government, he would like to make the following recommendations:
Second, the Ministry must continue to study, research and develop the construction, repair and improvement of rural roads through new technologies to respond to the reduction of raw materials such as red gravel, sand, mountains, etc. At the same time, we must continue to strengthen the use of rural roads more effectively through maintenance and repair, especially efforts to prevent and suppress overweight transportation on rural roads.
Fourth, strive to pay attention to both the political and technical level by trying to turn the other three target provinces, Kampong Chhnang, Kep and Kampong Speu, into provinces that will stop open defecation (ODF) in 2023.
Fifth, continue to promote and expand rural economic diversification activities through job creation, entrepreneurship and economic activities, as well as vocational training in agriculture, handicrafts, services and other occupations in order to participate in solving daily life problems, increasing family income. Each in the countryside will contribute to reducing the risk of migration to cities or cross-border risk to other countries.
Sixth, continue to promote and strengthen the capacity development of civil servants at all levels, both national and sub-national, and further develop institutions in order to improve efficiency, transparency and accountability for growth and sustainability.
Citing a statement from the North Korean government, Seoul-based NK News reported without mentioning Kovid 19, but said Pyongyang residents were required to stay in Pyongyang. Their home until Sunday this week and have to get heat checked several times a day.
On Tuesday, NK News reported that people in Pyongyang were likely to buy stockpiles in anticipation of tight government measures, while it was unclear whether other parts of the country were closed.
North Korea recognized the first outbreak of Kovid 19 in its country in 2022, and in August of the same year, North Korea declared a complete victory over Kovid 19. North Korea has an estimated 4.77 million Kovid 19 out of a total population of 25 million. However, Pyongyang has stopped reporting 19 Kovid cases and deaths since July 29, 2022.
