(Tbong Khmum): Mr. Dith Tina, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that the Ministry will turn the rubber plantation located in Chi Ror II Commune, Tbong Khmum District, Tbong Khmum Province into a museum for rubber seed research.
This statement was made during Mr. Dith Tina's visit to the Rubber Research Institute of Cambodia in Chiro II Commune, Tbong Khmum District / Province to learn about the local situation and reduce costs through the development of new varieties. High yield, disease resistance, maintaining soil quality and reducing production costs on January 24, 2023.
Mr. Dith Tina said that the rubber plantation has rubber from the previous generation, according to documents from 1924 to the present is 99 years old.
He pointed out that what is important is that we can consider it as a rubber museum or can be considered as a national treasure because there is nowhere else where rubber was planted before, there are about 477 trees left.
In addition, the Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries will provide expertise in the preparation, protection and treatment of rubber in rubber plantations, some of which may be diseased because it is a stock of seeds for further research and production.
