(Tbong Khmum): Mr. Dith Tina, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, confirmed that the Ministry is testing a new rubber variety that will yield more than 50 percent of ordinary rubber.
This statement was made on the occasion of Mr. Dith Tina led his colleagues to visit the Rubber Research Institute of Cambodia in Chi Ror II Commune, Tbong Khmum District, Tbong Khmum Province on January 24, 2023.
The above visit to the Rubber Research Institute of Cambodia to understand the basic situation and reduce costs by creating new varieties with high yields, disease resistance, maintaining soil quality and reducing production costs by No till planter method.
Mr. Dith Tina said that the rubber work is good and Cambodia is a large producer of rubber, both household rubber and industrial rubber, and he thinks that the results of all these studies will increase the product and increase profits.
In addition, Mr. Dith Tina recommended to study the production and cultivation process of rubber, the stimulation of each variety, especially the effect of ground cover crops and fertilizers between rubber trees. On the other hand, you need to look at the annual results, the market price and the labor force.
At the same time, Mr. Dith Tina also inspected the Agricultural Research Station for the Conservation of Men Khnor in Bos Khnour Commune, Chamkar Leu District, Kampong Cham Province. Long lasting quality.
Dith Tina said that experiments for planting without plowing are also underway and expanding, and that he will continue to monitor the results as he sees the results. It has to do with technology, to see more economic efficiency, whether it is really profitable or not.
At the same time, Dith Tina also expressed interest in the carbon footprint in the soil related to climate change. However, he suggested looking further at the method, both in the field and in the presentation.
