(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to renovate Veal Bek Chan Airport in Battambang province and upgrade it to 4C to attract tourists to this ancient land.
This is according to Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Battambang Province, this morning, January 24, 2023, in the press conference of the Spokesperson of the Royal Government on "Success for the past 5 years of Battambang Provincial Administration".
According to Mr. Sok Lou, the 4C level that needs to be improved at Veal Bek Chan Airport is equal to the size of the airport in Siem Reap today. However, the provincial governor has not been able to confirm when the site will open, while the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation and the provincial administration are currently meeting to address the impact.
The Battambang provincial governor said, "In 2019, Samdech Techo recommended the conversion of Veal Bek Chan airport into the 4C airport in Siem Reap today." "But after the Kovid crisis, we have not studied it, but recently the civil aviation has met with the provinces several times and addressed the impact, we will continue to do this."
Mr. Sok Lou expressed his strong belief that when the airport is improved, it will make it easier for both investors and tourists to travel and boost the economic growth of Battambang province.
Please be informed that Battambang Airport (or Veal Bek Chan Airport) was first opened during 1967, but after the Khmer Rouge took power in 1975, the airport was completely closed until 1979, Battambang Airport was closed. Launched for military flight only.
However, by 1991, on the way to peace, Battambang Airport was completely closed to the military until now and became the evening resort of the people in the provincial town of Battambang. Samdech Kittipritthbandit would like to thank His Majesty the King of Cambodia for donating $ 1,000 to the Cambodian Red Cross for January.
