The following is the full text of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen's message to His Majesty the King of the Kingdom of Cambodia: Cambodia-Switzerland Wants Free Trade Agreement to Promote Trade Karma
(Davos-Closter, Switzerland): Cambodia and Switzerland want to establish a free trade agreement together to promote better trade.
During the bilateral meeting, the Minister mentioned that the diplomatic relations between the two countries, which were established in 1963, have led to good relations to this day.
The minister said that trade between the two countries is increasing year by year, with the total trade volume between Cambodia and Switzerland in the total amount of about 379 million US dollars. In 2021, the total trade volume will be more than 974 million US dollars.
He thanked the Swiss government for its assistance and development programs in areas such as good governance and people's participation in agriculture and food security, as well as vocational training and employment.
She praised Cambodia's success in curbing the spread of Kovid 19 and congratulated Cambodia for chairing ASEAN in 2022 and successfully hosting the ASEAN Summit.
The two sides pledged to further strengthen existing bilateral ties and expand cooperation in priority areas as well as international cooperation.
Cambodian, Thai Armed Forces Meet to Strengthen Cooperation in Preventing and Suppressing Border Crime
(Banteay Meanchey): The Cambodian and Thai armies met to strengthen cooperation in preventing and cracking down on border crime.
The meeting took place on the morning of January 24, 2023. The Cambodian side is led by Major General Seng Thearin, Deputy Commander of the 5th Army Division, on behalf of Lt. Gen. Sam Oun, Deputy Commander of the Army, 5th Army Commander, and the Thai side is led by Major General Pakna Khlev Platuk, 1st Army Commander. Thailand.
The meeting was also attended by Mr. Oum Rath, Governor of Banteay Meanchey and Sa Kaeo. The meeting took place at the Cambodia-Thailand Friendship Bridge, Poipet-Khlong Leuk International Port.
The meeting was held to strengthen the sisterhood and cooperation between the two armies.
1: Solving problems in border areas better.
2. Continue to implement the mechanism of the meeting between the commanders of the two countries' Armed Forces. Cross-border theft, deforestation, other crimes and prevention of terrorism, crime along the border.
During the meeting, the Commander-in-Chief of the 1st Thai Army thanked Cambodia for assisting Thais in the recent fire at the Grand Diamond Hotel in Poipet.
Major General Seng Thearin asked the Thai side to help prevent politicians from the two countries from using the border as a political issue, as the border issue is the responsibility of both countries' forces.
The meeting was held in an atmosphere of warmth, joy, friendship and brotherhood.
