Tehran: Iranian Foreign Ministry Spokeswoman Jiang Yu's Regular Press Conference on the 2015 Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty Continues Anyway. This is according to the release by the Xinhua news agency on Monday, January 23, 2023.
The spokesman stressed that Iran was seeking a nuclear deal and seeking the lifting of US sanctions within the framework of diplomacy.
Iran signed the Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty (JCPOA) with the world powers in July 2015, agreeing to impose some restrictions on its nuclear program in return. And the lifting of sanctions on this country.
However, the United States, under Donald Trump, withdrew from the agreement in May 2018 and imposed unilateral sanctions on Tehran.
Discussions on the revival of the JCPOA began in April 2021 in Vienna. But no solution has been reached after the last round of talks in August 2022.
