(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Monday, January 23, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen presided over the graduation ceremony for nearly 7,000 students of the Cambodian University of Specialties (CUS) who successfully graduated. . The event was held at the Chroy Changvar International Convention and Exhibition Center.
CUS University is a well-known higher education institution in Cambodia and has the high support of the Royal Government, especially Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Samdech Techo is always honored to preside over the graduation ceremony for graduates.
According to the report, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has already presided over seven university graduation ceremonies.
Dr. Steng Sokhom, President of the University Board of Directors, expressed his great pleasure that the Board of Management, Personnel, Professors and Students of CUS University were honored to receive the most meaningful hospitality to Samdech Techo. Invited to give the highest honor for the eighth time in the graduation ceremony for the winning students.
Dr. Steng Sokhom also said that the total number of successful graduates, including associate degree, bachelor's degree, master's degree and doctoral degree, is now 6,791 females. 2,940 people from 4 branches (Phnom Penh, Kampong Cham, Kampong Thom and Kampot).
Dr. said that among the winning students, there are 178 students of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, 105 women.
The Cambodian University of Specialties began training in 2003. The University has been active in training, imparting knowledge and skills to participate in building human resources, which is an important foundation for building society.
In order to build human resources with quality, value and success for the society, the specialized universities of Cambodia have set the basic principles in the operation of their daily work, namely students, professors, academic staff must learn, teach, research and provide services. With quality, professional ability and good personality.
Dr. Steng Sokhom highlighted that the results and achievements of the past 20 years clearly show the ability, ability and experience that colleagues and colleges and universities of Cambodia have in its noble mission is "training to know. "Training to have knowledge, training to have a good personality to succeed in work and career."
The University has cooperated and signed MoUs with 56 foreign universities and institutions from South Korea, China, Japan, Thailand, the United Kingdom, the Philippines, Bangladesh, Malaysia, India, Indonesia, Germany, Vietnam and Israel. Through this cooperation, the University has sent professors and students to study long courses and short internships, as well as to accept foreign students to exchange studies with students of specialized universities of Cambodia.
To make it easier for students to find internships, internships, volunteer work and job search, the Cambodian University of Specialties has signed MoUs with 543 local companies and institutions across the country and will continue to promote it more widely.
