Ukrainian Demining Officer Successfully Completes Demining Training in Cambodia
(Siem Reap): Ukraine Mine Action Specialists have successfully completed a demining technology training course conducted by the Cambodian Mine Action Center (CMAC) supported by the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA).
Mr. Heng Ratana, on behalf of the leadership and staff of CMAC, especially the people of Cambodia, would like to express our condolences to the people of Ukraine who have lost their lives and are suffering from the war.
He said that the one-week training of the demining technology training course went smoothly, proceeded as planned and was completed successfully.
Mr. Heng Ratana expressed his deep gratitude to the people and government of Japan, especially the management of JICA in both Phnom Penh and Tokyo for their active support in establishing this training.
Heng Ratana also hopes that all experts from Ukraine will use demining equipment that is suitable for real, safe situations to be implemented in Ukraine.
Please be informed that for the whole week, the Ukrainian trainees received professional training and experience on the minefield under the cooperation of CMAC technical technicians, along with additional demonstrations on mine machine technology equipment.
During the training, the Ukrainian trainees were very interested and learned more about the CMAC's specialized forces operating on minefields that can respond to the situation in Ukraine, such as mine clearance. Machinery and demining skills by commanding dogs.
