Vendors of vegetables, fruits, cakes, and utensils for Sen Pren have all said that this year's sales are better than last year because people seem to be willing to pay for Sen Pren again.
Che Mom, a jewelry seller for preparing Chinese offerings in the Central Market of Phnom Penh, is very busy with his sales, with a steady stream of customers. She said that since the 199 outbreak of Kovid, sales during the holiday season have fallen sharply, but during the Chinese New Year 2023, she has gained more customers by about 20%.
This week is the time when some Cambodians of Chinese descent in Cambodia celebrate the three-day Chinese New Year from January 21 to 24, 2023. For the past two or three years, each market in Phnom Penh has been crowded with buyers for gifts and food.
At home, as well as on the streets, there are gradually arranged colorful flowers, especially art flowers and curtains, home decor, lanterns and so on.
