(Phnom Penh): Paragon International School, originally named Zaman, is an international educational institution in Cambodia. The school, which provides international education, is now 25 years old. After overcoming many difficulties and obstacles over the past 25 years, Paragon International School is gaining strong support both domestically and internationally.
Prior to its current recognition, Paragon International School faced many difficulties, especially in the early stages. According to Eang Sophalleth, founder of Paragon International School, the difficulties encountered at that time were not yet familiar with the international education system, not yet adapted to an education system with many hours of study and difficulty. Find a teacher and so on.
Paragon School pursues a strategy of educating students in the direction of "quality first" and in accordance with the principles of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, especially on the bilingual curriculum, Khmer-English and full-day study.
For Eang Sophalleth, Paragon International School's biggest achievement is the quality of its education, recognized by world-renowned schools. Students who graduate with Paragon International School are able to continue their studies with an overseas school without the need for additional training.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth was very pleased with the achievements of Paragon International School over the past 25 years. He called this achievement the achievement of one of his big dreams, especially to be able to manage the school on his own, without foreigners controlling the education in the school as before.
Along with this glorious achievement, Mr. Eang Sophalleth also announced the expansion of the school branch, giving the opportunity to former students of Paragon School to become the owner of Paragon School Branch B. Mr. Eang Sophalleth also expressed his ambition to expand overseas.
Despite the school's remarkable success, the provision of a quality education in line with the wishes of the parents as well as the Royal Government remains a strong ambition of the management of Paragon Education.
Renovation of Angkor Wat Hanging Bridge in the second phase achieved 90%
(Siem Reap): From 2016 to 2023, the repair of the bridge over the Angkor Wat temple in the second phase has achieved about 90% of the results under the cooperation between APSARA Authority and Sophia University, Japan to increase the value and maintain the form. The origin of this ancient building to be restored.
"According to the actual situation, the process of repairing the bridge by January 2023 has reached about 90 percent, and the team may take at least another year to complete this work," he said.
He added that in the process of repairing the bridge over the Angkor Wat temple, some challenges are always encountered, such as despite being in the state of Kovid 19 for more than 2 years, but the repair activities continue to rain during the rainy season, especially the bridge. Dry, surrounded by water, difficult to repair.
Mr. Sato Rimiva expressed his happiness when he assisted Cambodia in repairing the bridge and other conservation projects. He observed that the APSARA Authority has made great efforts in the conservation and development of Angkor, especially the capacity building of human resources until the implementation of projects at each site does not have to rely on foreigners as before.
Please be informed that since 1989, Sofia University of Japan has been cooperating with APSARA Authority in many activities to help Angkor site related to human resource training in archeology and architecture, excavation at Banteay Kdei, educational program Heritage to the people and students living around the Angkor area, the initiative to establish the Norodom Sihanouk Angkor Museum.
