Senior Cambodian officials go out to attract Japanese investors operating in Thailand to expand production lines in Cambodia, especially vehicles and electronics, as of January, Japan invested $ 2.9 billion in Cambodia
(Bangkok): Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister, Secretary General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC) and his delegation left for Bangkok, Thailand to preside over a seminar on Cambodian investment aimed at informing Japanese investors. Operating in Thailand and aiming to find a location to expand the production chain in neighboring countries from the investment climate and legal regulations on investment in Cambodia.
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea thanked JETRO and JBAC for co-organizing this workshop and always playing an important role in promoting the investment opportunities and investment environment in Cambodia to Japanese and Japanese investors. Who spent valuable time attending this workshop.
The Minister said that the Royal Government of Cambodia welcomes foreign investment by opening the door to welcome investment from all countries in all fields without discrimination. In particular, Cambodia's investment law provides an open, transparent incentive to all investors, guaranteeing and protecting investment without discrimination.
He also emphasized that the Royal Government of Cambodia pays close attention to investors by organizing forums between the government and the private sector to provide opportunities for investors to raise challenges and suggestions to the government to interpret and come up with solutions. Win-Win In addition to this forum, the Cambodia-Japan Joint Committee Meeting has also been held semi-annually for Japanese investors since 2009.
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea praised the Japanese investment in the past, which not only brought investment, but also contributed to the diversification of the Cambodian economy, bring new technologies, and participate. Increase the skills of Cambodian workers.
Mr. Sok Chendasophea informed the workshop that recently, the official road map for the development of the Cambodian automotive and electronics sector, which was officially approved for use by the Cambodian government in December 2022, has set the Country Plus strategy as a priority measure while Japanese investment in industry in the past has been mostly "Thai + 1" investments by Japanese investors operating in Thailand.
The workshop also included a presentation on the roadmap for the development of the automotive and electronics sector in Cambodia by Mr. Nuth Un Vanra, Deputy Secretary General of the Cambodian Investment Committee and a presentation on investment incentives by Mr. Lim Visal, Assistant to Minister Sok. Chenda Sophea too.
Please be informed that as of January 2023, the Council for the Development of Cambodia has approved 150 Japanese investment projects with a total investment capital of approximately $ 2.9 billion.
