"This shows that our country, though small, has the economic growth that we want to show the world and also shows the pope, who is one of the religious leaders in the world, that we Cambodians are Live in peace and prosperity and may the pope pray for our people to be sustainable in the long run. "I also sent a message to the pope wishing him a long and healthy life."
Kouch Mengly also called on Cambodians living in and out of the country to work together to make the country's name known to the world. As Cambodians, we must love and care for each other so that the nation can be valued by the world.
At the same time, Venerable San Sochea said that he was happy to participate in this activity and bring Cambodia to the fore. He also warned Cambodians, whether traveling abroad or not, not to forget that they are Cambodians.
Venerable San Sochea added that when meeting with the pope, he and Duke Kouch Mengly clearly told the pope that he was Cambodian. He added that this confirmation was not despised, but praised because he knew who he was and had a clear identity and was trusted.
At the same time, the Catholic priest Will Conquer said that any religion is very important in building a prosperous society. The priest also thanked the Royal Government of Cambodia for its efforts to give all religions in Cambodia complete freedom of religion.
"I would like to thank the Khmer state because I am a foreigner," he said. I have lived in Cambodia for about 20 years with freedom, no one persecuted me, no one despised me, even though I am a Christian. "I thank God, I thank His Majesty Norodom Sihamoni, Samdech Techo Prime Minister Hun Sen, the Cambodian People's Party and all the leaders who helped bring the country to harmony, and I do not want to see war destroy Cambodia again."
He considered Cambodia as a model in Asia with religious harmony.
Please be informed that Duke Kouch Mengly and Venerable San Sochea are rare Cambodians who have had the opportunity to visit him, the Pope. So far, only two Cambodians have joined him, the pope: his father (King Norodom Sihanouk, the King) in 1950 and His Majesty the King in 1986.
According to the same source, Pope Francis thanked the Cambodian delegation for their visit to the Vatican City, where they continued to meet with Vatican officials for interfaith dialogue. Open China will provide more opportunities to the world
China's latest foreign trade data released in 2022 shows that China's total exports and imports exceeded 40 trillion yuan for the first time, maintaining the status of The largest trading country in the world for six consecutive years. In the context of the current global economy, it has become a vivid picture that China adheres to a high degree of openness.
The 20th Congress of the Communist Party of China (CPC) said that China will adhere to openness as a fundamental national policy. As Xi Jinping said, "China, which continues to move towards modernization, will surely provide more opportunities to the world and contribute more to the development of humanity as a whole!"
