(Ratanakkiri): Two representatives of the Ratanakkiri Provincial Prosecutor's Office led a police force against economic crime and the Forestry Administration to close a handicraft factory to make rubber bowls in the company "Mittapheap Rubber Development" in Ten village, Yatung commune, O'Yadao district.
It should be reminded that on January 16, 2023, Mr. Hang Sambath, Deputy Prosecutor of Ratanakkiri Provincial Court, with the participation of Brigadier General Nou Dara, Deputy Commissioner of Police for Economic Crimes and Mr. Keo Vuth, Chief of Bor Keo Forestry Administration. Inspected the location of "Mittapheap Rubber Development Company".
Mr. Yoeung Hertiek, Representative of "Mittapheap Rubber Development" Company, said on January 19, 2023 that the company bought firewood from the people who cut the remaining wood in the plantation and transported it to sell to the company, but the company did not accept the purchase. Know that it is illegal.
He said that in order to facilitate its business, the company is willing to pay fines in accordance with the forest law and the law of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
He added that the company "Mittapheap Rubber Development" has contributed to creating jobs for many people to have a comfortable life. The company has started to make rubber bowls as a test for internal use, as rubber will start to open in 2023, as well as local development and forest protection.
Regarding this case, Mr. Keo Pheakdey, Spokesman of the Ratanakkiri Provincial Prosecutor's Office, told Fresh News on the morning of January 20, 2023 that on January 16, 2023, the representative of the Prosecutor of the Provincial Court, Mr. Hang Sambath, led Authorities inspected and found illegal timber stockpiles, but the Forestry Administration, after fining the company owner under the Forestry Law, did not report to the Ratanakkiri Provincial Prosecutor's Office.
Only on January 19, 2023, Mr. Ngin Pech, Prosecutor of Ratanakkiri Provincial Court, appointed Mr. Muth Sambath instead of Mr. Sambath to lead the inspection force in the company again, finding illegal forest firewood collection from Forestry Administration.
