Former two-star Soy Chansoeun, who arrested and abused a woman in early 2021, has been acquitted
(Kampong Speu): A 48-year-old former two-star military officer named Soy Chansoeun or Tes Chansoeun alias Va, who was sued by a woman for forcing and using violence in January 2021 and was arrested and sent to The former military officer has now been acquitted and sentenced to life in prison.
This decision is in accordance with the order of the Kampong Speu Provincial Court, which has Judge Slina on December 22, 2022. According to the court order, which went through three trials: June 7, 2022, October 6, 2022 and December 6, 2022.
In the court order, it was decided as follows:
* First, the name Soy Chansoeun or Sar Chansoeun alias Va, male, 48 years old, Khmer nationality, was released on charges of "illegal detention" committed in Takhmao City, Kandal Province and Kampong Speu Province on January 22, 2021. Criminal offenses that are punishable under the provisions of Article 253, point 1 of the Penal Code.
* Third: Name: Soy Chansoeun or Tes Chansoeun alias Va, Male, 48 years old, Nationality Khmer, Reimbursement for medical expenses in the amount of USD 10,000 and Compensation for mental illness in the amount of USD 5,000 Duong Hemalis' civil lawsuit under Article 355 of the Code of Criminal Procedure.
It should be noted that on January 22, 2021, at 9:00 AM, the victim, Duong Hemalis, 41 years old, and Soy Chansoeun drove together to the Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie with Soy Chansoeun as the driver. As they approached the Takhmao roundabout, Soy Chansoeun and Duong Hemalis argued.
After leaving the hospital, Duong Hemalis came to file a complaint with the Kampong Speu Provincial Prosecutor for legal action.
In addition to the case in Kampong Speu, the two-star former military officer also has a case at the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, in which two people were charged with "using violence against a real estate occupant in good faith and defamation."
Judge Theam Chanpiseth sentenced Soy Chansoeun to one year in prison for this crime. According to the victim's complaint, another accomplice, Sobin La, was also convicted and ordered to jointly reimburse the civil party 10 million riels. Meanwhile, Thi So Channa was fined 1 million riel for defamation.
Please be informed that on February 25, 2022, the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, which has Mr. Theam Chanpiseth as the trial judge, also announced the conviction of two defendants, one of whom is a two-star ex-military officer at the Ministry of National Defense. Soy Chansoeun and another accomplice were involved in a defamation suit committed during 2020.
According to the judge's decision, two-star veteran Soy Chansoeun was sentenced to eight months in prison and 20 million riels in compensation, while another accomplice, Sopin La, was also given 20 million riels in compensation. Also.
The two defendants are:
* First name: Soy Chansoeun, male, 45 years old, a former 2-star military officer, residing at 310E, Monivong Blvd., Sangkat Chaktomuk, Khan Daun Penh, Phnom Penh (currently detained in Kampong Speu Provincial Prison) * Second: Name: So Bin La, Male, 43 years old, Residence: No house number, Concrete street, Tnot Chrum 3 village, Sangkat Boeung Tumpun, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh.
The two defendants were charged by the prosecution with "defamation" committed in Phnom Penh during 2020, which is punishable under Articles 311 and 312 of the Penal Code. Party Committee of the Ministry of Mines and Energy issues a petition in support of the CPP statement and measures and condemns the Candlelight Party, which has seriously damaged the CPP's dignity.
