Preah Vihear Province Launches "Fire Truck" Campaign to Reduce Traffic Accidents
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Kim Rithy, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, on the morning of January 19, 2023, in collaboration with the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, Preah Vihear Province, Provincial Police, Provincial Police Departments and 8 municipal and district authorities launched a bulldozer campaign. There are lights to reduce traffic accidents and distribute lighting to municipal and district authorities to continue to close the bulldozers at their local level.
Mr. Kim Rithy said that the fire truck campaign that is being held now is to reduce traffic accidents caused by trucks driving on the road without traffic lights. The current campaign is a campaign to promote and educate you to participate in the implementation of everyone, which lasts for 3 months, starting from the opening day of this campaign.
In the second stage, if you refuse to turn on the traffic lights, the traffic enforcement officers as well as the authorities have the authority to stop the trucks and keep them when you drive on the road until the trucks have traffic lights to allow traffic. Yes.
He said that in the first phase of the campaign, he received funds to buy truck lighting from the fundraiser of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia in Preah Vihear province, with each city-district received 100 cars and each truck has a number of lights. 4 A total of 2,400 lights and bulbs.
Meanwhile, the Governor of Preah Vihear Province instructed the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia to cooperate with the municipal authorities, district inspectors, administrative posts to equip people who have bulldozers driving on the road, as well as to equip them in a special location. In the commune hall. The authority shall provide a report on the activities of the working group on the implementation of the lighting campaign to the provincial administration to summarize the results.
According to the report of the 8 municipal authorities, there are a total of 20,000 bulldozers. In the second phase, Mr. Kim Rithy will buy more lighting to provide to people in each city-district will receive 1,000 cars.
