(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police, on behalf of General Neth Savoeun, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police, presided over the closing ceremony of the first private security agency training course on January 19, 2023. 45 of the Department of Private Security Management.
Speaking on the occasion, Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi said that the General Commission of the National Police, which has the Department of Private Security Management as its staff, has been taking care to ensure that all private security agencies have the ability to know the profession and ethics in order to Promote this sector for continuous growth.
In addition, Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi assigned some important tasks to the private security agencies after completing the training, including:
* First: Request private security agents to have the appropriate attitude to participate in the work by adhering to what is right after receiving training to respect the qualifications of private security agents: must have discipline, ethics, use of security uniforms Private and adequate facilities.
* Second: To establish cooperation with the authorities and local authorities: good citizens and good people, an important support force to the competent authorities, good cooperation, timely response.
When they see or suspect any illegal activity, whether in their standing position or where, they must immediately report to the competent authority or to the department directly through the telephone number or to jointly prevent and suppress Offenses were timely.
* Third: Jointly participate in the implementation of the policy of the Royal Government, especially the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats.
* Fourth: Directors of private security companies and institutions (continue to support the training) by sending private security agents to attend the course.
* Fifth: All participants must apply the knowledge gained from this study and continue to expand their knowledge, intelligence, creativity and high responsibility in fulfilling their roles.
According to the report of Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, Director of the Department of Private Security Management, the 45th Private Security Agency Training Course was held for 2 days from 18 to 19 January 2023 with 159 participants. (2 females), of which 62 private security agents provide services (1 female) from 52 companies and 97 private security agents do not provide services (1 female) from 25 enterprises.
He emphasized that the training was aimed at meeting the need to increase the capacity to become a qualified and qualified private security agent for participation in the maintenance and protection of security, safety, order and security. The lives of the people as well as improve the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats.
