During the meeting, the two sides also agreed in principle to conclude the third round of talks in the United Arab Emirates in February 2023 and plans to formally conclude in March in Phnom Penh, when the Minister of International Trade of the United Arab Emirates will come. Visit to Cambodia.
Mr. Pan Sosak stressed that the entry into force of the Cambodia-UAE Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement will boost economic growth through market diversification, opening up more markets for goods and services, and increasing investment flows. Job creation and expansion of cooperation in other areas, as well as mutually beneficial mutual benefits.
On that occasion, Mr. Pan Sosak congratulated the United Arab Emirates Government on being selected to host the 13th WTO Ministerial Conference in 2024.
