National Bank of Cambodia: Use of e-wallet accounts to reach 17.9 million accounts by 2022
This was stated by Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, on the occasion of attending the opening ceremony of the meeting to review the work results for 2022 and the work direction for 2023 of the National Bank of Cambodia on January 19, 2023.
Chea Chanto said that since the 19th Kovid Crisis, online commerce has grown rapidly and electronic payments have become more popular across the country, with 19.6 million mobile phones and Internet users growing. 18 million people.
He added that currently, the Cambodian payment system, especially the Bakong and KHQR (KHQR) system, has facilitated cross-bank and financial institutional payments, boosted the financial environment, and raised the profile of the Cambodian payment system on the international stage for innovation. And high innovation.
"The use of e-wallet accounts has increased significantly, reaching 17.9 million accounts. In addition, payment system connectivity with other countries in the region has been steadily promoted," he said. "The height of trade, investment, tourism and remittances."
The National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) has focused on cybercrime hedging through regular monitoring of payment system operations, enforcement of relevant regulations, and inspections of payment service providers.
Three financial associations have issued a code of conduct for banking and financial institutions to be fully implemented.
(Phnom Penh): The Banking Association of Cambodia, the Cambodian Microfinance Association and the Federation of Finance and Technology of Cambodia have officially announced the full implementation of the Code of Conduct for banking and financial institutions.
The implementation comes after the provisional code was announced in March 2022.
On January 18, 2023, the Association of Banks in Cambodia, the Association of Microfinance of Cambodia and the Association of the Federation of Finance and Technology of Cambodia organized a workshop to orient and strengthen the implementation of the Code of Conduct for banking and financial institutions under the participation of Mr. Kith Sovannarith, Deputy Director General of the First Inspection of the National Bank of Cambodia.
Mr. Kith Sovannarith commended the Banking Association of Cambodia, the Cambodian Microfinance Association and the Federation of Finance and Technology of Cambodia for initiating and implementing the Code of Conduct for Banking and Financial Institutions and the Credit Rules as a key achievement for maintaining the stability of the banking system. And strengthen public trust.
He added that member institutions that strive to adhere to the principles of the Code of Conduct and Credit Rules are also necessary to jointly maintain the provision of the Code of Conduct, professional ethics, responsibility and consideration of rights and interests. Of users.
Mr. Kith Sovannarith added that maintaining the stability and sustainability of the development of the banking and financial sector, as well as strengthening the implementation of marketing principles and consumer protection of financial services, requires the implementation of marketing principles and consumer protection. Financial services require the involvement of the National Bank of Cambodia and the private banking sector.
Mr. Sovannarith stated, "I urge financial institutions to continue to promote the protection of financial services users and to consider this work as a priority and important, as well as to ensure that their institutions operate and compete with customers ethically." Professionalism and responsibility. ”
Mr. Sovannarith added that the implementation of the Code of Conduct for Banking and Financial Institutions and Credit Rules is a platform to help all banking and financial institutions to better understand all the principles of the Code of Conduct and Credit Rules and have the opportunity to raise And discuss the challenges encountered after the temporary implementation of the Code of Conduct and Credit Rules.
Raymond Sia, Chairman of the Board, said that in the field of banking and finance, the attitude and activities of each institution are very important, which is the foundation to build integrity and trust with customers and the public.
It should be noted that the Code of Conduct for Banking and Financial Institutions has been initiated and implemented in line with the National Strategy on the Financial Environment 2019-2025 to ensure the sustainable development of the banking and financial sector, resilience, promotion and Strengthen consumer protection and improve ethics and professionalism for banking and financial institutions.
Mr. Sok Voeun, Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Cambodian Microfinance Association, stated that after the Code of Conduct has been on trial for almost a year, the Cambodian Microfinance Association has disseminated and strengthened the implementation of the Code through regional workshops organized. By the Cambodian Microfinance Association for Financial Services Providers on Strengthening Branch Management Efficiency, Sustainability, Ethics and Professionalism.
The workshop, organized by all MFIs, was attended by the regional leaders of about 800 Cambodian MFI members across the country.
