Cattle vaccination campaign for farmers in Santuk district, Kampong Thom province
(Kampong Thom): The working group of the Provincial Production and Veterinary Office led by Mr. Chan Panhavan, Director of the Production and Veterinary Office of Kampong Thom Province and the office staff on the morning of January 19, 2023, led the Village Animal Health Agency to launch a vaccination campaign. Crab firewood for farmers in North Chambok village, Tang Krasaing commune, Santuk district, Kampong Thom province.
The campaign was co-sponsored by Santuk District Governor Long Kiseng, as well as officials from the Santuk District Office of Agriculture, Natural Resources and Environment in charge of animal health and local authorities.
Mr. Long Kiseng also mentioned the importance of launching the cattle foot-and-mouth disease vaccination campaign. The vaccine protects against this disease.
Mr. Chan Panhavan reported that the team decided to inject a total of 200 animals. The team from the Office of Production and Veterinary has provided some veterinary equipment, medicine and foot-and-mouth vaccine to district agriculture officials, especially village animal health agencies, to intervene to their local farmers.
It should be noted that the team also continued to conduct biosecurity spraying in Santuk district slaughterhouse to prevent the spread of various diseases to other animals in the area.
Tourism business owners in Phnom Penh need to improve service quality to be ready to receive millions of guests during the SEA Games
(Phnom Penh): In order to be ready to receive and provide services to tourists during the SEA Games, the Phnom Penh Municipal Authority has advised the owners of tourism businesses such as restaurants, canteens, accommodation and adult entertainment businesses to improve the quality of hotel and hospitality services. Better hygiene from now on.
On that occasion, Mr. Huot Hay, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, called on the owners of restaurants, canteens, accommodation and entertainment businesses for adults to pay close attention and properly implement the laws and regulations in force for their own safety. And public welfare.
He said that Cambodia will host the 32nd SEA Games and the 12th ASEAN Para Games in May 2023. By then, athletes, coaches, commissions, along with millions of spectators and spectators. Many people will come to stay, eat and visit in Phnom Penh. Therefore, all tourism businesses need to improve the quality of hotel services and sanitation from now on.
Deputy Governor Huot Hay emphasized that improving the quality of the above services also enhances the image of Cambodia in the SEA Games.
He also called for attention to be paid to the garbage issue as instructed, to be properly packaged and released on time. He said that garbage should be divided into two types: wet garbage means garbage from the kitchen, food waste to be stored in black bags and dry garbage to be stored in white bags.
Meanwhile, Mr. Ley Sopheap, President of the Federation of Investors of Cambodia and President of the Federation of Tourism and Hospitality of Cambodia, said that the association is currently increasing the dissemination of food safety law (vegetables, fruits, fish, meat ...) and related documents of the Ministry. Health, Ministry of Tourism, Commission for the Suppression of Counterfeit Products, etc. He called for such a comprehensive and in-depth implementation.
Mr. Ley Sopheap also promoted professional training in food and beverage safety, hospitality and accommodation services to promote the improvement of hotel and sanitation services and to be ready to receive and provide services to tourists during the event. Sea Games.
NBC: The banking system plays an active role in supporting economic recovery and maintaining financial stability
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that the Cambodian banking system has maintained strong stability and has played an active role in supporting economic recovery and maintaining financial stability.
Mr. Chea Chanto's remarks were made on the occasion of the opening of the meeting to review the work results for 2022 and the work direction for 2023 of the National Bank of Cambodia on January 19, 2023.
Chea Chanto said the reserve requirement rate was kept low to provide liquidity to banking and financial institutions for lending and liquidity management.
He said credit restructuring had helped streamline operations as well as the survival of businesses and alleviated people's difficulty in repaying when incomes plummeted. Credit restructuring is allowed until mid-2022 as the economy recovers, while the amount of credit restructuring has rapidly decreased from 12.7% to 6% of the total portfolio.
In addition, the National Bank of Cambodia has allowed credit restructuring for flood-affected people. Completion of the credit restructuring program is part of the implementation of a crisis exit strategy that is implemented in accordance with the actual situation.
Rising interest rates on international markets, as a source of capital for the Cambodian banking system, have also resulted in a slight increase in interest rates in Cambodia. In the past, high levels of liquidity have helped banking and financial institutions manage the pressure of rising interest rates, but if international interest rates rise further, they could also lead to higher interest rates in Cambodia.
Mr. Chea Chanto praised the banking and financial institutions that have contributed to the implementation of the Royal Government's policy to mitigate the impact of the Kovid 19 crisis in the past and not to raise interest rates at the rate of interest rate growth. International market.
He said that with the support of credit growth to the private sector, financial literacy and consumer protection are also priorities to strengthen the responsible use of credit and maximize the benefits of the financial sector to improve livelihoods. Of the people.
He added that the financial environment has also been gradually improved, reflecting the growing number of financial services users who are more diverse and ubiquitous. According to a 2021 UNCDF report, Cambodia's financial environment is moderate, with 67% of the adult population using formal financial services, while the rate of non-formal financial services is about 3%, down from 12%. % Compared to 2015.
However, in a situation where the economy is facing uncertainty, high credit growth remains a major risk to the banking system, especially as corporate and household debt levels have risen due to the Kovid-19 crisis.
