Japanese doctors encourage regular eye examinations to avoid serious problems
(Phnom Penh): The eye is an important organ for people's daily lives that requires attention, care and regular check-ups to avoid problems, especially for children.
Ophthalmologists from Japan recommend regular eye examinations to keep your eyes healthy and to avoid serious problems.
The doctor shared his experience in Japan that children in Japan are highly concerned about eye health. Children in Japan have their eyes checked at school every four months, and medical records are kept to check for any changes in the future.
A Japanese doctor said that a proper eye examination is essential before undergoing any eye surgery. Based on the results of the examination, the specialist will be able to easily diagnose and develop a proper treatment plan.
The doctor suggested that the examination and monitoring of the child's eyesight is very important. Therefore, the doctor calls on all parents to bring their children to check their eyes and vision regularly and to protect the eyes of children.
For doctors, early and accurate detection of eye problems can help prevent and treat eye problems and diseases in a timely manner to maintain a comfortable quality of life. Therefore, solving the eye problems of the Cambodian people is a special mission for the leaders of the Japanese Eye Hospital who are present in Cambodia.
Dr. Manabe graduated from the Japanese Medical University in 1986 with a PhD in Laser.
