Landmine Victims in Battambang Province's Koas Kralor District Expect Safe Farming After Demining Team
(Battambang): People affected by unexploded ordnance in Prey Toteung village, Chhnal Moan commune, Koas Kralor district, Battambang province have expressed their expectation to engage in agriculture without worries after demining experts deal with demining and unexploded ordnance. Explosion from farmland already.
Mao Man, 52, said with a sad face that he had been paralyzed since 1980 by a landmine in Pailin province.
He said he was saddened by the landmines, which left him paralyzed and unable to go to work other than working on a small farm, earning enough money to support his family.
Mr. Mao Man stated that once the demining team has completed the demining work of the people's agricultural land as well as his land, he will be able to farm without having to worry about landmines. Will expand more farmland.
Nop Theavy, 48, also called on the Royal Government to expedite the clearance of landmines left over from the war in Cambodia to make it easier for people to engage in agriculture. Going forward.
