(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance in early January 2023 issued a Prakas on Rules and Procedures for Implementing Tax Obligations for Business Gambling Enterprises, a New Mechanism for Implementing Tax Revenue in the Gambling Business. These include casinos, gambling, gambling, fortune-telling and other commercial games.
The Prakas of the Ministry of Economy explains in detail the procedure for calculating and tax rate for applying tax obligations to enterprises engaged in gambling business.
Speaking on January 19, 2023, Mr. Kong Vibol, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Taxation, confirmed that the General Department of Taxation will implement a new mechanism to collect tax revenue on gambling (casino) in This 2023 and expect that this new mechanism will help to get more tax revenue.
He said that in the past, the government has set a non-tax revenue for the gambling sector, which sets the annual package revenue paid through the Cambodian Gambling Management Commission of the Ministry of Economy, but for the mechanism of the economic declaration is required. The gambling business is also subject to tax obligations, no longer subject to subcontracting.
He added that before preparing the Prakas on the rules and procedures for applying tax obligations to businesses, the General Department of Taxation has conducted a lot of research from countries such as Singapore, Malaysia, Korea and Australia to determine the type of tax is not complicated. There is a 20% income tax and value added tax (VAT).
However, Kong Vibol has not yet been able to estimate the amount of tax revenue that will be received from the gambling industry, but he only claims that he can get a lot of revenue.
