On January 18, 2023, the Minister of Foreign Affairs of Japan, Mr. Hayashi Yoshimasa, announced the appointment of Ms. Mina Miniyoko as a singer and goodwill ambassador for the 70th Anniversary of Japan-Cambodia Friendship. This appointment is from January 18 to December 31, 2023 in order to further promote exchanges between Japan and Cambodia due to the 70th anniversary of Japan-Cambodia friendship.
According to the Facebook page of the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia, Ms. Mina Miniyoko paid a courtesy call on Japanese Foreign Minister Hayashi Yoshimasa (Japanese Deputy Foreign Minister Taki Ishizuki was also present).
"I came to Cambodia in 1989 and 2013 and since then I have had a special feeling for Cambodia. I am very happy to be a goodwill ambassador in the year of the anniversary," said Mina Minoyoko. 70 of the friendship between Japan and Cambodia, which is a special country for me.
In addition, Ms. Mina Minoyoko stated that she will continue to do various activities to make the Cambodian people understand Japan and the Japanese people also understand Cambodia. "This year, I really look forward to coming to Cambodia and meeting the Cambodian people again."
Please be informed that Ms. Mina Minuyoko and her team have prepared the song "Rainbow to Tomorrow" especially for the "Kizuna Festival 2022" and the 70th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between Japan and Cambodia in 2023.
The song "Rainbow to Tomorrow" is a song written to express the deep feelings of the friendship between a famous Japanese singer and the people of Cambodia when the singer came. Play in Cambodia since Cambodia was in poverty due to the civil war crisis.
Through the song "Rainbow to Tomorrow", Mina Minuyoko recalls her memories of traveling to Cambodia in 1989, when Cambodia was in a state of crisis, war and the economy was not yet developed. She traveled to the orphanage and did some activities to help the orphanage.
