Xi Jinping expresses concern over 19 cases of Kovid infection in rural areas during Chinese New Year
BEIJING (Reuters) - Chinese President Xi Jinping has said he is concerned about the situation of 19 cases of Kovid in rural China as millions of people travel to their hometowns ahead of the Lunar New Year celebrations. Coming soon. This is according to the publication by the AFP news agency on Thursday, January 19, 2023.
On the eve of the holiday, the Chinese leader told local officials of his main concerns about the situation in rural areas and residents after China adjusted its response to Kovid 19. Xi stressed efforts to improve medical care for the most vulnerable, including addressing shortages in preventing and controlling rural outbreaks.
China closed the Zero-Kovid 19 policy in December 2022 and will reopen its full border in early 2023. Travel or return home of Chinese people during the Lunar New Year is expected to lead to the spread of Kovid 19 to rural areas under improving living conditions. Still.
