(Phnom Penh): The Cambodia Securities Exchange on January 19, 2023 held a ceremony "Official listing of green bonds of Golden Tree". The official green bond sale ceremony was presided over by Dr. Hean Sahip, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Cambodia Securities Exchange.
The event was also attended by Mr. Sou Socheat, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Securities Regulator of Cambodia, Mr. Hong Sohour, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Cambodia Securities Exchange, Mr. Kuy Vat, Chairman of the Board of Directors of Golden Company. Mr. and Mrs. representatives of ministries, institutions and the private sector, as well as many national and international guests.
Mr. Oum Serey Ratanak, Deputy Chief Executive Officer - Chief Financial Officer of Golden Trinity, said that the issuance of green bonds not only allows the company to obtain the necessary capital to expand its business and increase the confidence of local and international investors. Not only on the company's business, but also contributed to the expansion of the potential of the securities sector in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Mr. Hong Sochua pointed out that Golden Trinity Company has successfully issued and listed green bonds for a total amount of about 6 billion riels (approximately $ 1.5 million) with a coupon rate of 7% in One year and 5 years credit.
He pointed out that, including the green bonds issued today, the Cambodia Securities Exchange has registered 18 companies, including: 9 listed companies and 9 bond companies. These 18 listings raised a total of $ 317 million from the Cambodia Securities Exchange.
Along with the increase in the number of listed companies, the volume and volume of daily average stock trading has also increased steadily. In fact, in 2022, the average daily trading volume increased to about $ 500,000 and the number of trading accounts increased to 36,000 accounts.
