(Phnom Penh): HLH Aggregate (Cambodia) Limited, a Singaporean company that is investing in agriculture in Kampong Speu province's Oral district, has announced that it will provide land for cassava cultivation and will repurchase it for about $ 60 per tonne.
LHH Agricultural Co., Ltd. (Cambodia) Limited and Hong Lai Huot Group Limited, a Singapore-based company that has invested in Cambodia for many years, have established the Cambodia-Singapore Agricultural Center (CSAH) on an area of approximately 10,000 hectares. In Oral district, Kampong Speu province, to concentrate mixed investment in agriculture, such as food processing, animal husbandry, commercial space and solar plantations.
Dylan Ong, CEO and General Manager of the Singapore-based company, said that in order to promote the full potential of the government-invested land, the company has opened up opportunities for local investors to follow the cassava. The company will buy back the land for $ 60 per ton.
Please be informed that LHL Aggregator (Cambodia) Limited has been licensed and invested in the above land since 2008. The company has now set up a clearing system to clear the forest, so there are no obstacles for cultivation on this land. When harvested, it is transported to a processing plant in the area.
In addition to growing cassava, the company also receives agricultural investments in other sectors, such as vegetable growing and animal husbandry.
Those who wish to invest in growing cassava, vegetables and raising livestock in the above land location can contact for information by calling 099 829 545 and 015222202.
