(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ly Chantola, President of the Bar Association of the Kingdom of Cambodia, on January 18, 2023, assigned the Department of Defense of the Poor to visit and defend two victims, a couple who were hit by a truck. Thom Bok caused injuries and became paralyzed in Battambang province, but has not received any compensation so far, almost a year ago.
It should be noted that Mr. Ly Chantola, a lawyer, has launched a policy on consultation and protection of the poor for a fee, dated February 5, 2021.
Immediately after being assigned, a delegation from the Bar Association of Battambang Court visited the two victims, a couple living in Kon Damrey Village, Sangkat Nimit, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province, to be their legal lawyers after the accident. A traffic accident on February 26, 2022 in Battambang province until he became disabled.
It should be noted that two mercenaries driving a couple were hit by a Hyundai truck and suffered serious injuries. They have not been treated for almost a year and have not yet received compensation. From the driver yet.
With the difficult situation for their livelihood due to disability, the two victims would like to urge the Battambang Provincial Court to expedite the case to receive compensation for treatment of injuries and illnesses, as well as to solve their daily lives. It is impossible.
Mr. Van Pov, 38 years old, and his wife Saing Saran, 29 years old, resident of Kon Damrey Village, Sangkat Nimit, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province, described that they were the victims last night at 8:15 pm on February 26, 2022 They are mercenaries driving a green Hyundai brand truck with license plate Phnom Penh 3D-4776 driving on National Road 59 from south to north.
At the scene in Samrong village, O'Romduol commune, Phnom Preuk district, Battambang province, a blue Hyundai car with license plate Phnom Penh 4A-2376, owned by Nhep Soksan, was traveling from north to south in the opposite direction and crashed. Their car was driving across the normal right lane.
Saing Saran's wife stated that after the incident, her husband Van Pov, who was trapped in the car, was seriously injured and was pulled out by the locals to remove the car door. The windshield fell to the ground but suffered minor injuries.
Ms. Saing Saran added that after arriving at the hospital, her husband fainted and suffered serious injuries. His leg was broken and his hip was broken. Still unable to do anything, even standing up was difficult.
