Ministry of Tourism promotes smoke-free tourism by establishing a smoke-free tourism city
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism has set guidelines for the establishment of a smoke-free tourism city in order to improve the implementation of a smoke-free environment in tourism and protect tourism from the effects of tobacco use, as well as additional Benefits to tourism. This was confirmed by Mr. Hor Sarun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism on January 17, 2023.
Mr. Hor Sarun added that the Ministry of Tourism is taking into account the impact of the use of tobacco products, especially in the tourism sector, and has done a lot of work to reduce this impact on health, economy, society and the environment by building the sector. A smoke-free tour.
He added that in the past, the Ministry of Tourism has disseminated and raised awareness of laws and regulations related to the control of tobacco products among tourism businesses and encouraged all to participate in the implementation. The Ministry of Tourism has also presented awards and commendations to tourism service businesses that have excelled in implementing a smoke-free environment.
The implementation of a smoke-free environment in tourism is done in accordance with the minimum standard operating procedures on the implementation of a smoke-free environment in tourism, which aims to encourage tourism service businesses to comply with the law on tobacco control and Eliminate smoking or use of tobacco products where prohibited by law.
Mr. Hor Sarun also stated that the introduction of guidelines on the establishment of a smoke-free tourism city will strengthen the implementation of minimum standard operating procedures on the implementation of a smoke-free environment in tourism, as well as facilitate the participation of Municipal, district and Khan administrations to promote the implementation of smoke-free environment in tourism to ensure Cambodia is a safe, clean and green tourism destination.
He asserted that the effects of tobacco use were being taken into account by all stakeholders, both in the country and in the region, as they were so large that they were not only harmful to health. Not only that, but it also causes economic losses, creates social burdens and harms the environment.
Neak Oknha stated that the project to build Koh Rong International Airport has been strongly encouraged and supported by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, in line with his policy of peace and development.
Koh Rong International Ecotourism Airport is scheduled to be built soon, taking five years.
Duke Kith Meng stated that construction on the island was two to three times more difficult and costly than on land due to transportation problems.
Neak Oknha Kith Meng stated, "I promise that I will make this airport in accordance with the master plan, according to the plan that we signed today, the memorandum of understanding for the policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen is that peace and Development.
Neak Oknha Kith Meng said that under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the head of the Royal Government, Samdech has set out an open policy to attract investors to create jobs for the people and raise the image of the country. Equal as other countries in ASEAN and the world.
Dr. Mao Havanal, Minister in charge of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, said that the airport to be built on Koh Rong is the fourth new international airport with private sector investment, after Darasakor International Airport, International Airport. Siem Reap-Angkor and Techo International Airport.
Dr. Mao Havanal said that this development project is within the framework of a multi-purpose joint venture for the whole of Koh Rong, which is a private sector investment and is similar to the investment of UDG (UDG). Also in Darasakor area (100% private investment for multi-purpose project development). On the other hand, this project is in line with the vision, plan, policy and strategic direction of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
He requested Royal Group to work closely with the Council for the Development of Cambodia, the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation and relevant ministries and agencies to obtain permits or licenses / certificates related to the above development projects. This.
Mr. Sin Chanserivutha, Undersecretary of State and Spokesman for the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, said that after the signing of the agreement, the Royal Group Koh Rong Development Company will start immediately, with no end in sight.
Mr. Sin Chanserivutha said that the construction of this airport to facilitate the travel of the tourism sector, and according to research, any tourist area with an airport is more developed than any tourist area without an airport.
Please be reminded that on February 28, 2008, Royal Group Co., Ltd. signed a lease agreement with Koh Rong Council with the Council for the Development of Cambodia, which is a party representing the Royal Government of Cambodia, to develop a business development area, eco-tourism resort, including airport infrastructure. Well.
Royal Group Co., Ltd. has invested in Koh Rong Development Zone, Koh Rong City, Sihanoukville Province, including:
* Red gravel road: The company has been transporting machinery to build roads and infrastructure in Koh Rong since July 6, 2009.
3-star hotel: The company built the 3-star Royal Soksan Hotel in 2013 with 153 rooms with an investment of 15 million US dollars.
5-star hotel: The company built the 5-star hotel Royal Sorn Koh Rong was built on December 12, 2015 with 63 villas connected by swimming pool with an investment of 40 million US dollars. The hotel was officially inaugurated on April 23, 2018 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Ame Concrete Road: On July 14, 2020, Royal Group Koh Rong Development Company signed an agreement to build a 70 km long, 8 m wide and 250 mm thick concrete road on Koh Rong at a cost of 35 investment. Million US dollars. Currently, about 50 km of concrete roads have been built.
