Pursuant to Prakas No. 7394 Prak of the Ministry of Interior dated 28 December 2022, it was decided to appoint 15 civil servants to the position of Deputy Governor of Pursat Province, including Mr. Sok Darasmey, the rank of Chief of Kramakar. Level 6 is the Deputy Governor of Krakor District Board of Governors and Mr. Leh Safirin, the rank of Senior Officer Level 4 of the Administrative Division is the Deputy Governor of Krakor District Board of Governors.
Mr. Khoy Rida, Governor of Pursat Province, instructed Mr. Sok Darasmey and Mr. Leh Safirin, who have just been appointed as Deputy Governors of Krakor District, to be honest with their subordinates and superiors, especially with the Royal Government, and to abide by their commitments. As during the announcement of the new position and asked the two of you to work hard to cooperate and strengthen solidarity with colleagues, relevant units and the three forces.
He would like to encourage the new district governor to continue his efforts to dedicate time, physical and mental strength by performing work based on the legal position as the main factor, especially to ensure the work of general administration, public service delivery, out-of-court dispute resolution. Works well to respond to the requests of local people with quality for Krakor district to grow even better.
Cracking down on sex massage parlor in Prek Pnov district, arrested a site owner and found 8 female victims
(Phnom Penh): The Anti-Human Trafficking and Juvenile Protection Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police has cooperated with local authorities in cracking down on aggravated prostitution, opening a massage parlor and arresting a sex worker. Eight victims, including three minors, and some exhibits.
Lieutenant Colonel Hak Ly, Director of the Office, said that the operation took place on the night of January 17, 2023, at the massage parlor brand "9999" located at a house with no number at the end of the Prek Pnov Bridge west of Vimean Chhnach Road, Lime Village. Sangkat Svay Pak, Khan Russey Keo.
The operation was carried out under the direction of Lt. Gen. Thet, Deputy Commissioner and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner, and Lt. Gen. Chan Kittikhom, Deputy Commissioner for Anti-Human Trafficking and Juvenile Protection of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police under the coordination of By Mr. Sith Vannak, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
