(Koh Kong): Families of relatives of veterans who lost their lives in the war in Koh Kong province have expressed their happiness over the construction of the Tomb of the Veterans in accordance with the merits they have sacrificed for the nation.
"Joining the government is to oppose the return of the Khmer Rouge and to keep Cambodia safe because three generations are miserable," Chhay said.
Mr. Pov Chhay recalled that during that time, he and his younger brother, who had lost their lives along with other fighters, were fighting with Khmer Rouge soldiers in various areas in Koh Kong province.
Mr. Pov Chhay expressed his feelings: "The loss of my brother's life is very sad, but I think in my mind what to do to protect the motherland, the territory must be like this, and I would like to thank you for raising this body as a grave, I thank you very much, Samdech "Considering the corpses of the fighters who built a clean cemetery, it is very good for my corpse. I am satisfied, I am happy to see it with my own eyes."
Mr. Pov Chhay said that Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen has made the people live in prosperity and have all the rights and freedoms far from the past.
Living with a hard-earned peace roof, this veteran of the bloody war between Cambodians and Cambodians called on the people, especially the younger generation of Cambodians, to do their part to maintain peace, political stability that exists today. Don't let it fall into the flames of war again.
On the other hand, another man whose father sacrificed his life for the nation when he had only seen the light of day for about 10 days described that his father sacrificed his life for the honor of contributing to the peace of the country. Until now.
"Before, I was searching for my father's body, but I did not know until now, only now did the commander here contact me. At that time, the land was marked as a small grave, but now I have come to see the government preparing the grave," he said. "Beautiful, I'm really happy."
Please be informed that the construction site of Koh Kong Province Veterans Tomb was opened on February 23, 2021 and officially inaugurated on January 17 yesterday under the presidency of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh. The Tomb of Warriors covers an area of nearly 1 hectare and is located in Village 3, Sangkat Smach Meanchey, Khemarak Phoumin City.
At the grave site, there were 448 corpses of female warriors from 18 capitals and provinces who were sacrificed between 1979 and 1998, one of whom was an official of Koh Kong Provincial Hall. In 2022, the bodies of five more unidentified fighters were recently found, bringing the total number of bodies buried at the site to 453. The state will use credit guarantee mechanisms to help tourism business owners get business restoration loans
(Phnom Penh): A senior official of the Ministry of Economy and Finance has stated that the Royal Government will use the Cambodian Credit Guarantee Corporation (CGCC) mechanism to support or assist non-mortgage tourism business owners to obtain loans for business rehabilitation. It is recovering from the devastating effects of the Kovid 19 crisis, while tourism restoration financing schemes are currently limited to small business owners.
He added that the Royal Government will continue to pay attention to tourism business owners to resume their business through state assistance and cooperation with banks and microfinance institutions to obtain loans for business recovery.
"The government is using the mechanism to guarantee this credit to the tourism sector, which we ask the bank to look at the practical feasibility and softness that can go together, so the tourism sector is being encouraged," he said. "Our open phase hopes our visitor returns to normal and gets a loan from a bank, even if he does not have collateral."
Regarding this case, Mr. Sok Voeun, President of the Cambodian Microfinance Association, believes that if the lending to business owners in the tourism sector is supported by the Credit Guarantee Corporation of Cambodia (CGCC), the chances of obtaining a loan will be higher.
As of the end of December 2022, the Credit Guarantee Corporation of Cambodia (CGCC) has provided $ 92 million in loan guarantees to 985 small and medium enterprises that are unable to access collateral. Loans for rehabilitation and expansion of businesses in and after the Kovid 19 epidemic. Lt. Gen. Meas Bunly: If you want to maintain peace and stability, please do not believe in the incitement of the traitors
(Koh Kong): Lt. Gen. Meas Bunly, Deputy Director General, Representative of General Chao Phearun, Director General of the General Department of Technical Equipment, Ministry of National Defense and Chairman of the Local Government Working Group, Botum Sakor District, Koh Kong Province, on January 18, 2023. Invited for the 44th anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day, Botum Sakor District, Koh Kong Province, with a total of more than 500 participants.
Mr. Krouch Borey Seiha, Governor of Botum Sakor District, said that peace, stability, people have full rights today because of January 7, 1979, the second birth of the people across the country and people across the country will never forget. Today's celebration is to express our feelings and gratitude and celebrate the 44th anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day, the second day of all Cambodians.
The district governor said that the 44th anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day this year was celebrated in a situation where Cambodia is developing well in all areas and is continuing to implement the fourth phase of the Royal Government's Rectangular Political and Strategic Program. The 6th legislature of the National Assembly in order to develop the country in all fields to ensure the advancement of the living goal of the people and democracy in Cambodia.
On that occasion, Lt. Gen. Meas Bunly confirmed that today is a special day that makes parents and siblings want to remember the 44th anniversary of the January 7 Victory (1979-2023) to show in the spirit of always remember. To the great merits of the heroic cadres of the Cambodian National Salvation Front who have made great sacrifices in the fight to overthrow the genocidal regime of Pol Pot and to protect the Cambodian resurrection.
He continued that the spirit of National Liberation Day is in the hearts of all people and a symbol of national unity and the great Khmer family is immortal under the shadow of peace forever. He said that January 7, 2023 is the 44th anniversary of the country being liberated and liberated from the Democratic Kampuchea regime or the so-called Khmer Rouge genocidal regime led by Pol Pot, which turned Cambodia into Black Killing Fields.
(Battambang): The pre- and postpartum waiting building of Sar Kheng Kamping Puoy Health Center in Anlong Svay Village, Ta Kream Commune, Banan District, Battambang Province, which cost $ 29,333, was officially inaugurated to improve public health.
The ceremony was held on the morning of January 18, 2023 under the presidency of Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Battambang Province, and was attended by leaders of provincial health departments, departments around the province, commune councils, Banan district administration officials, forces and people. Too many.
The prenatal and postnatal waiting building is 96 square meters (16 meters by 6 meters) with a total budget of $ 29,333 and the health promotion building is 72 square meters (12 meters by 6 meters), height 5.90 meters, height One tile floor costs a total of $ 25,105, which is a grant from the Government of the Republic of Korea through the Korea Foundation for International Health Care.
Mr. Sok Loo thanked the Government of the Republic of Korea through the Korea Foundation for International Health Care, a regular donor that has helped Battambang in all areas, especially health, for the well-being of people in urban and rural areas.
The provincial governor confirmed that this is another new achievement that we have received a new health center to provide health services to the people closest, easy to reduce difficulties and easy for them to run to the health center. Farther, closer and easier.
Mr. Sok Lou also called on all citizens to voluntarily be vaccinated with a stimulant dose to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 because the virus has not gone far from us yet.
Putin calls for end to EU Council statutes and human rights conventions for Russia (Video inside) (Moscow): Russian President Vladimir Putin has presented a draft law to parliament calling for an end to the EU Council statutes and conventions. Europe on the suppression of terrorism and the protection of human rights in relation to Russia. This is according to the publication by the Russian newspaper TASS on Wednesday, January 18, 2023.
On March 15, 2022, Russia announced its withdrawal from the European Union, and its membership ended on December 31, 2022. A day after Russia's withdrawal, the European Commission voted to remove the Russian network from its members.
Cambodia holds preparatory meeting to host Mekong Tourism Forum 2023 in late April in Sihanoukville
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, this morning, January 18, 2023, chaired a meeting to review plans and set out key work directions to prepare for hosting the Mekong Tourism Working Group Meeting. 51st and organized the Mekong Tourism Forum 2023, which is scheduled to be held from 24 to 28 April 2023 in Sihanoukville under the theme "Rethinking resilience and technology in tourism".
The preparatory meeting was also held at the Ministry of Tourism with the participation of Mr. Thong Rathsak, Director General of Tourism Development and International Cooperation, as well as the leadership of the Ministry of Tourism, the Sihanoukville Provincial Administrative Representative. Including private sector representatives.
Mr. Thong Rathsak emphasized that the Mekong Tourism Forum is a program within the framework of the Greater Mekong Subregion (GMS) Economic Cooperation, focusing on strengthening and enhancing state partnerships and Private Tourism (PPP) in the tourism sector aims to develop products and promote tourism promotion of the Greater Mekong Subregion to become a common destination and provide a new and unique experience for tourists.
He added that in addition, the program has organized three discussions, including: (1) smart tourism and smart tourism destinations through technology, (2) rethinking the food sector to protect the planet, and (3) Strengthening human capital for resilience in the tourism sector, with the participation of national and international facilitators and speakers from public, private and international institutions.
At the same time, through this meeting, Dr. Thong Khon also recommended important tips to prepare for this event, such as:
First, establish an inter-ministerial committee and sub-committee by clearly dividing the roles and responsibilities to ensure the safety, comfort and good hospitality of delegates, private sector speakers and national and international journalists.
Second: Organize a reception for the delegation of private sector speakers and national and international journalists at the international airport and the expressway to Sihanoukville and return.
Third: Approved the draft agenda of the 51st Mekong Tourism Working Group Meeting and organized the Mekong Tourism Forum 2023 from 24 to 28 April 2023 in Sihanoukville and organized a reception and banquet for Delegates, speakers from the private sector and national and international journalists.
Fourth, promote the dissemination of the above events more widely, both nationally and internationally.
(Pursat): In order to protect the well-being and food safety, especially in response to the requests of the people, the branch officials of Consumer Protection, Competition and Fraud Suppression in Pursat Province (KPR) cooperate with laboratory and Local authorities inspected 19 items at home near Samaki Krakor market in Pursat province without finding any chemicals.
The inspection of the goods at the back of the house was carried out on the morning of January 18, 2023 with the participation of HE Khoy Rida, Governor of Pursat Province, as well as the Deputy Governor and some provincial officials. More.
Mr. Ou Manrin, Head of Pursat Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud Branch (KPR) said that the inspection of goods in order to protect the interests and health of consumers focus on unsafe goods or Mixing banned chemicals.
In fact, the experts inspected the goods and took a mobile food test vehicle to do a preliminary test on the goods, including: dried fish, smoked fish, swollen fish, swollen fish, sausage, prahok, fish, frozen meat, fish, wine, medicine ... a total of 19 Sample. As a result, no chemicals were found in the 19 samples that could affect the health of the people.
On that occasion, Mr. Khoy Rida as well as professional officials also advised traders to avoid using chemicals on food products or food processing that endanger health and advise traders to be aware of hygiene.
