Ms. O Vandin warns against the prevention of communicable disease 19, alcohol and food poisoning during Chinese New Year and Khmer New Year
(Phnom Penh): Dr. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Chair of the Commission for the Prevention of Kovid 29 Vaccine, reminded all people to continue and increase their vigilance on the prevention of Kovid 19 and food poisoning. Alcohol poisoning during Chinese New Year and the upcoming Khmer New Year.
Through the social network Twitter on January 18, 2023, Ms. O Vandin asked the people to continue to implement 3 health measures to prevent and 3 not to be consistent, and to continue to be vaccinated against Kovid 19 in all doses. Base dose and boost dose (3rd dose, 4th dose, 5th dose, 6th dose and subsequent dose).
According to O Vandin, this practice is to protect oneself, one's family and one's community from the transmission of the Kovid 19 virus.
The health official also reminded people to take care of their health to avoid food poisoning and to avoid drinking alcohol that is not properly prepared and not to use methanol mixed with wine or drugs. Drunk mixed with other beverages that can cause poisoning or health hazards.
