Official announcement of the appointment of Dr. Mam Vandy as Advisor to the National Committee for Disaster Management
(Phnom Penh): Honorary General Dr. Kun Kim, Senior Minister, First Deputy Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, on the morning of January 18, 2023, was the High Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman. The National Committee for Disaster Management (NDMA) has officially appointed Dr. Mam Vandy as its Advisor to the National Committee for Disaster Management.
Dr. Mam Vandy was appointed by the King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, as an Advisor to the National Committee for Disaster Management on January 13, 2023.
The appointment was made at the request of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to provide an opportunity for Dr. to help in addition to disaster work. In the past, Dr. has been involved in social work and has been actively involved in disaster relief work and Jobs of Cambodian Veterans.
In today's inauguration ceremony, Dr. Mam Vandy is committed to his physical, mental, intellectual, knowledge and experience to contribute to the promotion and strengthening of disaster management in accordance with the Law on Disaster Management in Cambodia.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Kun Kim expressed his congratulations on the presence of Dr. Mam Vandy to assist in disaster management. Mr. Kun Kim said that the current disaster in Cambodia is more acute, which requires more forces to work together to solve the problem in time.
The Senior Minister considered the presence of Dr. Mam Vandy as a new impetus to respond to disaster management and respond better to the Royal Government and the affected people.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Kun Kim praised and appreciated the hard work, dedication and dedication of the leadership and civil servants at all levels of the National Committee for Disaster Management to achieve results. Proud. The senior minister said that this has really contributed to reducing disaster risk in Cambodia now and in the future.
