General Knowledge: Who was the first woman to travel to space?
Her passion for skydiving led to the Soviet space program intriguing her as the Soviets were trying to find astronauts to send them into space during the early 1960s. Another goal to achieve before the United States.
In February 1962, she was recruited along with three other paratroopers and one pilot to begin training to become astronauts.
In 1966, Tereshkova became a Member of Parliament for the Soviet Union and served as the Soviet Representative to many women's organizations and international events. She never traveled to space again. It was not until the 1980s that Soviet women astronauts returned to space.
