Oil tanker blast kills at least 3, injures dozens in central Thailand
BANGKOK: At least three people have been killed and dozens injured in a tanker accident in the central Thai province of Samut Songkhram, the Thai Ministry of Transport said. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Tuesday, January 17, 2023.
Authorities say the ship was carrying about 30,000 liters of fuel when it exploded.
In this horrific incident, 3 people were killed and at least 10 were injured. But the fire was completely extinguished as rescuers stepped up their search for the injured and missing.
The cause of the accident, authorities suspect, was that the ship, when repaired, was not properly cleaned and refueled. However, an investigation into the matter is ongoing and preliminary results will be announced within 10 days.
