Samdech Techo Hun Sen Leads a High-Level Delegation to Return to Cambodia After the Official Visit to the Maldives (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): At 3 pm on January 17, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Sen, led a high-level delegation to return to Cambodia after a fruitful official visit to the Republic of Maldives.
Please be reminded that Samdech Techo Hun Sen led a high-level delegation to visit the Maldives on January 15, 2023. This is Samdech Techo's first visit to the island nation, which is surrounded by beautiful seas, after Cambodia and the Maldives established diplomatic ties in 1995.
On January 16, Samdech Techo Hun Sen began his official visit. Samdech Techo's visit to this island paradise was warmly and warmly welcomed by the President of the Maldives, Ibrahim Mohammed Soli, and many other senior Maldivian government dignitaries. A long, bright red carpet.
During the official reception, the Prime Minister, accompanied by the President of the Maldives, paid homage to the flags of the two countries, including a traditional Maldivian art performance by a Maldivian student art group and seven artillery shells of the army. Maldives.
After the welcoming ceremony, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the President of the Maldives met to discuss the work. The working meeting was held at two levels: narrow level and bilateral level.
During the two-level meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the President of the Maldives discussed with a strong focus on strengthening and expanding cooperation between the two countries in all fields, including finding new ways to strengthen cooperation. Further operations in trade, investment, connectivity, health, culture, agriculture and human resource development.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the President of the Maldives also exchanged views on regional and international issues of mutual interest.
After the working meeting, the President of the Maldives organized a banquet in honor of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the delegation with great pleasure and closeness.
In the afternoon of the same day, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also had a courtesy call and discussed with the Vice President, the President of the National Assembly, the Minister of Foreign Affairs and the President of the Supreme Court of the Maldives.
It should be noted that Cambodia and the Maldives have established diplomatic ties since September 21, 1995, but the two countries do not yet have national embassies and trade and investment cooperation is still low. .
The Maldives, with an area of only 300 square kilometers, gained independence from the United Kingdom on July 26, 1965.
The country is located in the Indian Ocean, located in southwestern Sri Lanka and India and has a population of just over half a million, mostly Muslims, while Buddhism also has a history of reaching the island.
The Maldives is a country with a constitutional presidential system, with the president as head of state and head of government.
Before 1970, the country's main economy was agriculture, but now tourism is the main source of 28% of the country's GDP, but 90% of government revenue comes from taxes. Related to tourism and export-import.
Fisheries and aquaculture are also the main sources of the island nation's gross domestic product. It is a source of income that contributes about 15 percent of GDP and employs about 30 percent of the population.
