Kandal Provincial Court sentences woman hired to kill husband and murderer to life in prison for 'premeditated murder'
(Kandal): Investigating Judge of Kandal Provincial Court, Mr. Oeung Vanna, remanded in custody the woman who hired her husband to kill her husband for $ 1,000 and her hired killer after being charged by the prosecution. Cardinal.
Article 200 of the Penal Code "Premeditated Murder" Premeditated murder is an act of premeditated murder or by hiding. Forethought is a project developed before the harassment of the victim. Hiding is the act of watching over a person for a period of time in order to commit an act of harassment on the victim. Premeditated murder is punishable by life imprisonment.
Please be informed that a woman named San Thida, his wife, planned to hire an assassin for $ 1,000 to end her husband's life and then dumped her body in a canal in Kien Svay district, Kandal province. A few days later, the wife and the hired killer were jointly investigated by the joint police force of the Criminal Police Department, Phnom Penh and Kandal Provincial Police and cracked down on January 15, 2023.
According to the confession of San Thida (the victim's wife), she confessed that she had planned to kill her husband by hiring 33-year-old Thuok Ravi, a driver of a cement truck, living in Sambour village, Dangkor commune, Dangkor district. Phnom Penh, for $ 1,000, after preparing the project, on January 13, 2023, at 6:00 pm, he hid Thuk Ravi Chea in his house.
The reason for planning to kill her husband, according to his wife, Sun Thida, said that her husband, Khem Phally, left the house for two or three days before coming home late at night to find out about his wife. He also hired her for $ 1,000 to kill her husband.
