Please note that Samdech Techo Hun Sen is leading a high-level delegation to visit the Maldives. This is the first visit for Samdech Techo Hun Sen after Cambodia and the Maldives established diplomatic ties in 1995.
It should be noted that Cambodia and the Maldives established diplomatic relations on September 21, 1995. Since the establishment of diplomatic relations, the two countries, Cambodia and the Maldives, have had little contact with each other, including exchanges of official visits, bilateral trade and cultural ties.
The Maldives is an island nation in the Indian Ocean with an area of nearly 300 square kilometers and a population of over half a million. Maldives' gross domestic product will reach nearly $ 5 billion by 2020. National GDP per capita is nearly $ 9,000 for 2020.
The Maldives' economy is dependent on services for 78 percent, industry for 13 percent and agriculture for 8.8 percent. Exports were worth nearly $ 2 billion, and imports were worth $ 2.56 billion.
Tourism is the main economic sector, contributing about 28% of GDP. The Maldives reopened the country for international tourism on July 15, 2020. The Maldives is an island tourist destination that includes ecotourism along the coast, which is considered to be the number one most beautiful beach in the world.
In the first 11 months of 2022, the Maldives received nearly 1.5 million international tourists, an increase of 32.5 percent.
