The Ministry of Public Works and the World Bank Organize the Closing Ceremony of the 3rd Generation Training Course, the Opening Ceremony of the 4th Generation Training Course and a Lecture on Sharing Experiences of Leadership and Innovation Program
(Phnom Penh): Under the cooperation between the Ministry of Public Works and the World Bank, with the Royal School of Administration as the executive unit, the closing ceremony of the third generation training course and the opening ceremony of the fourth generation training course and a lecture to share experiences of the leadership program And Innovation was held on the morning of January 16, 2023 at Sokha Residence Hotel, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Youk Bunna stated that the main purpose of this training program is to provide knowledge support, skills development in human resource management, leadership and change management in the organization and organization in the workplace with good cooperation and Highly efficient, providing the necessary resources to meet the specific needs of civil servants who have a role at the management level in ministries and institutions at both the national and sub-national levels.
Afterwards, Minister Prum Sokha shared his work experience with the participants by presenting in the lecture on "Leadership and Innovation" with the main content of the first: leadership and innovation, the second. Democracy: Third: Public Administration Reform, Fourth: The Role of Government and Fifth: Conclusions.
Sharing knowledge and experience to today's participants, he presented the theory of connection and practice, as well as his own knowledge and experience of 43 years in public administration. Today's lecture will provide knowledge and experience. For all participants to be the basis of new thinking in the framework of leadership and management of the organization, as well as the provision of better public services.
On this occasion, the Minister thanked the World Bank, the European Union in Cambodia and the Australian Embassy in Cambodia for their cooperation with the Royal School of Administration and the Ministry of Public Works in organizing this training program to support and develop the capacity of senior officials. A key player in the field of key reforms within the policy framework of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
At the end of the program, Mr. Prum Sokha presented certificates to the trainees of the third generation Leadership and Innovation Course, which was successfully completed at the Royal School of Administration. Experts introduce a new type of fragrant rice variety "Champis 70", planted in a short time, weather resistant, helps farmers to benefit
(Phnom Penh): Rice seed research experts in Cambodia have introduced a new variety to Cambodian farmers called "Champis 70", a type of fragrant rice grown in a short time, resistant to weather, not seasonal, while this rice is being researched. And breeding for 9 years in Cambodia.
Mr. On Chhuon, Deputy Director of the Office of Botanical Selection of the Cambodian Agricultural Research and Development Institute (CARDI), a rice seed researcher, said that by the end of 2022, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries through the Cambodian Agricultural Research and Development Institute (CARDI) ) Has released a new rice variety called Champis 70d, a kind of fragrant light rice.
He said that according to experiments, the cultivation of this variety can get yields from 4 tons to 4.5 tons per hectare.
Although 70 varieties of Champis rice have not yet been produced for sale on the market, he encouraged farmers to choose this rice variety to grow because this new variety is weather resistant and insect resistant. Select the type of soil that is not seasonal and cultivate in a short time, which will allow farmers to reduce other costs such as fertilizer.
He believes that in the future, this new rice variety will be supported by consumers both in the country as well as the international market, because the variety provides standard rice that meets the needs of the international market.
He added, "Because this variety is fragrant and short-lived, it is hoped that farmers will be able to reduce production costs, such as pumping water and using less fertilizer than older varieties." Long-term, which makes farmers profitable. "As a researcher, I hope that this new rice will be able to penetrate the international market in the future because it is a variety that provides standard rice that meets the needs of the international market."
He said experts are now working to educate farmers and communities on the benefits of new rice varieties. Through the promotion and experimental cultivation, which has been received by farmers in the past, they have shown satisfaction and hope that from 2023, farmers will select this new variety to grow.
Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries Dith Tina said that despite some difficulties, CARDI was still able to develop a new rice variety that was good and important for farmers.
Please be informed that Champey 70 is a name that represents the 70th anniversary of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and Australia. The development of this rice variety was funded by two sources: the Cambodian government and partly supported by the Australian government.
General knowledge: Why are planets all round?
(Phnom Penh): You probably already know that the sun and the eight planets in our solar system are all round. What is the reason? The answer is due to the strong gravitational force of the mass of these large objects, which absorbs all their matter to the nucleus, which is the center. In particular, there are many small objects in our solar system that are not round because gravity is not strong enough.
