NEC Releases Information on Outreach Meeting with Re-Election Stakeholders to Elect Newly Established Municipal and District Councils
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) on January 16, 2023 issued a press release from a meeting with stakeholders on the re-election process to elect the city council and Newly created district.
The meeting was chaired by Mr. Nuth Sokhom, Deputy Chairman of the NEC and chaired the meeting to disseminate the calendar of the first election (re-election) to elect the Noble City Council, Sampov Poun Municipality, Kandal Province, Udong Province. May Chey, Samaki Monichey district of Kampong Speu province and O'Kreang Senchey district of Kratie province in 2023.
In a press release, Mr. Nut Sokhom stated that on December 23, 2022, the Royal Government issued four sub-decrees establishing Arey Ksat and Sampov Poun in Kandal province, establishing O'Kreang Sen Chey district of Kratie province and separating Udong district of Kampong Speu province is divided into two cities: Udong Mechey and Samaki Monichey.
He added that political parties registered in accordance with the Law on Political Parties at the Ministry of Interior have the right to register political parties to stand for election for the first election in order to elect the Noble City Council, Sampov Poun Municipality, Kandal Province, Udong Mechey District. Samaki Mony Chey of Kampong Speu Province and O'Kreang Sen Chey District of Kratie Province.
The registration of political parties and candidates will be held at the Election Commission of the relevant province from 19 to 23 January 2023.
Mr. Nuth Sokhom stated that the registration of political party agents to observe the election must be done at the Election Commission of the relevant province in accordance with the form set by the NEC. The registration of political party agents to observe the election is divided into two stages: the stage of registration of political party agents for election registration and the stage of registration of political party agents for election observation and counting. Ballots.
Minister of Agriculture: Research on new varieties must be based on economic efficiency
