He added that sustainability does not only refer to certain techniques, the biggest sustainability is economic sustainability. Suppose a variety of rice produces a high yield per hectare, but cultivation requires the use of fertilizers and expensive production costs, while that type of rice is unpopular and cheap.
He noted that at present, the production of seeds for domestic consumption is not enough, which he urged CARDI to produce enough seeds to meet market demand at an affordable price. At the same time, in addition to sufficient supply to the domestic market, he also wants to look at foreign markets to export rice seeds in addition to rice and paddy to be profitable and to strengthen the economic efficiency of Body.
At the same time, he urged CARDI to survive on its own, independent of the state budget, by producing rice seeds for sale directly to farmers, competing with other seed producers, as well as collaborating with foreign partners to export rice seeds. Go abroad.
