The cable-stayed bridge across the Tonle Sap to the Chroy Changvar Development Zone will be completed by early April.
(Phnom Penh): The construction site of the Russey Keo cable concrete bridge across the Tonle Sap River, parallel to the ballet bridge in front of the gas station in Russey Keo district, connected to the Chroy Changvar development area, Chroy Changvar district, reached the connection of the bridge on January 16, 2023 It is scheduled to be completed in early April 2023.
The ceremony to connect the concrete bridge across the Tonle Sap River was presided over by Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh and Duke Pung Kheav Se, as well as the participation of many officials under the administration of Phnom Penh.
Mr. Sam Piseth, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, confirmed that the construction site of the concrete bridge across the Tonle Sap River parallel to the ballet bridge in front of the gas station in Russey Keo district connected to the Chroy Changvar Development Zone, Chroy Changvar district as of January 16. Achieved 93% of the project and is scheduled to be completed in early April 2023.
It should be reminded that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of a concrete bridge parallel to this ballet bridge on October 23, 2017, and the bridge is scheduled to be completed in early April 2023. This face. Senior officials of the Ministry of Land Management promote the issuance of state land titles throughout Ratanakkiri province
(Rattanakiri): On January 16, 2023, Mr. Sor Sovann, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, and Mr. Van Sophea, Deputy Governor of Rattanakiri Province, held a meeting to promote the issuance of title deeds on state land in Rattanakiri Province.
Speaking on this occasion, Mr. Van Sophea said that in the past, the management of state property in Ratanakkiri province has not been fully organized because some departments, units and administrations of municipalities, districts, communes and sangkats have not yet been fully implemented in Inventory of state assets or increase or decrease of annual state assets in a timely manner as determined by the Royal Government's sub-decree.
He said that the registration of real estate and the application for a certificate of ownership of real estate is still delayed and many gaps due to some real estate in dispute or involving abusive occupants.
The Deputy Governor continued that after the meeting to promote the inventory of state assets in 2022, only 34 departments, units and sub-national administrations have made a list of increases and decreases of state assets in 2021. There are 592 real estate listings in Ratanakiri province, with 148 title deeds, equivalent to 25%, and 444 unlicensed plots, equivalent to 75%.
At the same time, he also urged the state land registration team to strive to perform their duties properly, accurately and quickly in accordance with the principles of the Royal Government.
