An agreement between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of the Republic of Maldives on visa waivers for holders of official and ordinary diplomatic passports was signed on the morning of 16 January 2023.
"I am pleased to see and reach a visa agreement between the two countries," said the Maldives President. "Maldives and Cambodians will be able to travel freely without a visa for 30 days."
According to the President, six agreements and memoranda of understanding between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Maldives were signed this morning, January 16, 2023, and he and Samdech Techo Hun Sen presided over, including:
* 1: Agreement between the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Government of the Republic of Maldives on visa waiver for holders of official and ordinary diplomatic passports.
* 2: Agreement between the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Government of the Republic of Maldives on Economic Cooperation.
* 3: Memorandum of Understanding on Bilateral Consultation between the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Maldives and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
* 4: Memorandum of Understanding between the Government of the Maldives and the Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia on Cooperation in Tourism.
* 5: Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Health of the Republic of Maldives and the Ministry of Health of the Kingdom of Cambodia on Cooperation in the Health Sector.
* 6: Memorandum of Understanding between the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and the National Chamber of Commerce and Industry of the Maldives.
