(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group in Preah Sihanouk Province, stated that not recognizing the January 7 Victory Day means loving the genocidal regime and war.
Mr. Say Sam Al's statement was made during his presidency of the celebration of the 44th anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day (1979-2023) in Sihanoukville on the morning of January 15, 2023. The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Senator, National Assembly Chairman, Deputy Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group, Municipalities, Districts, Communes, Sangkats, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province and nearly 1,000 people.
Mr. Say Sam Al said that January 7 Victory Day is not only a day to commemorate the day of national liberation and the people from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, but also a historical fact that warns Cambodians of all generations not to return. Step on this dark history again.
Mr. Say Sam Al added that the factors of peace, political stability and macroeconomic stability have led to significant changes in economic structure, for example, Cambodia has shifted from a complete reliance on agriculture and natural resources to focusing on industry and services. Etc. by creating a lot of jobs and improving the lives of the people.
He stressed that we have this day because we have national unity, the unity of the people of all walks of life, civil servants, the armed forces of all kinds who have united to maintain peace under the wise leadership of the heroic guide. Of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Sen.
