The Bangkok Post quoted Arkhom as saying the baht's appreciation was in line with capital inflows to the stock and bond markets, coupled with Thailand's healthy fiscal stability.
"Foreign investors are investing more in Thailand because they have confidence in our economy," Arkhom said. He said the baht's volatility was not a concern as the Bank of Thailand was monitoring the volatility.
