(Kandal): A woman planned to hire an assassin for $ 1,000 to end her husband's life and dumped her body in a canal in Kandal province's Kien Svay district. A few days later, the wife and the hired killer were jointly investigated by the joint police force of the Criminal Police Department, Phnom Penh and Kandal Provincial Police and cracked down on January 15, 2023.
At 12:20 AM on January 14, 2023, she opened the bedroom door for Thuk Ravi to kill her husband and came out of the room after Thuk Ravi acted. After killing her husband, Thuok Ravi put the body in a red-and-white cloth bag with red-and-black lizard eggs.
After that, San Thida and I drove a truck to transport Khem Phally's body and dumped it in a canal in Prek Dong village, Kampong Svay commune, Kien Svay district, Kandal province. I do not know what material is in the bag.
Please be reminded that in accordance with the order of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner, Lt. Gen. Nheng Chuor, Director of the Criminal Police Department, ordered Brigadier General Kheng Meng Chheang, Deputy Director of the Department to lead the specialized force in cooperation with the Phnom Penh Municipal Police and Kandal province to investigate and arrest the perpetrators.
Until noon on January 15, 2023, the Criminal Police Department arrested the perpetrator, Videl, who killed the victim for $ 1,000 from the victim's wife. Currently, the perpetrator and the victim's wife have been handed over to the Kandal Provincial Police for further action.
Phnom Penh Governor Inspects Unseasonal Flood Situation at Stung Prek Tnaot
(Phnom Penh): The Governor of Phnom Penh, Mr. Khuong Sreng, on the afternoon of January 15, 2023, led a professional officer to inspect the flood situation in Stung Prek Tnaot after several days of rain caused flooding and In part, it affected people's homes in Dangkor district.
Ms. Kim Nheb, Governor of Dangkor District, said that the unseasonal flood situation has affected more than 1,000 houses in 25 villages in 10 communes in Dangkor district, forcing all homeowners to leave for safety. Build temporary huts and tents.
Please be reminded that in relation to the situation of Stung Prek Tnaot, Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, assigned a team of professional officers to work day and night to prevent the flooding of Stung Prek Chhnot during the off-season floods due to Heavy rainfall in Stung Prek Tnaot basin in Kampong Speu province.
In fact, on January 13-14, the working group monitored and evaluated the flood situation of Stung Prek Tnaot in Kampong Speu, Kandal and Phnom Penh by taking practical measures day and night, which has been done so far. Water does not flow into the delta, only flooding along the estuary, which usually floods during floods.
