(Phnom Penh): Ms. Pheung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts, encouraged and encouraged Japanese producers to explore the possibility of creating investment opportunities in the film industry in Cambodia by using Cambodian territory for direct filming.
The remarks came after the Minister was invited to attend the 8th Japan Film Festival on January 14, 2023. The event was also attended by Ms. Toun Panha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and Mr. TANINAI Ichitomo, Acting Chargé d'Affaires of the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia.
Taking that opportunity, she praised and appreciated the efforts of the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia and the Phnom Penh Liaison Office of the Japan Foundation, which organized the above-mentioned General Assembly every year, especially in 2023 to celebrate the 70th anniversary of the establishment of relations. Diplomacy between Cambodia and Japan.
Ms. Phoeung Sakona continued, "The Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts considers the Japanese Film Festival as part of the celebration of the 70th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between the two countries, helping to promote and enhance bilateral relations between Cambodia and Japan." To be more cohesive, especially in the field of culture and fine arts.
She said that this event is not only a forum to promote Japanese films, but also a meeting place for Cambodian-Japanese producers and technicians to share experiences, explore strengths and weaknesses in terms of human resources, technology and create new investment opportunities. More in the film industry to contribute to the development of the film industry between the two countries.
"In this regard, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts and I personally would like to encourage and encourage Japanese producers to explore the possibility of creating investment opportunities in the film industry in Cambodia, especially the use of Cambodian territory as a venue for filming in accordance with the national policy on culture. Ms. Phoeung Sakona added.
In addition, he expressed his pleasure for the process of organizing the last eight Japanese film festivals, which have become part of the strengthening of Cambodian-Japanese relations, as well as make the Cambodian people learn more about Japanese culture. Through each story. In addition, stakeholders, including producers and film technicians of the two countries, also established good relations, sharing experiences and knowledge related to the film industry.
Dispute in the family of a woman who hired the killer to kill her husband and dumped the body in Kien Svay district, Kandal province, the perpetrator was arrested by the police
(Central): Starting a family dispute, a woman decided to hire an assassin for $ 1,000 to kill her husband and throw the body away, and the body was found floating on January 14, 2023 at Prek Dong Village, Kampong Svay Commune, Kien Svay District, Kandal Province.
According to the report, after the villagers found the body and reported it to the Kampong Svay Administrative Police Station, the police force immediately reported to the district and village authorities, commune, doctor to inspect the floating body. That. An autopsy found that the body had died of strangulation and shock (murder).
Brigadier General Kheng Meng Chheang, Deputy Director of the Criminal Police Department, told Fresh News on January 15, 2023 that immediately after receiving the information, the Department's forces cooperated with the Kandal Provincial Police to conduct a search.
As a result, special forces arrested San Thida, 34, the wife of Khem Phally, 33.
In front of the police, a woman named San Thida confessed that she had hired Vy, a 40-year-old construction worker, to kill her husband by shock and extortion for $ 1,000.
Pursuant to the order of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police, Lt. Gen. Nheng Chuor, Director of the Criminal Police Department, ordered Brigadier General Kheng Meng Chheang, Deputy Director of the Department, to cooperate with the Kandal Provincial Police to investigate the arrest. The perpetrators arrived.
Until noon on January 15, 2023, the Criminal Police Department arrested the perpetrator, Videl, who killed the victim for $ 1,000 from the victim's wife.
Currently, the perpetrator and the victim's wife have been handed over to the Kandal Provincial Police for further action. Cambodian real estate experts set up a public forum to provide knowledge to those planning to step into the real estate sector
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Association of Real Estate Professionals has set up a public forum to provide legal knowledge, standards and strategies to the public, especially those planning to step into this field.
The public forum was held on January 14, 2023 with the participation of many experts on "Resolving the Stalemate Real Estate Sales and Real Estate Technology".
Mr. Oknha Kheang Puthy, Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Cambodian Association of Real Estate Professionals, presented a lot of knowledge to the participants to prepare and become a successful business owner.
Mr. Oknha added that after the sharing program on "Solving the problem of stuck real estate sales and real estate technology in the current era" this time, we hope that the Association of Real Estate Professionals of Cambodia will continue to have more programs to share knowledge to Public.
Mr. Kang Sovantha, President of the Cambodian Association of Real Estate Professionals, said that the public forum organized by the Cambodian Association of Real Estate Professionals was aimed at sharing knowledge focusing on the real estate sector to the members of the association and the general public.
"For today's forum, it is very important to share laws such as business law, real estate tax law, marketing methods, market pricing, location to spend less, be profitable and have a good time," he said. Presenting technology on the work of the real estate sector as well.
Mr. Oum Saravuth, Advisor to the Technical Committee of the Association of Real Estate Professionals of Cambodia, said that for today's forum, he shared on the topic of rules and regulations for companies working in the real estate sector, tax obligations for real estate companies.
He added, "In general, business is inevitable to pay taxes, so in today's forum, I raised the obligation to pay taxes to all real estate companies that start a business, what are the obligations to pay? Apply for a license to any institution? "What are the monthly and annual obligations on the tax administration?"
He said that for today, the forum has spread the knowledge of tax law to all business people, so today's forum is really useful for those who want to learn more about the law, how to do business, etc. and ask the Cambodian Association of Real Estate Professionals. Continue to share knowledge to provide Cambodian businesses as well as the public to do business with the right rules and be successful.
Mr. TOU MENG, Sales Training Specialist of the Association of Real Estate Professionals of Cambodia, presented the tips for selling real estate, including factors such as: product factors to focus on location, quality, aesthetics, needs, benefits, prices, etc. Another factor is the agency. Sales need to know how to create, lead and maintain the team, build capacity, the team must have knowledge of real estate, how to find customers, how to deal with rejections in sales and how to close sales.
In addition, there was also the sharing of knowledge from many other speakers about the real estate sector in this public forum.
General Hing Bun Heang: The Peace Factor Creates a Convenient Environment for Investment and Building Achievements
(Central): Honorary General Hing Bun Heang, Deputy Director General of the Prime Minister's Cabinet, stated that the peace factor has created a conducive environment for investment and achievement.
He said this when representatives of Samdech Prime Minister Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit cut the roots of Preah Vihear and passed on the achievements of Wat Preah Vihear Bit Meas in Prek Sleng commune, Kandal Steung district, Kandal province on the morning of January 15, 2023.
