Official: Blood donation is a wonderful humanitarian act, hopefully more blood donors this year
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Khay Sokheng, Deputy Director of the Technical Office of the National Blood Transfusion Center of the Ministry of Health, said that donating blood is one of the best humanitarian acts that gives renewed hope to victims who need blood.
According to this official, in 2023, blood consumption will increase as every year. This is because the health sector is growing and the population is increasing year by year, which makes the demand for blood does not fall easily, so he hopes that this year people will donate more blood.
According to doctors, donating blood not only saves lives, but also provides health benefits, reducing the risk of cancer, lowering blood pressure and iron overload, which can affect the liver. And pancreas, helps improve heart health, reduce weight gain, stroke and make it fun too.
Dr. Khay Sokheng also confirmed that blood donation is done at the National Blood Transfusion Center every day. The National Blood Transfusion Center welcomes your voluntary blood donation.
He added that today's blood donation program is an urgent need to support and address anemia as well as to raise public awareness for the society and he will continue to create programs for this society. He stressed that red blood cells are formed automatically every 120 days, so we should donate blood better than leaving blood.
