(Banteay Meanchey): Mr. Sar Sokha, Deputy Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group for Banteay Meanchey Province and Initiator of Banteay Chhmar New Year Program, and Mr. Oum Rath, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, chaired a meeting with the provincial administration to prepare for the New Year program. Banteay Chhmar 2023 in the area of Banteay Chhmar temple in Banteay Chhmar commune, Thmor Puok district on the morning of January 14, 2023 yesterday.
According to Mr. Sar Sokha, the organization of the Banteay Chhmar New Year program aims to:
* First: Create an atmosphere for parents, youth and the public to celebrate the traditional Khmer New Year under the shadow of peace
* Second: As a great Khmer family, it is a contribution in return for the souls of the ancestors who sacrificed their lives for the nation, in return for leaving a beautiful traditional cultural heritage for future generations.
* Third: Remind and revive the Khmer Intangible Heritage on the site of the Intangible Heritage
* Fourth: Provide opportunities for young people, people, national and international tourists to learn more about the glory, richness of culture, civilization, customs, traditions, religions and continue to preserve this heritage and continue to expand national prestige on the international stage.
* Fifth: Demonstrate the culture and art of sharing the tenderness of the Cambodian people in helping each other like a brother.
* Sixth: Provide opportunities for traders, entrepreneurs, traders to participate in the exhibition of souvenirs and handicrafts that show the local cultural identity.
