The length of the river varies, with many scientists believing it to be at least 6,400 kilometers long. Compared to the Nile, it is still shorter than the Nile, while the Nile is considered to be 6,650 km long, the longest in the world. However, some claim that the length of the Amazon is longer than the Nile.
Many people find that measuring the length of the Amazon River accurately may be easy, but in reality it is not, despite modern equipment and technology.
The most important problem in determining the length of the Amazon River is determining the source of the river or headwaters and the endpoint or end of the river, which is the basic data for determining the length of an object, but there are differing opinions surrounding determining the starting point. Of the Amazon.
For the upper reaches of the Amazon River, Brazilian researchers have redefined the southern part of the island of Maracou, an additional 353 kilometers, as a new location, as opposed to the previous one. They also redefined the total length of the Amazon River to 6,992 kilometers.
Meanwhile, the length of the Nile has been redefined, with researchers finally concluding that the Nile has a total length of 6,853 km, up to 200 km longer. However, the Nile is still 145 km shorter than the Amazon, making it the longest river in the world.
Following the release of this decision, many people were skeptical of the new figures because the study by the Brazilian group was not widely disseminated. A hot tub.
Scientists still have many missions to explore and continue to describe other locations at the headwaters of the Amazon, the exact length of the Amazon is still unknown.
National team visits Krek commune: Providing study materials to poor students helps them avoid dropping out of school
