(Kandal): Due to continuous rain, the water of Stung Prek Tnaot River rises and flows strongly, causing a wooden bridge named Batachi in Batachi village, Sangkat Takdol, Takhmao city, completely collapsed, flowing along Stung Prek Tnaot and causing the bank Among the Chinese, Hong Zhi also entered the river.
Immediately, the Kandal Provincial Authority, led by Mr. Dim Bora, Deputy Governor, represented by Mr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province, led a team to inspect the situation.
During the inspection on the evening of January 13, 2023, Mr. Dim Bora said that due to the rain in recent days, the water has risen rapidly and flowed across the river bank and caused the Batachi Bridge, which is a wooden bridge. It collapsed completely, so the team came down to check the situation and report to the upper level.
Please be informed that the people in Battachi village, Takdol commune always use this pedestrian bridge every day on foot, that is, this bridge is a kind of wooden bridge and is very dilapidated, can only be crossed by pedestrians, and the bridge is more than 10 years old People have already asked the Kandal provincial authorities to help build another bridge.
Regarding this case, Mr. Moeng Yuleng, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Kandal Province, said that the bridge had been proposed for construction as a concrete bridge for a long time and also put a sign prohibiting crossing. This evening, Samdech Techo Hun Sen had a solidarity dinner with nearly 5,000 journalists for the 5th time
(Phnom Penh): After missing for two years due to the outbreak of Kovid 19, on the evening of January 14, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, had the honor to meet and have a solidarity meal with the media again. .
The 5th Media Reunion and Solidarity Dinner will be held at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center, attended by nearly 5,000 journalists.
This year's Solidarity Meal is no different from previous years, apart from the media, senior leaders of the Royal Government, provincial governors, spokespersons and government officials involved in the media are allowed to participate. The ceremony, too.
Mr. Phos Sovann, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Information and Audiovisual of the Ministry of Information, told Fresh News that the meeting was open and that all journalists working in Cambodia were allowed to attend without permission. There are journalists from institutions that support or do not support the Royal Government.
According to Mr. Phos Sovann, the journalists who participated in the above program were also about 20 foreign journalists.
It should be noted that the information sector is considered as one of the sectors that has contributed significantly to the building of Cambodian society along the path of democracy, contributing to social improvement, eliminating corruption and inactivity. Journalists have also become messengers and a sacred bridge between the people and the government. In addition, the news also played an important role in presenting Cambodia's image on the international stage.
Since Cambodia was liberated from the genocidal regime, the media has been an indispensable partner of the Royal Government in building and developing Cambodian society. As a leader who likes to write, like to take notes and has a high eloquence in front of the public, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, considers the media as a left hand, right hand, nose and nose, which is important to help Samdech's leadership to achieve good results. Brilliant for the past 35 years.
Seeing the important contribution of journalists, this is why Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to provide the opportunity to enjoy a solidarity meal with journalists every New Year and on the day that Samdech was entrusted by the National Assembly. As the Prime Minister of Cambodia.
For the past four years, during this solidarity dinner, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has always evaluated the performance of Cambodian journalists and also provided various recommendations to improve the work of this information. More effective in helping to improve and develop Cambodian society.
Journalists, on the other hand, are no different from four years ago. They considered the time of the Solidarity Meal with Samdech Techo Hun Sen a sacred time for them. Journalists in Cambodia consider the solidarity meal to be a great honor and value given to them by the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Prior to the meeting, reporters posted messages including ID cards to attend the event, while some even prepared their gowns to attend the solemn ceremony. Through the message, through the preparation, the qualifications and the fresh faces show that they are really happy to have the opportunity to have a solidarity meal with the head of the Royal Government.
