Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Sihanoukville Continues to Distribute Relief to Prey Nup Victims
(Preah Sihanouk): The Cambodian Red Cross branch in Preah Sihanouk province brought zinc and noodles to distribute to the victims of the collapse of their houses on December 17-18, 2022 in Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province.
The distribution was led by Mr. Koam Sokhom, Provincial Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross and Mr. I Thearin, Prey Nup District Governor, on behalf of Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Chairman of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch Committee, with the participation of Branch Officers, Volunteers and Local Authorities. In the afternoon of January 12, 2023.
Koam Sokhom, director of the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Sihanoukville, said that the strong winds had caused the collapse of 43 houses in Prey Nob district and that 21 houses had not yet been rebuilt. In Prey Nob district. Separately, nearly 4,000 other houses were roofed in Prey Nup district, including 114 houses in Kampong Seila district.
He said that immediately after the natural disaster, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun assigned to bring emergency relief supplies to the affected people in Prey Nob and Kampong Seila districts on time, without leaving any people. Lack of food.
At the same time, local authorities have been monitoring the statistics of people affected by the typhoon in the target villages in a timely manner, without any discrimination on the basis of race or political affiliation. Timely.
The provincial branch of the Red Cross will continue to bring zinc and noodles to the affected people in Prey Nup district so that they can have a proper shelter in the future.
