Two men were arrested by police in Bati district, Takeo province, while five others escaped.
(Takeo): Two young men were chased and attacked on the street and then proceeded to the Angkor Pich Chambok Polyclinic and Maternity Hospital in Seiha Village, Chambok Commune, Bati District, Takeo Province, causing a man to be seriously injured in the hospital. Only once. This incident happened on the night of January 9, 2023.
The inspector confirmed that prior to the incident, the victims, Lach Vicheka and Lim Chai Leng, had an argument with a group of seven suspects, in which the seven suspects pulled out a sword and chased the victim. The victim, Lach Vicheka, then jumped off the motorcycle, threw a stone at the side of the road, threw it at the suspects and escaped.
The victim, Lim Chai Leng alias Che, tried to escape on a motorbike to the north in front of Angkor Pich Chambok Polyclinic and Maternity Hospital. Swords were cut several times until the victim fell asleep in a pool of blood in the hospital. The suspect and his accomplices fled on a motorcycle.
Colonel Chhay Keo Mony continued that until January 12, 2023, 19-year-old Vorn Nath, alias Khnat, a resident of Ta Su village, Trapeang Sap commune, Bati district, Takeo province, confessed that he and his party had six members. Others, a total of seven.
With the guidance of the Takeo Provincial Police Commissioner and the Coordination of the Takeo Provincial Prosecutor's Office, the Bati District Police Inspectorate's specialized force arrested another suspect, 18-year-old Phannasara alias Chara. Address: Poun Phnom Village, Trapeang Sap Commune, Bati District, Takeo Province.
