On January 14, 1985, Samdech Techo Hun Sen was elected by the National Assembly of the People's Republic of Cambodia as Chairman of the Council of Ministers (Prime Minister) of the Government of the People's Republic of Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has emphasized that taking office as Prime Minister after Samdech served as Minister of Foreign Affairs, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs for 6 years and also served as Acting Prime Minister for more than 3 months. Chan Si went to Moscow for medical treatment and died in the former Soviet Union.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, who became the Prime Minister from the youngest (32 years old) and continued to hold office until he became the oldest Prime Minister under the support of the people, once said that the position of Director Samdech's first minister received the support of party and state leaders. Especially Samdech Heng Samrin, Samdech Chea Sim, Mr. Say Phu Thong and Mr. Chea Soth etc.
The prime minister's career as a veteran of countless battles and battles has been fraught with difficulties as the country has been economically besieged by liberal countries and disrupted by the Khmer Rouge's attempted occupation. Country again.
The 1980s was a time when Cambodia struggled to overcome all obstacles. Cambodia is considered the poorest country in Southeast Asia. The poorest Cambodians depend on farming, rice, and small-scale trade, with no major trade.
Apart from the economic problems, there are many other issues such as education, training, human resources and ending the fires of war in Cambodia are all things that this young Prime Minister has to struggle to decide as a person responsible for fate. Nation and people.
Despite tens of thousands of chapters, the young Prime Minister Techo Sen has worked hard to overcome obstacles and solve problems.
Dr. Kin Phea, President of the Institute of International Relations of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, sees that as the Prime Minister for 38 years, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has brought nine important achievements to the Cambodian people. The nine major achievements include:
First, Samdech is the leader of the resistance movement to liberate the country from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, which is the greatest sacrifice of Samdech Techo Hun Sen as well as the leaders of the Cambodian People's Party who took their lives as the capital to liberate the Cambodian nation. Get out of the genocidal regime.
Second, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, after liberating the country and the people from the genocidal regime, Samdech made every effort to prevent the return of the genocidal regime by setting out many important strategies and policies to Ensure the survival of the Cambodian nation.
Third, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, since the day of liberation on January 7, 1979, Samdech has strived to rebuild the economy in one hand, to prevent the return of the genocidal regime, and in the other hand to strive to rebuild the nation from the palm of his hand. Empty in a situation where Cambodia is in dire straits, with the world on one side surrounded, both economically and politically.
Sixth: Samdech Techo Hun Sen is the only founder of peace in Cambodia through win-win politics, which has made Cambodia fully historic peace since 1998. Through peace, this is the most important core value for rehabilitation and development in all areas.
9th: Samdech Techo Hun Sen is the most important character who fought for the lives of the people from the death of Kovid 19. Through policies and strategies to fight Kovid 19, Cambodia overcame the Kovid 19 pandemic, leading Cambodia to develop antibodies to prevent Kovid 19, enabling Cambodia to fully reopen the country.
For Dr. Kin Pheap, Samdech Techo Hun Sen remains an important figure for Cambodian society. In particular, Samdech Techo's philosophy of peace remains an essential element for the building and development of Cambodian society.
Minister Dith Dina Encourages Youths of the Khmer-Chinese Association in Cambodia to Continue Strengthening Relations with Chinese Businesses to Attract Investors to Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Dith Dina, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, encouraged the youth group of the Khmer-Chinese Association in Cambodia to continue to strengthen and expand closer and closer relations with Chinese businessmen, traders and investors to enhance relations. Good relations between the people and the two countries, as well as to attract more business and investment to Cambodia.
The encouragement of the Minister of Agriculture was made when he presided over the celebration of the Chinese New Year, organized by the Khmer-Chinese Association in Cambodia on the night of January 13, 2023 at the Convention Center. And Chroy Changvar International Exhibition, Phnom Penh.
On that occasion, Minister Dith Tina also appreciated and highly appreciated the many achievements of the Association's youth group in business, trade, investment, humanitarian and social. These vibrant activities have really contributed significantly to the development of Cambodia to be more prosperous under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Minister Dit Dina said that the fruits of economic and social development in Cambodia can not be separated from the contribution of the Chinese government and people. In addition, the donation and supply of vaccines to Cambodia before and in the millions of doses really contributed greatly to the success of the fight against Kovid 19 and the achievement of community immunity in Cambodia.
Addressing Chinese investors, on behalf of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Dit Tina warmly welcomed all Chinese businessmen, traders and investors who wish to do business and invest in Cambodia, especially in the agricultural sector. . The Ministry continues to support and promote the export of Cambodian agricultural products to the wider Chinese market, focusing on high-quality and high-value products that benefit both peoples and countries.
Mr. Oknha Lim Tong, President of the Cambodian-Chinese Coalition in Cambodia, said that since Cambodia achieved peace, political stability under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Cambodia has made progress in all areas of opportunity. The work and living standards of the people are gradually improving.
Mr. Oknha Lim Tong said that the Cambodian-Chinese Coalition Association in Cambodia has set up a youth group to mobilize Cambodian-Chinese youths of Chinese descent in a spirit of unity and solidarity through various humanitarian activities and trade relations programs, especially relations with partners. China has contributed to the development of the national society and strengthened the Cambodian-Chinese relations.
He hopes that the youth group of the Khmer-Chinese Association in Cambodia will grow stronger and fulfill its mission to make new contributions to promoting relations and cultural exchange between the two countries and to jointly build a community of common destiny between Cambodia and China in the new era. Both create more new achievements.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts has officially launched the book "Film Articles" to make a significant contribution to the promotion and sharing of basic experiences related to film writing to the public, producers.
The inauguration took place on January 13, 2023 with the participation of Mr. Tit Thavrith, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, as well as producers and many other participants.
The launch of this book to help the public and producers to be more knowledgeable, while the last few years have observed that the Cambodian film industry has improved in terms of quality, technique, performance, professional team. The growth of cinema and the birth of production for both cinema and television.
Mr. Tith Thavrith stated that through the active support of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, with the Department of Film Arts and Cultural Promotion as the staff to play an important role and contribute to building human resources in the Cambodian film industry. Past training in film directing, film production techniques, filming, writing and acting skills.
He added that the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts considers the publication of this first screenplay book very important because it is a document and a foundation for young filmmakers to learn how to write short films to long films. Which is the key to further development to film.
"Through this book, it helps to motivate and train human resources in the Cambodian film industry to further develop and improve the quality of Cambodian films to be able to compete with the local film market," he said. I am confident that this first screenplay will be a resounding success and will continue to publish more books as an important path in the Cambodian film industry. ”
Please be informed that this book can be published with the support of Miss Ton Chanseima, Singer for Galaxy Cinema Production under the initiative of the Department of Film Arts and Cultural Promotion in collaboration with Mr. Dip Panda Gogo Chan, Department Advisor.
DC-Cam Holds Forum on "Promoting Women's Rights" in Anlong Veng District
(Phnom Penh): The forum "Promoting Women's Rights" in Anlong Veng district was organized by the Anlong Veng Peace Center of the Documentation Center of Cambodia on the morning of January 13, 2023.
Twenty-three people (20 females and 3 males) out of a total of 107 families in Yeang Tbong village participated in this forum, focusing on the history of the Khmer Rouge, the trial of Khmer Rouge leaders in the Extraordinary Chambers. In Cambodian courts and women's right to information, education and social development.
Dr. Ly Sok Kheang, Director of the Anlong Veng Peace Center, led the discussion, presenting the work of the Anlong Veng Peace Center and the health care project for survivors of the Khmer Rouge regime that has been implemented with people in Yeang Tbong village and throughout the district. Anlong Veng.
The exhibitions are reminiscent of women who went through the Khmer Rouge era, a bittersweet experience that they felt seemed to have recently happened to her and her family. Most of the women talked about forced labor, such as building dams, digging canals and fertilizing rice fields, but in order to survive, they worked hard to do whatever the Khmer Rouge required.
As the discussion progressed to the trial of senior Khmer Rouge leaders in the Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia, most women said they had never heard of or known about the process before. However, the memories of these women continue to be their dedication and participation in the cause of the motherland.
Will isolation from the proceedings of the Khmer Rouge tribunal affect women?
The forum provided discussions on the rights and history of the Khmer Rouge, especially the challenges of women in the village, as the context of the Khmer Rouge history led to some changes in attitudes and lifestyles.
Ignoring or alienating the Khmer Rouge tribunal's proceedings is one of the shortcomings of women, which indicates a lack of education or a real learning experience about the experiences of the Khmer Rouge era and a change of mindset over time. Peace. The process of seeking justice is also part of educating and educating people in society about the mistakes that have been made, especially in relation to basic human rights from one generation to the next.
The next part of the forum also includes discussions on community development projects, a project that focuses on motivating community members to find local unique features to capitalize on them. Support its community.
The development also incorporates frugality and meticulous thinking to keep the local economy out of the way, including the cultivation and cultivation around the house.
Finally, the leaders of Yeang Tbong Village also thanked the Anlong Veng Peace Center for setting up the forum, which encouraged the discussion of rights, especially on local women, as the people needed to address these issues. This is better than before. Lt. Gen. Thet inspected 600 Phnom Penh police force ready to protect the security and order of the SEA Games and Para Games.
