(Phnom Penh): On January 14, 2023, it is 38 years since Samdech Techo Hun Sen became the Prime Minister of Cambodia, a highly responsible role for the destiny of the nation and the people. Samdech Techo Hun Sen became the Prime Minister at the age of 32, the youngest minister in the world.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen took office as Prime Minister at a time when Cambodia was surrounded by many complex economic, political and other social issues. In particular, the crisis of war and national disintegration that occurred after the coup d'etat of March 18, 1970.
What kind of achievements has Samdech Techo Hun Sen's 38 years as Prime Minister brought to the nation and people of Cambodia?
Dr. Ros Chantreaboth, a historian in Cambodia, pointed out that since the post-Angkorian period, especially after the 18th and 19th centuries, Cambodia has always experienced the flames of war and suffering. People are always moving from one place to another, never knowing peace, only knowing the flames of war and deprivation.
The Cambodian historian also points out that in the 19th century, Cambodia was invaded by Siam and Vietnam and lived under French colonization. Then in 1970, the flames of war followed the coups of Lon Nol, In Tam and Cheng Heng. The flames of war have left a total of 3 million Cambodians dead.
For Ros Chantreabot, this tragic war ended when the country was liberated on January 7, 1979. Especially after Samdech Techo Hun Sen took office as the Prime Minister of Cambodia in 1985.
Mr. Ros Chantraboth highlighted that the feature of Samdech Techo's leadership is not to take any Cambodian as an enemy. Based on the win-win theory that all political philosophies win without taking anyone as an enemy, this is what makes Cambodia peaceful, united, and developed like today.
"Samdech Techo Hun Sen is a Cambodian who went to seek peace for Cambodia. In the 20th and 21st centuries, we ask, who gave peace to the Cambodian people to Cambodia? "Those who have sought peace, well-being, happiness and prosperity for Cambodia until today are Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen." This is the confirmation of Mr. Ros Chantraboth.
The Cambodian historian continued, "Therefore, during the 38 years that he led Cambodia, he wished Cambodia, our Cambodian people, happiness and prosperity, overcoming the three fields: the field of war, the field of disease and Hungry fields. "And he brought us into the field of happiness, the field of growth and the field of development."
Mr. Ros Chantraboth also noted that during the 38 years of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's leadership, not only did he promote economic growth and well-being of the people, but he also promoted national prestige on the international stage. Ever been in history as well.
