Ms. Sopheak stated, "On behalf of all the trainees, I would like to express my deep gratitude to the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, for providing us with invaluable things. Peace and development. These two things have given us the opportunity to develop ourselves with a smile and hope. ”
On that occasion, Mr. Youk Bunna, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Public Works and Director of the Royal School of Administration, praised the 80 trainees of Chenla Senior Officials who worked hard to complete this course.
He said that the training of civil servants at both the national and sub-national levels at the Royal School of Administration of the Ministry of Public Works is based on the fundamental goals of public administration reform and public financial management reform programs, which are an important part of governance. Good, which is the backbone of deep state reform based on the Royal Government of Cambodia's Fourth Rectangular Strategic Plan.
Please be informed that the interns also donated 5 laptops to the Royal School of Administration.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, who became the Prime Minister from the youngest (32 years old) and continued to hold office until he became the oldest Prime Minister under the support of the people, once said that the position is Samdech's first Prime Minister received the support of party and state leaders. Especially Samdech Heng Samrin, Samdech Chea Sim, Mr. Say Phu Thong and Mr. Chea Soth etc.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, who took the life to put out the flames of war, recalled that Samdech's inauguration as Prime Minister came at a time when the country was in dire need of food due to the floods and drought of 1984.
Despite leading the country in such a food shortage, the young prime minister addressed the National Assembly on the main policy of ensuring the lives of the people without leaving any people to starve. Unknowingly and unresolved. This politics has survived to the present day, not only theoretically or politically, but has become a practical activity of the CPP as a whole.
The beginning of his life as Prime Minister in the country, just liberated from the flames of war and disturbed by the flames of war along the border, as well as the economic blockade of neighboring countries, is the most difficult discipline of leadership for Samdech Techo. Hun Sen.
* Cambodia's economic development under the leadership of strong man Techo Sen
The 1980s was a time when Cambodia struggled to overcome all obstacles. Cambodia is considered the poorest country in Southeast Asia. The poorest Cambodians depend on farming, rice cultivation and small-scale trade, with no major trade.
Despite tens of thousands of chapters, the young Prime Minister Techo Sen has worked hard to overcome obstacles and solve problems. Finally, the wise and ingenious wisdom of Cambodia's young leaders at the time led to peace talks with Cambodians along the border, negotiating with King Norodom Sihanouk until the Paris Agreement of October 23, 1991. And lead to elections and the re-establishment of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
After the 1993 elections, and with the help of countries in Asia and Europe, the momentum of Cambodia's development has been steadily rising under the Royal Government's sharp development policies. Led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
It cannot be forgotten that, despite foreign aid and clear policies, Cambodia could not be as strong in its development if the Khmer Rouge movement along the border Khmer-Thai is not closed.
Under the clear vision that the end of the border war is the key to national development, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, also launched a plan and implemented a win-win policy by opening negotiations. With the Khmer Rouge, until the Khmer Rouge resistance took refuge under the roof of the same Royal Government, leading Cambodia to completely end the war between its own nation on December 28, 1998.
Starting from the end of the civil war, Cambodia has had full opportunities for national development. For 38 years under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Cambodia, the poorest country after liberation from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot in 1979, has become the current low middle income country. Cambodians, who have no income, have an average income of about $ 1,730.
Cambodia, after being liberated from the genocidal regime with a population of just over 5 million, has become a country of about 17 million people today.
Cambodia, which used to lack a road, bridge and road system for people to travel and serve in the past, is becoming a country with a system of roads, bridges, thousands of kilometers from one province to another, including bridges. Large river crosses more than 10 bridges, unprecedented in the history of Cambodia.
Bridges across the river were born during the reign of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, such as: Neak Leung Bridge, Monivong II Bridge, Koh Thom Bridge, Chroy Changva 2 Bridge, Sekong Bridge, Stung Treng Province, Prek Kdam Bridge, Pretamak Bridge, Mekong River Bridge, Stung Treng Bridge, Takhmao Bridge, Stung Trang Bridge. ... etc.
Phnom Penh, the economic, cultural and tourism heart of Cambodia, with an area of just over 300 square kilometers, has become the capital with an area of more than 760 square kilometers today.
Phnom Penh, with a very small population, is becoming a capital city with a large population of up to 3 million people and people come to live, work, study and study, as well as tourism. Up to nearly 2 million more today.
Phnom Penh, with few residential buildings left over from the fires of war, is becoming a capital with many high-rise commercial buildings. From the beginning of implementation from 2000 to November 2022, there are 2,534 high-rise projects from 5 to 40 floors nationwide.
In addition to the sectors mentioned above, it is also seen that many important sectors of Cambodia are growing significantly compared to the past and present. Looking back at the Cambodian economy, there is also a remarkable momentum. Prior to 2020, the year of the 19-year-old plague, Cambodia maintained a growth rate of around 7 percent for about two decades.
Wisdom, ingenuity, full of will, long-term vision, clarity and the preservation of the national interest of the people have made Samdech Techo's leadership continue to remain strong in the present, despite the society facing the crisis caused by the epidemic and harassment. Kovid 19 disease.
Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen for 38 years not only promotes the growth of the national economy and the people, but Samdech has set out a lively foreign policy. Through this ingenious foreign policy, Cambodia has transformed from a country that was once helped to resolve crises to a country that actively participates in resolving regional and global crises.
Battle of Democracy 6 mandates Strong man Techo Sen defeated 5 consecutive mandates
Excluding the events of the 1993 election, which was the first election and the full participation of the people, the last five terms since 1998, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the CPP's prime ministerial candidate, has always been Excessive support from the electorate towards the leadership of the Royal Government.
In total, during his 38 years as Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has been at the helm of the Cambodian navy with the utmost care to restore and lead this miserable country to a new era of development. All areas are remarkable and have helped people to have a better life. Build honor, fame, pride and hope for progress and prosperity.
