General Knowledge: The "Death Triangle" in the western Atlantic Ocean is as dangerous as it gets, isn't it?
Whether the above rumors are true or not, please find the following explanation:
Although there are countless theories about the Bermuda Triangle, none of them can be substantiated. On the contrary, there are still ships and planes passing through the area every day without any accidents.
However, the actual boundaries of the Bermuda Triangle are not universally recognized. Estimates of the total area of the area are between 1,300,000 and 3,900,000 square kilometers. All these estimates show that this area is triangular in shape.
The name Bermuda Triangle is not officially on any world map. In addition, this geographical area is not recognized as an official area in the Atlantic Ocean.
Please be informed that at present, the Bermuda Triangle area is still busy every day, both by water and by air.
Russia says Belarus could intervene in conflict if violated by Ukraine
MOSCOW (Reuters) - Belarus could enter the conflict in Ukraine if Kiev decides to "invade" any country, a Russian Foreign Ministry official said on Friday. This is according to the publication by the AFP news agency on Friday, January 13, 2023.
"Ukrainian forces must be prepared on the border with Belarus, but for now, what we have seen is only a disgusting statement," said Ukrainian President Vladimir Putin. "However, we must be ready both at the border and in the region."
In an interview with the media, a Russian Foreign Ministry minister, Aleksey Polishchuk, said that Russia's military exercises with Belarus were designed to prevent provocations and warned that Belarus could be involved in the conflict. Ukraine if it or Russia is invaded. However, it is up to the leaders of both countries to decide.
Russia used Belarus to launch an attack on Ukraine on February 24 and has been deploying troops to the joint Russian-Belarusian military force since October 2022. The two countries have since agreed to strengthen military cooperation, raising fears that Moscow could use its close ally to launch a new offensive on Ukraine from the north.
