Ministry of Social Affairs issues press release on Lay Samnang arrested by ACU for embezzling state budget for personal gain
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation has issued a press release informing the public that Lay Samnang, former Deputy Director of the Finance and Supply Department of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, was arrested by the Anti-Corruption Unit yesterday. On January 11, 2023, he was arrested for embezzling the 2019 and 2020 state budgets for personal use.
The Ministry of Social Affairs stated in a statement that prior to the arrest, the ministry had set up a task force to investigate the irregularities and demand that the person be reimbursed, but Lay Samnang tried to evade and delay the settlement. Not responsible for repaying all those state budgets.
In connection with this case, the Ministry has taken administrative disciplinary action and requested the Ministry's lawyers to prepare a complaint to the Anti-Corruption Unit for legal action.
It should be noted that this morning, January 12, 2023, the Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court issued a temporary detention order for the accused Lay Samnang at the Education Center (PJ) after being accused of embezzling the state budget and money. Disability policy regime more than $ 380,000.
Koh Kong Provincial Authority instructs municipal and district authorities throughout the province to disseminate the voter list review process to the public.
