Notice! The section of National Road No. 4, km 42 in Kampong Speu province was flooded while 4 cities and districts were affected by the flood, the provincial governor intervened and prepared to rescue people
(Kampong Speu): Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu Province, said that due to the change of weather, a series of rains in early January caused 4 districts of Kampong Speu Province to be hit by floods. At the same time, on the evening of January 12, 2023, he led the working group of the relevant departments to inspect the flood situation in the four cities and districts.
On January 13, 2023, due to continuous rain on the left side of the Oral Mountains, National Road No. 4 at km 42 in front of Borey Sovann, Chbar Morn City was also flooded.
Mr. Vy Samnang said: “The districts that were attacked were Chbar Morn, Oral, Thpong and Phnom Sruoch. "Currently, the district authorities are investigating the case very carefully and have prepared all means to prevent the rescue of the victims."
With this statement, the Governor of Kampong Speu Province has not been able to confirm the number of houses, schools, hospitals, pagodas and people's property yet, while the district-municipal, village-commune working group is working to help prevent the people from leaving. There were no immediate reports of injuries or severe damage from the floods.
According to Mr. Nhanh Cheab Hung, Director of the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Kampong Speu Province, the rain continued to fall in the upper part, the water flowed to the lower part, causing some reservoirs to raise the water level alarmingly.
Mr. Su Sunthara, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Kampong Speu Province, also said that many roads were flooded and cut off from the flood. Of all kinds of vehicles are stuck, can not go to some roads, and if the rain continues to fall, all roads in the province of Kampong Speu may be temporarily closed to traffic, waiting for the water to recede.
