ISIS claims responsibility for deadly bombing that kills five in Kabul, Afghanistan
ISIS claimed responsibility for a deadly bomb blast near the Foreign Ministry in the Afghan capital, Kabul, on Thursday, killing at least five people. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Thursday, January 12, 2023.
The bombing was the second major attack on Kabul in 2023 and drew international condemnation.
ISIS's Amaq news agency said the attack coincided with a ministry training course for diplomats.
Extremists have stepped up their attacks since the Taliban took control of Afghanistan in 2021. The overall target is Taliban soldiers and members of the country's Shiite minority.
Russia begins to intervene in foreign exchange markets as Chinese yuan becomes more important to the country
Russia has said it will resume foreign currency intervention with the sale of the yuan from Friday, highlighting the growing importance of the Chinese currency in Moscow's efforts. To ensure economic stability in the face of Western sanctions. According to Reuters.
After the West imposed the heaviest sanctions in modern history due to the war in Ukraine, Russia's economy has shown remarkable resilience, but the world's largest natural resource producer is now increasingly turning to China. .
Russia's Finance Ministry, along with the central bank, has responded economically to sanctions, saying it would sell 54.5 billion rubles ($ 798 million) in foreign currency. From January 13, at a time when oil and gas revenues fell.
"In order to increase the stability and predictability of the domestic economic situation, as well as to reduce the impact of the volatile energy market situation on Russia's economy and public finances, the Ministry of Finance will restart. "Liquidity assets (liquidity) transactions."
Russia's 2023 budget is based on the price of Urals at $ 70.1 a barrel, although it is currently trading below $ 50 a barrel. Russia's gross domestic product (GDP) is expected to reach $ 2.14 trillion this year, the highest level since 2013, according to the International Monetary Fund.
In Russia, where the US dollar has dominated the market for years after the collapse of the Soviet Union in 1991, the Chinese yuan has been a major currency for Moscow since its sanctions. The West comes. According to Reuters.
