Vietnam's cashew industry is expected to remain in a difficult situation in 2023
According to VINACAS, there are a number of reasons for declining exports. The association said the price of raw cashew nuts remained high and processing costs were high, but export prices were low, meaning exporters were hesitant.
"So people are spending more on necessities and reducing the cost of non-essential items like cashew nuts," he said. "This situation is expected to continue this year, demand for cashew nuts will be low and it will be difficult to raise prices."
According to the VINACAS Information Council, by 2023, cashew production and supply chains will continue to face challenges due to factors such as the Russia-Ukraine conflict, inflation and the recession, the central bank's credit tightening, volatility. VND and US exchange rates, declining demand and rising processing costs.
