This statement was made on the occasion of Mr. Kun Nhem holding a press conference to present the closing results of the tax collection work on existing tax-free vehicles in the country at the General Department of Customs and Excise on the afternoon of January 12. This year 2023.
Mr. Kun Nhim stated, "Duty-free motorcycles, especially large motorcycles, are also targets that we need to focus on, suppress and control when importing. "According to the results of the crackdown, we have been looking for the reason or the gap, why there are big motorcycles and no tax, it can come."
Mr. Kun Nhim said that at the border, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia is aware that motorcycle smuggling is also rampant and that motorcycle smuggling through the corridor is a complex issue that the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia is difficult to prevent. 100 percent.
At the same time, Mr. Kun Nhem also said that each month, the General Department of Customs and the Cambodian Excise prevented a lot, but at the same time there was a disappearance, which is not all. At the same time, the customs also tightened controls on the import of motorcycles from distant countries, such as: from Europe, Japan, Korea, contained in containers.
Mr. Kun Nhem pointed out that the import of motorcycles stored in containers, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia has been inspected, meaning that 10 containers can be clicked to inspect 5 cabinets or 6 cabinets by conducting detailed inspections to prevent Do not allow the number of duty-free motorcycles to evade taxes into the country.
Mr. Kun Nhim said that the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia also paved the way for the owners of tax-free motorbikes to pay taxes, but it was less than the fines that the General Department of Customs and Excise cracked down on.
Mr. Kun Nhim also said that in principle, the General Department of Customs and Excise does not have a preferential tax campaign on existing tax-free motorcycles in this country.
Please be reminded that the Customs and Excise Force of Phnom Penh raided and inspected the compliance of many modern big motorcycles that gathered in Chroy Changvar district on October 08, 2022, and found a total of 150 modern big motorbikes duty free.
Many of these big motorbikes have gathered to prepare for a trip to Siem Reap, but have not yet left, so they were inspected by the customs authorities, and some of these big motorbikes are known to cost tens of thousands of dollars.
This was stated by Mr. Kun Nhim, Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, said in a press conference on "Closing the tax collection work on existing tax-free vehicles in the country" on the afternoon of January 12. 2023.
"Throughout 2022, 728 duty-free vehicles were seized, totaling more than 2.3 million US dollars, received from the owners by paying 297 taxes and fines," he said. . "As for the remaining cars, the General Department of Customs is waiting for the car owners to come and deal with the tax obligations and fines."
He said that in 2022, the crackdown on duty-free vehicles was 728, with only 40 right-hand drive vehicles, about 6 percent, which shows that the number of right-hand drive vehicles suppressed in 2022 decreased significantly compared to 2022. By 2021, 82 out of 250 right-hand drive vehicles were cracked down on, with an estimated drop in the number of right-hand drive duty-free crackdowns due to border crossings.
