The General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia emphasized that after the campaign to collect tax on duty-free vehicles in the country, only crackdown and crackdown is a heavy burden.
In addition, Mr. Kun Nhim also said that left-hand drive vehicles are tax-free, while right-hand drive vehicles are tax-free, breaking both the customs law and the traffic law.
It should be reminded that the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to collect tax on existing duty-free cars in the country of refuge under various license plates from September 2021.
From September to December 31, 2021, left-hand drive tax-free vehicles can pay tax with a 10% tax preference. Right-hand drive vehicles also receive a 10 percent tax concession. The right-to-left steering wheel must be completed by June 30, 2022.
After the deadline, at the request of the people, on July 6, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen allowed the existing duty-free right-hand drive vehicles in the country to enter the tax without having to change the steering wheel from the right. Go to the left.
Duty-free right-hand drive vehicle owners are required to register as existing vehicles in the country by July 31, 2022. After registration, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia has until the end of 2022 to fulfill their tax and duty obligations. .
Deadline Registered right-hand drive vehicles that have not fulfilled their tax and duty obligations are subject to confiscation, seizure of spare parts, or demolition in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.
From September 2021 to December 31, 2022, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia collected about 106 million dollars, while the total number of vehicles that have been taxed and registered is about 20,000 units.
