(Phnom Penh): A group of police officers at the second office of the Anti-Drug Crime Department were fined by the unit after committing a crime of professional misconduct and hurting people who exploded on social media. Tik Tok. This is according to the press release of the Department of Anti-Drug Crimes.
According to the Anti-Drug Department, after receiving information from the Tik Tok account named Socheata on the phenomenon in Ta Nguon 2 Village, Sangkat Kakap, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh, the leadership of the National Police General Commission paid attention and issued an order. Investigate this case immediately.
The Anti-Drug Department investigated and found that a group of officers from the second office of the Anti-Drug Crime Department went to implement the incitement in accordance with legal procedures, reported to the Phnom Penh Municipal Police and with the coordination of Mr. Deputy Prosecutor of Phnom Penh. However, in carrying out their work, this group violated professional discipline and affected the people.
Therefore, the leadership of the General Commissioner of the National Police decided:
1: Discipline by sending to the regulatory unit to consider mistakes. 2: The Disciplinary Council will review and request for more practical discipline. The Anti-Drug Department would like to thank the cooperation from all walks of life, as well as constructive feedback from all media outlets, for providing timely information, participating in security, social autonomy, and participating in refinement of officials of the Anti-Drug Department. Drug offenses.
