Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that the pluralism and division of the bloc is growing more and more, respect for independence, sovereignty and determination to choose the path for the development of each country is a task that we are all countries. Developing must continue to stand firm.
"We must continue to promote multilateralism and a culture of dialogue in addressing challenges aimed at preventing economic divisions and trade bans, as well as avoiding any military conflict," he said. "It could eventually happen to maintain regional and global peace, security and stability."
In addition, Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that the experience of Kovid-19 clearly shows that the continuation of social resilience by focusing on the development of the health system, the promotion of public health services and social protection is very important. To be prepared for other conflicts in the future.
"We also need to continue to develop human resources that focus on opportunities for scientific change, labor market needs and development," he said.
At the same time, digital technology has become a driving force in promoting diversification and economic growth, strengthening competitiveness and resilience, however, the grasp of digital technology in developing countries continues to be a gap. This is an additional confirmation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that in this sense, we really need to share new technologies, training, as well as attract investment, business, finance and technology from developed countries. Senior Minister Osman Hassan pays a courtesy call on Malaya delegation (DMDI)
The meeting was held on the afternoon of January 11, 2023 at the office of Dr. Osman Hassan in Phnom Penh in order to discuss in detail the plans for the DMDI General Assembly, which Cambodia will host this year.
According to the plan, the General Assembly will invite the presidency and the presidency in the opening and closing programs. Cambodia, as the host country, will be ready to host about 150 foreign guests who will be attending the conference.
Please be informed that DMDI was established in 2000 in Malaysia to unite among Malay Muslims, such as promoting cooperation in all aspects of development among Malay Muslims with people of other countries in The world. In 2012, DMDI also established its Secretariat in Cambodia, headed by Senior Minister Dr. Osman Hassan.
Through DMDI, Cambodia receives scholarships for students to continue their studies at universities in the state of Malacca and to assist in humanitarian work such as building churches, schools, organizing seminars, teacher training, orphanage, algebra, and disaster relief programs. Nature and so on.
Notification: After continuous rain, Kampong Speu Provincial Authority temporarily opened the automatic water gates of 5 Anlong Chrey Reservoir dams.
(Kampong Speu): The administration of Kampong Speu province on January 12, 2023 issued a notice stating that with heavy rain in the past few days in the upper part of the water level. Anlong Chrey Reservoir Dam is located in Anlong Chrey Village, Pram Bei Mom Commune, Thpong District, Kampong Speu Province, which requires the authorities to temporarily open five automatic water gates to release water.
Based on this situation, the provincial administration urges the people, especially those who live along the Kraing Ponleu river, to pay more attention and be careful by preparing the important materials in the safe place properly, especially the people. The elderly and young children must hurry to safety first.
At the same time, the provincial administration asks people to be very careful about power lines that can cause accidents eventually.
Duke Kith Meng Encourages Turkish Businesses to Invest in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): This morning, January 12, 2023, the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce cooperated with the Ministry of Commerce of Cambodia, the Ministry of Agriculture and Forestry of the Republic of Turkey and the Turkish Foreign Economic Relations Commission to organize the Cambodia-Turkey Business Dialogue.
The talks were chaired by Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce of Cambodia and Prof. Vahit Kirisci, Minister of Agriculture and Forestry of the Republic of Turkey, and was attended by the Turkish Ambassador to Cambodia and senior officials. Relevant institutions and the private sector of both countries.
The talks are aimed at boosting trade and investment between the two countries in key areas, including tourism, garments, construction, medicine, food and vehicles.
Speaking on the occasion of the business talks, Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, warmly welcomed the Turkish delegation's visit to Cambodia led by Professor Wahid Kirizhi and highlighted the good relations between the two countries. Which has had diplomatic ties since 1959.
The President requested a direct flight between Cambodia and Turkey, a regular meeting once a year between the Cambodia-Turkey Business Council and a business forum twice a year.
The business talks ended successfully with fruitful results, in which the two countries' businessmen and investors exchanged business experiences, opportunities, policy updates and discussed potential areas for joint cooperation. Kampong Cham Provincial Governor: The implementation of the new garbage collection strategy in Kampong Cham City encounters some problems for business houses
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, said that after implementing the new strategy to collect garbage in Kampong Cham for the past 10 days, it was found that related to the collection of service fees, the team encountered some problems. Homes that do business separately to people's homes do not have a problem.
The provincial governor said so on the morning of January 12, 2023 in the 44th Ordinary Meeting of the third mandate of the Provincial Council at Kampong Cham Provincial Hall.
According to the provincial governor, in the six-month pilot process of implementing the new policy for Cintri waste collection in Kampong Cham so far, it has been more than 10 years and the team has encountered some problems. Contact the collection of fees with the houses of people who do business, such as open houses, restaurants, restaurants and warehouses, banks, etc.
The new governor said that the new strategy requires Cintri to collect garbage in Kampong Cham and weigh the kilos and charge the Kampong Cham municipal administration a ton of $ 17. There is another company that collects fees from the people and gives the money to the Kampong Cham Municipality for payment with Cintri, according to the price list of the Ministry of Environment.
The provincial governor added that in implementing the new policy, the provincial authorities have seen problems with people's homes doing business and have gradually resolved them. At the same time, the Kampong Cham Municipal Administration is also open to the public if they find that their house has to pay a high service fee to discuss to resolve at Kampong Cham City Hall.
The provincial governor confirmed that the garbage collection work was divided into three groups, including:
Group 1: Cintri Garbage Collection Monitoring and Inspection Team
* The second group: the management and revenue collection team to pay the garbage fee to Cintri Company per ton of $ 17.
* The third group is the working group to resolve disputes and requests of the people.
