Senior Minister Sun Chanthol Chairs a Meeting to Review Measures to Improve Rainwater Release System Along National Road 4 in Por Sen Chey District
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, chaired a meeting to review and understand the presentation on measures to improve the rainwater harvesting system along National Road 4 in Phnom Penh with the participation of the Ministry. Charges and relevant professional officers as well.
This meeting was held on January 11, 2023 at the Ministry to review and discuss various measures and methods to improve the rainwater harvesting system along National Road 4 in Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh to plan. To solve related challenges that have occurred in the past in order to improve health, hygiene, public welfare and maintain the beauty of the city.
During the meeting, the meeting actively exchanged views on technical work related to the project to study the improvement of rainwater harvesting system in order to identify potential challenges in the project. The meeting discussed to expand the scope of this work more broadly and clearly to be able to address the challenges in response to the real needs of the people.
On that occasion, the Senior Minister also instructed the working group to speed up the study of the technical aspects of the project to improve the rainwater harvesting system as soon as possible to make a respectful presentation to Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister. The Minister of Economy and Finance to review and make additional recommendations to promote the successful implementation of this project.
National policy on cashews to boost exports and cultivation is set to be submitted to the Cabinet this weekend.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, said that the National Policy on Cashew 2022-2027 will be submitted to the Cabinet meeting on January 13, 2023 to be officially introduced, which will help Strengthen and expand exports, help increase cultivation and processing, while Cambodia currently exports a lot of unprocessed cashew nuts to Vietnam, which loses value.
Mr. Pan Sosak emphasized this after the third meeting of the Joint Economic Commission between Cambodia and the Republic of Turkey on the afternoon of January 11, 2023 at the Raffles Royal Hotel.
He said cashews were grown on a large scale and provided a lot of export earnings, but had not been well managed in the past.
He expects that after the official implementation of the National Policy on Cashew 2022-2027 in 2023, after the approval of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia will promote the export of cashew nuts as well as help. Support farmers in cultivation.
"Normally, we must have a clear policy to share the responsibilities and work of each ministry to promote this sector together," he said. "I hope that exports will increase and be well managed because we know that the cultivation of cashews is large, but we have not processed or properly prepared for export on behalf of Cambodia."
He added that currently the cashew sector still has some challenges that need to be addressed to promote the sector to grow.
At the same time, he wants the intervention of the Ministry of Commerce to find markets that can help farmers sell agricultural products at affordable prices. However, the farmers themselves have to work together as a community to harvest and sell directly to the factory, managing and distributing the quality of the seeds to get a good price.
According to the report of the Cambodian Cashew Association, in 2022, Cambodia exported 670,000 tons of raw cashew nuts to the international market, valued at 1,077 million US dollars, a decrease of 34.65 percent.
