Kampong Speu Provincial Governor Calls on District Authorities Affected by Floods to Prepare for Rescue
(Kampong Speu): On the morning of January 12, 2023, Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu Province, during his visit to inspect the flood situation throughout the province, informed the people in some areas who may face danger due to flooding, please Be careful because the current rainfall situation is continuing to fall sharply in some areas of Kampong Speu province.
To address this challenge, the provincial governor calls on the Armed Forces authorities at all levels to facilitate residents on public roads, as well as some areas that are ready to be flooded due to rain, and evacuate them to safety. To ensure their well-being.
The provincial governor continued, "At this time, the sky is raining heavily on the geography of Kampong Speu province, especially some areas of Oral and Phnom Sruoch districts, which caused flooding of roads and plantations, so people should be more careful. "And our authorities are ready to rescue the people in time."
The governor of Kampong Speu province stressed that due to climate change, it caused continuous rain and flooded parts of Oral district, Kampong Speu province. In fact, since January 11, 2023, at O'Anchanh village, Ta Sal commune, Oral district, Kampong Speu province, flooding caused the flooding of Road 48-4, which cut off the traffic of the people for a while.
(Phnom Penh): Residents living on unregulated buildings on Street 151 in Samrong South Village, Sangkat Samrong, Khan Prek Pnov, Phnom Penh, should stop protesting on public streets, which affects the order and consider accepting policy land from the Capital Authority. Phnom Penh.
This is according to the appeal from the administrative officer of Khan Prek Phnov on the morning of January 12, 2023, while more than 20 families living in an unregulated construction on Street 151 in Samrong South village, Sangkat Samrong, Khan Prek Phnov is protesting in front Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction so that they can live on the old site on Street 151.
Even though you have been living illegally on the public road, the authorities have decided to provide a legal plot of land not far from the old location, about 1 km on the same road 151, for each of them. Get a plot of land measuring 4.2 meters by 20 meters.
Prek Pnov district administration official confirmed that for this offer, 28 people have understood and agreed to accept the above policy land and have left the old site to occupy the new land.
However, there are still some people who, due to listening to the incitement of some civil society organizations, continue to protest often, refusing to accept the policy of the Phnom Penh administration.
