In his video and letter of apology, Mr. Seang Hy stated that the reason he posted such pictures and information was to encourage the public to visit and comment, but this was not the case.
It should be noted that on January 11, 2023, there was a lot of sharing on Facebook after it was alleged that a police force at the Anti-Drug Department arrested and beat a man, causing him to faint and seriously injure himself.
After receiving such information, General Dr. Neth Savoeun, the National Police Commissioner General, ordered General King Sarath, Director of the Anti-Drug Department, to immediately investigate to find out the culprit. If the police are really wrong, they must take legal action without exception.
Immediately after receiving the order, General Kheng Sarath conducted a search until he met the person who posted the information. After interrogation, the man also admitted that he posted this information was a misunderstanding and just to be seen and commented on, in fact, no police came to beat his brother and sister-in-law. That.
In his video and apology, Sieng Hy apologized to the Anti-Drug Department and the National Police for posting such false information and promised not to do so again.
"I apologize to the leadership of the Anti-Drug Department and the National Police for disseminating false information that exaggerates the facts and discredits the National Police," he said. "I promise that in the future, I will not post messages and pictures that will affect government institutions and other entities. If something goes wrong, I will be held accountable before the law."
