This afternoon, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia held a press conference to present the closing results of the tax collection work on existing tax-free vehicles in the country.
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of January 12, 2023, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia will hold a press conference to present the closing results of the tax collection work on existing duty-free vehicles in the country under the chairmanship of Mr. Kun Nhim, Minister. Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia.
Duty-free right-hand drive vehicle owners are required to register as existing vehicles in the country by July 31, 2022. After registration, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia has until the end of 2022 to fulfill their tax and duty obligations. . Nearly 10,000 duty-free right-hand drive vehicles in Cambodia are now registered.
Registered right-hand drive vehicles that have not fulfilled their tax and duty obligations are subject to confiscation, seizure of spare parts, or demolition in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.
As of the beginning of October 2022, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia collected about $ 100 million, while the total number of vehicles collected tax and registered about 18,000 units.
