(Preah Sihanouk): Speaking from Preah Sihanouk Province on the occasion of inspecting the 19 doses of Kovid vaccination, urging the people this morning, January 12, 2023, Mrs. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Chair of the Commission Kovid vaccination 19 A nationwide framework reminds people not to forget or delay too long to go for the 19-dose measles vaccine.
In an interview with reporters after reviewing the vaccination process at the Sihanoukville Kindergarten and the Sihanoukville Provincial Prison, Ms. O Vandin emphasized that the delay was too long, some up to eight months to a year. In the body of the individual is reduced and vulnerable to the onset of Kovid 19.
The chairman of the commission said that in the case of the last dose, the gap is too long, up to eight months or a year, so the defense force is almost completely reduced, and if it falls to zero, there is a risk. Extremely high for individuals in the attack of Kovid 19, especially XBB XBB 1.5, which may provide another space for a re-emergence of omega virus transmission in the community.
Ms. O Vandin emphasized, "Do not forget, when we forget to leave for too long, it means that we try to inject before it becomes useless and then need to add to keep our body. "In order to maintain the familiarity in the community and to contribute to the sustainability of the nation and the family economy to grow, as well as to promote the economic growth of our country."
In this regard, Ms. O Vandin continued to call on the people to get vaccinated against Kovid 19 according to the arrangement of the sub-national authority, which has organized a clear program. She added that the vaccine was provided in the same way, regardless of race, ethnicity or political affiliation, as long as individuals living in Cambodia, including detainees.
In fact, in Sihanoukville Provincial Prison, all inmates were vaccinated against Kovid 19 at a specific time, which is now due to the fifth dose. Ms. O Vandin sees these as good points, as 19 new strains of the XBB virus have not yet reached Cambodia, and we have increased our pre-emptive forces.
Ms. O Vandin said, "If we supplement the Kovid 19 vaccine in the third, fourth, fifth and sixth boosts, it will save the lives of the people and help prevent the occurrence of future infections." "The 19 new Kovid virus has spread in our Cambodian community."
Once again, the health official continues to call on people not to discriminate against any type of vaccine, as the vaccines that Cambodia is currently using are all on the World Health Organization's emergency use list, and the health organization claims That all these vaccines are still effective in preventing, however small, all of these types of metabolism.
