Mine Authority and Norwegian Citizens' Aid Organization (NPA) Sign Memorandum of Understanding on Mine Action Capacity Development Project
(Phnom Penh): On January 12, 2023, at the Office of the Mine Authority, Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Vice President of the Mine Authority, presided over the signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding between the Mine Authority and the Norwegian People's Aid (NPA). On the Mine Action Capacity Development Project with a total budget of US $ 172,791.
The Memorandum of Understanding on the Mine Action Capacity Development Project covers the implementation of three major activities: 1 /. Capacity of the data unit, 2 /. Capacity of the quality control team, and 3 / Capacity on strategic planning.
On behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister and Chairman of the Mine Action Authority, Senior Minister Ly Thuch expressed his deep gratitude to the Royal Government and the people of Norway for their support of the Mine Action Capacity Development Project. Increase work efficiency and enhance the prestige of the Mine Authority, which is the staff of the Royal Government of Cambodia to lead, manage, control and coordinate mine activities in Cambodia.
The senior minister praised the NPA's commitment to continue working to make Cambodia landmine-free by 2025 and to reduce the impact of cluster munitions and other explosive remnants of war. This commitment is in line with the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to clear all mines in Cambodia by 2025, as reaffirmed by our Prime Minister recently.
He added that with the current efforts and under the leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, the commitment to a mine-free Cambodia by 2025 will become a reality and the continued strengthening and maintenance of the mine authority is a necessary task. . Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin Asks Former Korean National Assembly President to Promote and Mobilize Korean Investors to Invest More in Cambodia
