(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, confirmed that Samdech has never decided to hand over the house and land where Mr. Kong Koam currently resides (5290 square meters) to be privately owned and his letter of clarification is The evidence is indisputable, and any preparation of title deeds is a forgery of state land and houses.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's statement came just minutes after Kong Koam made a statement on the history of living in a house and land owned by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs along Preah Sothearos Street, Sangkat Tonle Bassac, Khan Chamkarmon.
"I remember when I decided to move into this house, I really informed the minister without any politeness, and the minister has always understood," Kong Koam said in the letter.
After seeing Kong Koam's clarification letter, Samdech Techo acknowledged that most of what Kong Koam described in the letter was true.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized, "I really understand the residence of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, but I have never decided to give the house and land to Mr. Kong Koam as private property, and the house and land are still Owned by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.
Samdech Techo emphasized, "Therefore, legally, this house and land still belong to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, and it is time for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs to take back this house and land in order to use it for the ministry's work." " This is an additional confirmation of Samdech Techo.
The following is the full text of Samdech Techo's presentation on his official social network on the afternoon of January 11, 2023:
I would like to confirm that I really understand the residence of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, but I have never decided to hand over the house and land to Mr. Kong Koam as private property and the house and land are still owned by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. The same foreigner. All of Kong Koam's preparation of documents to obtain a title deed to this land is a forgery of state land and houses as private property.
