One of them is Cambodia's progress in the context of global socio-economic development, both in the 21st century, in the stages of globalization, in the context of the Industrial Revolution 4.0, and to adapt to the labor market and The global economy.
Therefore, all participation and support in the reform process is very important. If we do not have the adjustments or reforms, we will surely be able to run after or catch up with the daily progress of global society, which requires us to work harder. More self-improvement as well.
For 2022, this is the second consecutive year that the Cambodia Securities Exchange broke the record for the highest trading growth with a double growth.
"Throughout 2022, the Cambodia Securities Exchange raised a total capital of 222 billion riels (equivalent to more than $ 50 million), an increase of 133 percent compared to the same period in 2021, the most significant increase. "From the issuance of bonds, corporate bonds accounted for 63 percent and state-owned securities accounted for 32 percent of total capital."
Although the average trading volume in 2022 decreased slightly, the average trading value doubled to more than 2 billion riels per day, making 2022 the second consecutive year that the Cambodia Securities Exchange broke the record for trading growth. Highest with a double growth.
In addition, the number of newly opened trading accounts in 2022 has increased by more than 5,000 accounts, equivalent to 31% compared to 2021. The Cambodia Stock Exchange Index at the end of 2022 also saw a slight increase of about 2% compared to 2021, as the total market capitalization increased from 7.2 trillion riels to 7.5 trillion riels.
The Cambodia Securities Exchange in 2022 also achieved the listing of seven companies, an increase of 2.5 times compared to the same period in 2021. The Ministry of Public Works is studying plans to set up passenger car parks outside the capital to avoid congestion
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, highlighted that the Ministry is in talks with the private sector to set up bus stops outside the capital to avoid traffic congestion.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol emphasized this while allowing a delegation of the Cambodian Road Transport Association (CAMBA) to pay a courtesy call and discuss work on January 11, 2023.
During the courtesy call, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol informed the delegation of the Cambodian Road Transport Association that the Ministry's efforts to strengthen and expand the infrastructure and transportation sector, despite the Kovid 19 crisis. . Recently, the bridge construction project as well as the project to expand and improve the quality of many roads have been held to announce the groundbreaking.
The senior minister added that within 10 years at the latest, the national and provincial roads in Cambodia will be transformed into all types of concrete, asphalt (AC) roads and have a minimum width of 12 meters or 4 lanes.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also mentioned the Phnom Penh-Bavet Expressway project, which has already studied and signed a framework agreement, and plans to sign a concession agreement next month during Samdech Techo's state visit to China. In addition, a new Phnom Penh-Siem Reap expressway project is also under study.
In connection with these expressway projects, the Senior Minister also requested the Cambodian Road Transport Association to help promote the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway and related to this request. The association would like to support and encourage transport service operators to use the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway as much as possible.
On that occasion, Dr. Chhim Chamnan, President of the Association, confirmed the participation in the use of expressways in the past and promised to continue to promote the use even more.
At the same time, Dr. also requested the Ministry to promote the arrangement of additional bus stops.
In relation to this proposal, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol confirmed that the Ministry, in cooperation with the private sector, is studying a project to set up a bus station outside the capital to avoid the large bus traffic into the city, which leads to congestion.
On that occasion, the Senior Minister requested the Association to promote the use of more electric vehicles in the transportation sector to join the Royal Government in the carbon neutrality campaign to preserve the environment for a long time.
Mr. Sun Chanthol informed about the location of the power station that is currently in operation and plans to continue to deploy more throughout the country.
In addition to discussing land transport infrastructure, the senior minister also mentioned the projects the ministry is studying: improving the quality of railways and water transport.
Please be informed that the Ministry is studying the project to transport water by sea without having to pass through the port of Vietnam, and if this project is achieved, it will be a historical project that changes the face of Cambodia as a whole in the field of water transport. Dr. Hun Manet: Youth House for Cambodia-China Friendship will be another example of steel friendship between the two countries
