Neak Oknha Kith Meng continues to be the President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Phnom Penh for the new mandate
(Phnom Penh): Duke Kith Meng, a well-known Cambodian billionaire with many businesses in hand, has been re-elected President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Phnom Penh for a new fifth term.
For the election of the President of the Phnom Penh Chamber of Commerce, Duke Kith Meng received a majority of 39 out of 40 votes.
Separately, for the election of the President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, Duke Kith Meng received 15 out of 18 votes.
The election of the President of the Cambodian-Phnom Penh Chamber of Commerce was held on January 11, 2023 at the General Department of the Phnom Penh-Cambodia Chamber of Commerce under the chairmanship of Mr. Buon Sarak Mony, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce and Ms. Keo Sok Pisey, Deputy Governor. Phnom Penh.
Please be informed that Duke Kith Meng has been the President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Phnom Penh for 18 years and now he has been elected by the members to continue to lead the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Phnom Penh for a new term. 3 more years. Notice! Phnom Penh Capital Administration No Fireworks or Explosives of All Kinds During Chinese and Vietnamese New Year
In order to maintain security, safety, order and public order during the festival, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration has introduced the following departments, units, Khans, Sangkats, Associations, Private Companies, NGOs and the public in Phnom Penh:
* First, it is strictly forbidden to set off fireworks, fireworks or make any kind of explosion during this festival, not to gamble of any kind, to march any other religion or tradition without permission.
* Second: In all places of entertainment, departments, units, factories, enterprises, homes must maintain security, safety, public order, dignity and be careful to light candles, incense, paper, electric stoves that can cause fires eventually. In particular, the burning of paper must use metal containers or earthen pots to burn, it is strictly forbidden to burn on the sidewalk or chest of public roads.
* 3: From now on, the competent authorities at all levels must take the strictest measures to prevent the import of fireworks of all kinds through the entrance of Phnom Penh and to confiscate these items that are on sale. Everywhere in Phnom Penh.
* Fourth, the Department of Cult and Religion of Phnom Penh must invite Chinese and Vietnamese associations to disseminate the above content widely.
Fifth, the 14 Khan administrations, departments and units around the Phnom Penh Capital Administration must disseminate instructions to civil servants, subordinate forces and local people to follow this instruction effectively.
* Sixth: The Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commission, the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie Command and the Special Regional Military Command must issue strict orders to their forces to implement them effectively.
* Seventh: Anyone who violates this instruction or commits a crime that causes social unrest, loss of order, security, safety and public order shall be punished in accordance with the law in force. Spokesman for the General Commission: 165 more vehicles were inspected and fined on January 11, 2023
