Siem Reap Provincial Council Holds the 44th Ordinary Meeting of the Third Mandate 2023
(Siem Reap): The Siem Reap Provincial Council held its 44th Ordinary Meeting, 3rd Mandate 2023. In this meeting, 5 agendas were discussed and approved.
This meeting was held on January 10, 2023, chaired by Mr. An Khun, Chairman of Siem Reap Provincial Council and Mr. Tea Seiha, Governor of Siem Reap Province, and attended by Mr. and Mrs. Provincial Councilors, Deputy Provincial Governors, Representatives Apsara and Mr. and Mrs. Municipal-District Authority, Department-Unit Leaders, Directors, Deputy Directors, Administration, Directors-Deputy Directors, Units around various provinces also participated. On January 10, 2023
The meeting has some agenda such as:
1: Review, discuss and approve the request for leave permit in the 442nd Ordinary Meeting: Review, discuss and approve the draft minutes of the 43rd Ordinary Meeting of Siem Reap Provincial Council 3: Review, discuss and approve the draft Annual Report 2022 on the performance of the Siem Reap Provincial Administration.
4. Examine, discuss and approve the action plan and budget of the Child Protection Project 2023-2025 of the Siem Reap Provincial Administration. It also focused on a number of issues such as disorderly parking on public roads, environmental sanitation, enforcement of traffic laws, road problems in the Apsara area are damaged and have not been repaired.
In this meeting, Mr. Tea Seiha explained and also allowed the Director of the relevant departments to explain to the meeting. After the explanation of the department, Mr. Tea Seiha also urged all relevant departments and units to pay high attention to address all issues raised in this meeting.
The Chairman of the Provincial Council said that by participating in the discussion, reflecting and reflecting the good opinions with professional ethics from the members of the Provincial Council, the Provincial Board of Governors, the heads of the departments, units and all stakeholders. The Ordinary Meeting of the Provincial Council shall be conducted in the order in which the results are planned.
At the same time, Mr. An Khun also expressed his deep gratitude to the Provincial Governor as well as all departments and units that have taken care to solve all these issues, because these are the problems of the people. Citizens who are always talking nonsense.
At the same time, the Chairman of the Provincial Council also commended the leaders of Siem Reap for their efforts to develop the province to be safe, orderly and prosperous, as well as to implement the work effectively, have internal unity and have a sense of responsibility to fulfill. Work in accordance with policies, laws and regulations related to decentralization and deconcentration reforms at the sub-national administration.
