Pursat Provincial Governor Intervenes to Solve Water Supply for Farmers in Svay Daun Keo Commune After Facing Water Shortage
(Pursat): On January 10, 2023, Mr. Khoy Rida, Governor of Pursat Province, led the Department of Specialization after receiving a request for emergency intervention related to water shortage and dry season rice cultivation of farmers in Chrob village, Svay Daun Keo commune, Bakan district. And the relevant authorities inspected directly to find measures to intervene to solve the problem of water supply for the farmers who are facing problems as they have exceeded the plan.
Mr. Hay Thura, Director of Pursat Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that the dry season rice cultivation work in Svay Daun Keo commune covers a total area of 2,520 hectares, of which 1,070 hectares are planned.
For Bakan district as a whole, the area covered is 24,126 hectares of the planned 7,200 hectares. The director of the department said that according to the figures and actual inspections, the area that the farmers have implemented is beyond the plan set by the competent authorities, and they may face water shortages in the future.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Khoy Rida asked the commune authorities to advise farmers not to continue to dry rice, while in the future may face water shortages and the authorities will find ways to solve the cultivation of rice beyond this plan. .
It is true that the farmers pumped water from the Stung Srok canal to the bottom to protect the rice fields, but we still have the third and fifth dams, which store more than 50 million cubic meters of water to supply water. Along rivers, main canals, secondary canals or Kep canals to prepare farmers to pump their respective fields.
