Experts optimistic about real estate recovery in 2023 after China reopens
(Phnom Penh): Real estate experts have expressed high optimism about the recovery of the real estate sector in 2023, after being affected for three consecutive years after the spread of Kovid 1 and the outbreak of war between Russia and Ukraine.
Experts are so optimistic about the recovery of the Cambodian economy and the reopening of China, allowing people and foreigners to travel in and out of the country without having to travel.
She said that 2022 was a difficult year for the real estate sector, and the sectors most affected were the office and retail markets, as they needed support from tenants, while in 2022 rents fell. Down a lot. In particular, the hotel sector has recovered slightly in 2022. The housing sector, on the other hand, does not seem to be affected much as it is supported by the local population, especially the middle class.
She explained that in 2023, the hotel and hospitality sector will continue to grow in a positive way, as this year we believe that Cambodia will attract more tourists, especially when China reopens. The land sector will also see positive growth, albeit with modest growth, as Cambodia develops infrastructure.
