Four groups of students completed the project planning "Tourism Destination Development in Banteay Srei District"
(Phnom Penh): Four groups of students from four different higher education institutions competed in the preparation of the "Model Tourism Destination Development Plan in Banteay Srei District" organized by the Ministry of Tourism, which also received an accurate evaluation from Inter-ministerial-institutional committee.
In fact, on January 10, 2023, the Ministry of Tourism organized a evaluation program to select the winners in the competition program, "Model Tourism Development Plan" under the chairmanship of Mr. Nep Samuth, Director General of Tourism Industry Management and Chairman of the Secretariat of the Management and Development Committee. Siem Reap-Angkor Tourism at the Ministry of Tourism.
"As a result, the committee selected three groups of winners, of which the first place went to a group of students from the National University of Battambang, the second place went to a group of students from St. Paul Institute and The third prize went to a group of students from the Royal University of Phnom Penh.
Mr. Nep Samuth said that the above competition program was participated in the scoring and evaluation by the committee composed of representatives from the Ministry of Tourism, National Institute of Tourism, Asia-Pacific Tourism Association of Cambodia (PATA) and Banteay Srei District Tourism Community Network.
Please be reminded that this program is designed to provide opportunities for tourism students to study and understand the potential of tourism, challenges and get practical experience on the management mechanism of the operation of each tourist destination in accordance with the campaign "Visit our district". In line with the slogan "Patriotism must know the land", especially in accordance with the recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia "Territorial tourism".
The competition program is conducted in 5 stages:
Phase 1: Announcement and dissemination of applications will start accepting applications from September 19, 2022.
Phase 2: Selection of potential and qualified students to participate in the oral interview at the Ministry of Tourism on October 5, 2022.
Phase 3: Refresher and Orientation Course for the four groups of students on the topic of "Community-Based Tourism" on November 16, 2022.
Phase 4: Student study tour in Banteay Srei district, Siem Reap province by a group of students on November 17-21, 2022.
The Director General of the Ministry of Tourism also expressed his expectation that the competition program "Model Tourism Destination Development Plan" will be a platform for education and public awareness to the public, especially students who embrace tourism skills in learning. By connecting the theory to practical application, especially gaining direct experience in the development and management of targeting and tourism communities effectively and sustainably.
(Phnom Penh): The Olympics is an international sporting event that is attended by athletes from all over the world and is usually held every four years. You may have noticed that the Olympic symbols are five contiguous rings.
