In January 1981, Samdech Heng Samrin, former President of the People's Republic of Cambodia, decided to send Hor Namhong to Moscow as Ambassador. When Kong Koam returned from working as an ambassador in Hanoi, he seized the house. At that time, Hor Namhong was transferred from Deputy Foreign Minister to Ambassador to Moscow, while Kong Koam was transferred from Ambassador to Hanoi to Deputy Foreign Minister.
Mr. Hor Namhong continued that until 2015, there was a certificate of ownership for Mr. Kong Koam. He recalled that in 1990, Kong Koam wrote a letter to the People's Revolutionary Committee in Chamkar Mon district asking for a place to stay, and he was only allowed to stay there before applying for ownership in 2015.
Kong Koam has always changed party membership from a former CPP member to an opposition party member. Recently, after resigning as the honorary president of the Khmer Will Party, with his son Kong Monika as president, he became a senior adviser to the Candlelight Party, while Kong Monika also resigned and became a member of the Candlelight Party.
Please be informed that in September 1980, Mr. Kong Koam went to Hanoi and on October 13, 1980, he presented his credentials. During the 12th session of the National Assembly, first term, February 9, 1987, Mr. Kong Koam was appointed Minister of Foreign Affairs by Decree No. 53, dated December 3, 1986.
During the 14th session of the National Assembly, first legislature, on February 8, 1988, Mr. Kong Koam was transferred from the Minister of Foreign Affairs to the Assistant Minister, Chairman of the Council of Ministers in charge of Social Affairs and Culture under Decree No. 64 Dated this 19th day of December, 1987. Assigned the task to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, then Chairman of the Council of Ministers, to be the Minister of Foreign Affairs.
During the 16th Session of the National Assembly, First Legislature, on February 11, 1989, Mr. Kong Koam was transferred from the Assistant Minister to the Chairman of the Council of Ministers in charge of Socio-Cultural Affairs to be the Minister of Supervision by Decree No. 42. Dated August 20, 1988.
Please be informed that during the groundbreaking ceremony for the expansion of the national road from Skun to Kampong Cham on Monday morning, January 9, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen warned to take action against Mr. Kong Koam, who used various forums to attack the Cambodian People's Party.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also warned to sue Kong Koam's house. Samdech confirmed that the house was a former property of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, which Kong Kom, who had previously returned as ambassador to Hanoi, seized. However, Samdech claims that Samdech still understands because Mr. Kong Koam used to be together.
More than 800 families of motorbike taxi drivers, tricycles and taxi drivers in Pursat City received humanitarian donations from the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Pursat Province.
(Pursat): More than 800 families of motorbike taxi drivers, tricycles and taxi drivers in 7 communes in Pursat city, including 11 women who have suffered from poverty, received humanitarian donations from the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Pursat province. Each received 25 kg of rice, 1 small box of noodles, 1 fishing rod and 20,000 Riels to facilitate and solve family life.
The ceremony was held on the evening of January 9, 2023 at Pursat Provincial Stadium, presided over by Mr. Keo Rattanak, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Director General of Electricite du Cambodge and Honorary Chairman of the Branch, and Mr. Khoy Rida, Governor and Chairman of the Board of Governors. Pursat Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross with the participation of the Deputy Provincial Governor, leaders of relevant departments, units and institutions.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Khoy Rida and Mr. Keo Rattanak informed that the families of motorbike taxi drivers, tricycles and taxi drivers, families of teachers and retirees were formed under the initiative of Mr. Mao Thunin, former Governor of Pursat Province. He is currently the Governor of Kampot Province.
This is the first time that more than 800 motorbike taxi drivers, tricycles and taxi drivers in Pursat City have met with the newly-appointed Governor of Pursat, Mr. Khoy Rida. Nearly 2 months. Despite the busy schedule, he took the time to find out about the well-being, concerns and challenges encountered together in a timely manner.
The two leaders said that the families of motodups, tricycles and taxi drivers often face many of these problems, requiring a high degree of caution when driving, respecting traffic laws, not using alcohol, drugs, understanding. Be neutral to each other while driving, think about personal safety and passengers.
