The Minister of Information allowed Mr. Chhay Sophal to pay a courtesy call and present the book "The Legacy of Techo Phisut Puth of Cambodia on the International Stage"
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, on the morning of January 10, 2023, received Mr. Chhay Sophal, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Information, to pay a courtesy call and present a book entitled "The Legacy of Cambodia's Proficiency on the International Stage". »100 copies for the Minister and the General Department under the Ministry of Information.
Historical Document on the ASEAN Summit 2022 and Activities of Samdech Techo More than 730-page Historical Document on the Activities of Cambodia to Host the 40th and 41st ASEAN Summits in 2022 (November 8-13, 2022) And the visit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and the delegation abroad before and after the ASEAN Summit.
Please be informed that more than 730 pages of historical documents on the activities that Cambodia will host the 40th and 41st ASEAN Summit in 2022 (8-13 November 2022) and the visit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia And delegations abroad before and after the ASEAN Summit have been officially released.
Mr. Chhay Sophal stated that, as Samdech Techo said in the closing conference of the summit, "the benefit that Cambodia has received is the prestige that is preserved as history for future generations." "We can spend a day or a year, but the legacy we get these days is not enough. This is a legacy for all generations to study."
Mr. Sophal also claimed that what is more proud is that because Cambodia is peaceful and capable enough, including the leadership skills of Samdech Techo, the Council of Southeast Asian Sports Federation officially handed over the "Sea Games flag" to Cambodia. Host the 32nd SEA GAME and the 12th ASEAN Para Games in 2023, which Cambodia has missed for more than 60 years.
Mr. Sophal recalled that it is not unusual for Cambodia to be able to successfully host this world event, with the coordination of the leaders of the superpowers in conflict and taking advantage of each other's political geography in Eastern Europe. East Asia and Asia-Pacific can come and sit in the same room, eat the same Khmer food and listen to the conversation carefully and cautiously.
Please note that this series has been printed in 10,000 copies, each copy costs $ 10.2 and will be distributed to overseas readers such as the United States, Canada, France, Germany, Belgium, Australia and New Zealand, as well as the library. National and universities across the country, including bookstores.
The release of this series also aims to celebrate the historic January 7 Victory Day and the wedding anniversary of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit 5 January.
One Commune and Three Villages in Kong Pisey District, Kampong Speu Province Declared All Mine Mines with the Support of the Malaysian Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia
(Kampong Speu): On January 10, 2023, Stok Commune and Ang Dauntey Village, Trapeang Thmor Village, Roleang Teuk Knong Village, Srong Commune, Kong Pisey District, Kampong Speu Province were declared as Amin Min Commune under the chairmanship of Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Deputy Chairman of the Mine Authority. With the support of the Malaysian Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia (MBCC).
On behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister and Chairman of the Mine Authority, the Senior Minister expressed his deep gratitude to Duke KM Tan, President of the Malaysian Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia and other companies for their generous donations, contribution to land security and relief. The lives of the people, as well as contribute to pushing Cambodia closer to achieving the goal of no mines by 2025.
The Senior Minister emphasized that demining work is considered as one of the most important and priority tasks of the Royal Government of Cambodia after the liberation on January 7 under the high leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, and this year 2022 is a year to participate. A lot of people from the private sector, philanthropists and people with Samdech Techo's national movement to solve the problem of mines in Cambodia by 2025.
He added that in order to achieve the vision of Samdech Techo Minesweeper 2025, Cambodia has three years left (2023-2025) to complete the work of clearing mines in the area of suspected mines of about 648 square kilometers. Mr. Pan Sosak was appointed by the Cambodian Red Cross as the Honorary President of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Kampong Cham Province, 5th Mandate.
