The drum dance, which originated in the village of A Lech in Kampong Leng district, is performed every year.
(Kampong Chhnang): Kong Skor Dance is a traditional dance that has existed since ancient times, which originated in the village of El Lech, Chronok Commune, Kampong Leng District, Kampong Chhnang Province, and is still preserved by the locals to this day. Preserve the legacy of living people from ancient times for future generations.
This was confirmed by Mr. Sok Thuok, Director of the Department of Culture and Fine Arts of Kampong Chhnang Province, who confirmed this while the dance was performed during the Autumn Festival, which took place in Po commune, Kampong Leng district recently.
Mr. Sok Thuok said that the drum was also taken into account by the Ministry as a cultural heritage, living heritage. This dance is also performed by the villagers of A Lech, Chronok commune every year on the 14th and 15th day of the month of Phalkun in the festival of climbing the mountain to pay homage to the ancestors who built the temple on the top of the mountain.
The director of the department praised the people for their hard work in preserving the rich cultural traditions of their ancestors. Our Khmer. On the other hand, the Department of Culture has tried to reform the dance in some performances to be in line with the original style.
In fact, during October 2022, before being put on the Autumn Festival, the teachers and officials of the Department of Culture recently went to train the performers, so the performance in the Autumn Festival has improved a bit. Also.
