Ministry of Social Affairs Holds a Workshop on "Strengthening International Adoption Practices"
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Nim Thoth, Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and Deputy Director of the Central Adoption Authority of Cambodia and Ms. Chan Sotheavy, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Justice, organized a workshop on International adoption ”for 2 days, January 10 and 11, 2023 at Himawari Hotel, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Nim Thoth said that today's workshop aims to present the adoption law to the relevant ministries / institutions and the roadmap to prepare for the reopening of the adoption, share information to the relevant agencies and authorities. Strengthen-expand cooperation with relevant institutions to jointly address challenges.
The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and the Central International Adoption Authority, with the International Adoption Administration as its staff, have collaborated with the CIFA CIAI AIBI and ARIETE project implementation and management team. Receive financial support from the Italian Inter-Adoption Central Authority in the process of providing both technical and financial support for training courses and workshops.
The Bright Future Project has already provided five training sessions:
1: Training course on relevant laws and regulations to implement international adoption work in Cambodia
2: Training course on counseling and care related to child development
3: Training course on the practical application of the form in accordance with international adoption procedures
4: Training on International Standards on Adoption, Unattended Children and Post-Adoption Services
5: Training course on the integration of policies, standards, guidelines for domestic and international adoption procedures for the target groups of the five provinces: Phnom Penh, Kandal, Siem Reap, Battambang and Sihanoukville.
