(Preah Sihanouk): Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration reported that as of January 10, 2022, the people in Sihanoukville have gradually started to use clean water after the collapse of the second dam. Anco Water Supply Company caused damage to one pump and reduced water supply to the people in the province.
It should be reminded that the incident of the second dam collapse occurred on the night of January 7, 2023, causing damage to the pump at the second water treatment plant nearby and reducing the water supply. Half in Sihanoukville and parts of Prey Nob and Stung Hav districts.
Preah Sihanouk Provincial Governor, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun also led a team of experts to inspect and intervene to solve the problem immediately overnight to speed up the solution to the people due to the decrease in water supply.
As of January 10, Mr. Long Dimanche, Deputy Governor of Sihanoukville Province, said that the team has already repaired the second dam of Anko Water Supply Company and repaired the engine that was damaged by the dam collapse while the engine Pumping water at the second water treatment plant is also pumping water to the third water treatment plant gradually.
The Deputy Governor said that the operation of the water pump from the second water treatment plant to the third water treatment plant will increase the water treatment plant capacity of the third water treatment plant to about 16,000 cubic meters per day. Continue to supply clean water to the people almost enough to return to normal.
Meanwhile, officials from the Sihanoukville Water Supply Authority also inspected the water pipes in Sihanoukville and reported on the smooth water supply.
According to the Sihanoukville Water Supply Authority, Anco Water Supply Company is a water supplier in Sihanoukville and partly in Prey Nup and Stung Hav districts in the amount of 74,000 to 80,000 cubic meters. This water production has 3 water treatment stations in Kbal Chhay area, Sihanoukville.
