For the winner of the election of the president of the Cambodian Intellectual Property Association of the third mandate, Mr. Kang Daravuth had 142 votes in favor. At the same time, the General Assembly elected seven councilors, including: Ms. Keo Lang Cheng, Mr. Satya Dado, Ms. Pech Seila, Ms. Nong Ratana, Ms. Tep Sokun Vannary, Ms. Chan Serey Ratha and Ms. Song Sopheak.
On that occasion, Ms. Seng Vuoch Hun said that today's meeting is the first meeting and the last meeting in the second mandate of the association under her leadership since August 2019. In principle, the association has to hold an ordinary meeting every year, but due to the outbreak of Kovid 19, the association has failed to hold a meeting in the past two years.
In addition, IPAC has signed a Memorandum of Understanding with the Anti-Counterfeiting Committee of the Ministry of Interior, the Bar Association of the Kingdom of Cambodia and signed a cooperation agreement with the Siem Reap Provincial Administration. The association is also preparing to sign a memorandum of understanding with other ministries and institutions, but I leave this task to the president of the association for the next mandate to continue this work.
