Mr. Hun Many shared his experience of learning basic work from Udong district, Kampong Speu province
(Kampong Speu): Mr. Hun Many, Member of Parliament for Kampong Speu Constituency, this morning, January 9, 2023, presided over a meeting to celebrate the 44th anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day at Udong District Hall, Kampong Speu Province.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Ly Son, Advisor to Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, Dr. Ouk Kosa, Advisor to Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu Province, Ladies and Gentlemen, District Assistance Team and Members 699 people.
On this occasion, Mr. HUN Many stated that Udong Mechey City (Udong District, Kampong Speu Province) is a place where he and his team have been training for more than 10 years. One point in particular, among many other modalities, is the coherence of work between different age groups and leaders.
He said that despite the different ages, thoroughness, gentleness, mutual respect in communication, internships remain, which leads us to achieve effective and efficient work results. He added that so far the team has learned and gained a lot of leadership experience from the basic work.
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, on the afternoon of January 9, 2023, led the civil servants, the Armed Forces and the people to vaccinate Kovid-19 dose, 3rd, 4th, 5th and 6th dose at Kampong Cham Provincial Hall. .
On that occasion, Mr. Un Chanda expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, for providing Kovid-19 doses, 3rd, 4th, 5th and 6th doses to the Armed Forces and People in Kampong Cham province.
At the same time, the Kampong Cham Provincial Administration also informed the people living in Kampong Cham that in order to increase the immunity in the community to better prevent the spread of Kovid-19 and ensure the protection of the lives of the people from Kovid-19 Genocide Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has authorized the Ministry of Health to continue vaccinating Kovid-19 in the third, fourth, fifth and sixth doses to local people.
(Kandal): Mr. Kong Vibol, Minister Delegate of the Prime Minister, Director General of the General Department of Taxation and First Deputy Chairman of the Working Group of the Cambodian People's Party, visited Lvea Em District, Kandal Province this morning, January 9, 2023. During the commemoration ceremony for the 44th anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day, which was held in Lvea Em district.
He said that in the worst of circumstances, the patriotic forces of the Cambodian People's Party, which survived the Pol Pot massacre, stood up against the most brutal regime. On the road to overthrowing the Pol Pot regime, there are some major historical events that have the deepest meaning to the national rescue process, including:
On June 20, 1977, Samdech Techo and his comrades fled to Vietnam to seek support for the national liberation struggle.
2: On May 12, 1978, the Armed Forces of the National Rescue of Cambodia was established, led by Samdech Techo
3 - On May 25, 1978, the army and the people throughout the Eastern Zone rose up against the Pol Pot regime under the leadership of Samdech Heng Samrin and Samdech Chea Sim, and resistance movements in some areas began to move.
4: Starting from the above movement, provided the opportunity to establish the United Front for National Salvation of Cambodia on December 2, 1978, which is the only political organization representing the will of the people.
5. The Kampuchean United Front for National Salvation, which has the support of the people everywhere and has received large, timely and effective support from the Vietnamese Volunteer Army, overthrew the genocidal regime on January 7, 1979.
Mr. Kong Vibol continued, "January 7 Victory ended the dark era and opened a new era of Cambodia, bringing independence, freedom, democracy and social progress, as well as giving back what the Cambodian people have lost, especially the right to life." . This is a historical fact that no man or force can forget, distort and destroy. "Only those who love the genocidal regime will oppose the January 7 victory."
Cambodia has recently achieved new achievements in the development of peace, political stability and security, which are the foundation for the development and harmonious living of the people. The slogan "Thank you, peace, thank you, politics, win, win" resounded throughout the country and became the spirit of a strong and vibrant society in the process of building and defending the motherland.
Mr. Kong Vibol also stated that with only 7 months left, the 7th National Assembly election will come on July 23, 2023, which is a historic event with great significance for destiny. He called on all members to continue voting for the Cambodian People's Party to continue peace and development.
At the same time, Ang Mithing solemnly announced his support for Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the candidate for Prime Minister for the seventh term and support for Hun Manet as the next candidate.
Spokesman for the General Commission: Another 496 vehicles were inspected and fined on January 9, 2023
According to the spokesperson, for January 9, 2023, the traffic police nationwide inspected and fined a total of 2,534 vehicles, including 2,264 motorcycles and 270 vehicles.
Noted offenses for motorcycles include: drunken helmets, offenses, signs and license plates. In particular, the car includes: speed belts, no driver's license, overcrowding and violation of the sign.
It should be noted that for January 9, 2023, traffic accidents throughout Cambodia also occurred 6 times, in which 4 people were killed and 9 people were injured (4 people were seriously injured). In nine days, there were 75 traffic accidents, resulting in 43 deaths, 84 injuries (59 serious injuries).
A spokesman for the Philippine president said Galvest, a former joint chief of staff of the Philippine military, had agreed to the appointment, which came after Marcos accepted the resignation of Jose Faustino. Festino was appointed head of the Philippine defense in June 2022 as Marcos prepares to be sworn in as the new leader, succeeding former President Rodrigo Duterte.
Prior to his appointment, Galvesto served as an adviser to Marcos in charge of peace, reconciliation and national unity. Under Duterte's former administration, Galvez also served as a leader in the fight against Kovid 19 and in charge of vaccine purchases. In addition, Galvesto served as Joint Chiefs of Staff for six months in 2018.
