By Dr. Chea Monirith, President of the Cambodia-China Progress Researchers Association, Anti-Drug Committee, Ministry of National Defense Holds a Meeting to Summarize 2022 Work Results and 2023 Targets
(Phnom Penh): The Anti-Drug Committee of the Ministry of National Defense on the morning of January 9, 2023, held a meeting to review the results of the fight against drugs in 2022 and the work direction for 2023.
The meeting was held at the Ministry of National Defense under the chairmanship of General Chai Saing Yon, Chairman of the Anti-Drug Committee of the Ministry of National Defense, with the participation of the two Vice-Chairmen and some relevant members.
According to General Chhum Socheat, Deputy Chairman of the Anti-Drug Committee of the Ministry of National Defense, according to the preliminary report in 2022, the General Secretariat and units under the Ministry of National Defense have made efforts to carry out their work responsibly. High to contribute to education, dissemination, treatment, rehabilitation, integration and maintenance of security, public order, social development.
According to the preliminary report, in 2022, the Ministry of National Defense, the General Command and its subordinates conducted 5,770 outreach activities on drug issues, with a total of 349,304 participants (10,450 women). ).
According to the report, in 2022, the National Gendarmerie cracked down on 619 drug offenses and arrested 1,534 suspects (28 foreigners), including 161 women. Take some materials and exhibits.
According to General Chhum Socheat, in 2022, all relevant units under the Ministry of National Defense have worked diligently and responsibly to achieve better results. In the new year 2023, the Anti-Drug Committee of the Ministry of National Defense will continue to pay more attention to implementing the Royal Government's plan to fight against illegal drugs.
Lawyer's Office Releases Clarification on False Allegations against PHVC 28A, a Licensed Company
(Phnom Penh): Lawyers Ok Odom and Su Seiha, lawyers for the Lawyer's Office, issued a statement on the false allegations against PHVC 2888 EK and claiming that the company's business is Established legally in order to contribute to economic growth, promote tourism, create jobs.
In a statement issued by the Office of Lawyers received by Fresh News on December 9, 2023, the public and journalists were asked to stop all activities of disseminating false information that violated their client companies and Only trust real information with clear local sources to avoid confusion and social unrest.
