Japan helps train Cambodian spa-massage experts to prepare for Japanese tourists
(Siem Reap): The Royal Government of Japan, through the ASEAN-Japan Center, has continued to cooperate with the Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia to provide training courses for spa and massage health professionals in Siem Reap to prepare for Japanese tourists to help promote Cambodian tourism.
It should be informed that the ASEAN-Japan Center has cooperated in training spa and wellness skills in Phnom Penh for one session and ended in December 2022 with 25 participants. The ASEAN-Japan Center continued the second training course in Siem Reap from January 9-20, 2023, with 25 participants.
The opening ceremony of the second training course was presided over by Mr. Pak Sokhom, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, on the morning of January 9, 2023 at The Century Au Residence Hotel, Siem Reap, online (Zoom).
Mr. Pak Sokhom said that this training is very important to enhance and strengthen the capacity of Cambodian spa professionals to provide services and skills in spa services better. This spa skills training is in line with the ASEAN Spa Expert Competency Standards, which Cambodia is supported by member countries in developing the ASEAN Standard Curriculum for this Spa skill.
The Secretary of State recommended to all participants to pay attention to the full course to gain new knowledge and skills from trainers with specific skills to apply in their respective business and work. .
Pursat Provincial Administration Notifies 19 Kovid Vaccination to Frontline Health Officers, Local Authorities and General Population
(Pursat): Pursat Provincial Administration has issued a notification on the 4th dose of Kovid 19 vaccine to children aged 3 to under 5 years and the 19th dose of Kovid 19 vaccine to children aged 5 to 12 years and the 6th dose. To front health officers, local authorities and the general population in Pursat province. This is according to the announcement that Fresh News received on January 9, 2022.
